('anki-card-1758690495133-39', 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'It works closely with insulin to regulate the release of energy from glucose: *', 'chromium', '', '["chromium","zinc","iodine","selenium"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-29T15:16:59.622Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T15:16:59.622Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T15:16:59.852Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758690594998-45', 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'The body’s magnesium is found mostly in the: *', 'bones', 'An adult human body contains roughly 25 grams of magnesium, and the vast majority (about 50% to 60%) is stored directly within the bones. The skeleton acts as a massive reservoir for magnesium, with part of it bound to the bone crystal surface where it can be readily drawn out into the blood if dietary intake drops.

Most of the remaining magnesium is found within soft tissues, split between the skeletal muscles (around 20% to 30%) and other metabolic organs.

• Nerves: While magnesium is absolutely critical for nerve impulse transmission and blocking neuromuscular excitability, nervous tissue holds only a very small percentage of the body''s total supply.
• Muscles: Skeletal muscle is the second-largest pool of magnesium in the body, but it is still vastly outpaced by the volume stored in bone tissue.
• Extracellular fluids: Less than 1% of the body''s total magnesium circulates within the extracellular fluid and blood serum. Because blood levels are tightly regulated at the expense of tissue stores, blood tests often fail to reflect a true total-body magnesium deficiency.', '["extracellular fluids","bones","nerves","muscles"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 4, 'An average adult body contains roughly 25 grams of magnesium. The overwhelming majority—about 50% to 60%—is structurally stored within the bones, bound to the mineral matrix. Muscles hold the second-highest concentration of magnesium (around 20% to 30%).', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-11T14:46:49.401Z","interval":13,"easeFactor":2.1,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:46:49.401Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:46:49.600Z"'::jsonb),
