('anki-card-1758690228047-24', 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'Examples of derived lipids except: *', 'gangliosides', 'Gangliosides are categorized as compound (or complex) lipids rather than derived lipids. Specifically, they are complex glycosphingolipids composed of a fatty acid, a sphingosine backbone, and a complex oligosaccharide chain containing one or more residues of sialic acid.

Derived lipids are substances produced via the chemical hydrolysis of simple or compound lipids. They include free fatty acids, structural alcohols, hydrocarbons, fat-soluble vitamins, and sterols.

• Vitamin D: A fat-soluble vitamin. Because it is a secosteroid derivative generated from lipid precursors, it is classified under the derived lipids family.
• Cholesterol: The principal animal sterol. It lacks ester bonds but exhibits lipid-like properties and is a primary hydrolytic product/derivative of complex steroid pathways, placing it firmly in the derived lipid category.
• Ergosterol: A plant and fungal sterol (the biological precursor to vitamin D2). Like cholesterol, it is a non-saponifiable steroid molecule classified structurally as a derived lipid.', '["vitamin D","ergosterol","gangliosides","cholesterol"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 5, 'Gangliosides are structurally classified as compound lipids—specifically, they are a subtype of glycolipids.', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-25T14:47:22.370Z","interval":27,"easeFactor":2.1,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:47:22.370Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:47:22.568Z"'::jsonb),
