('anki-card-1758690063705-16', 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'The body stores energy for future use in: *', 'triglycerides', 'Adipose tissue plays a fundamental role in maintaining long-term energy balance by storing concentrated energy in the form of triglycerides (fats).

Triglycerides provide a highly concentrated fuel source yielding 9 kcal/g, making them the most efficient and virtually unlimited way for the body to store excess calories for future energy needs.

• Proteins: While amino acids from proteins can be broken down for energy during late prolonged starvation, the primary physiological role of proteins is structural and functional (building tissues and machinery); they are not stored for the dedicated purpose of serving as an energy reserve.
• Acetyl CoA & Ketone bodies: These are intermediate metabolic molecules and transient byproducts of fuel breakdown. They are utilized immediately by tissues or converted further to produce ATP, but they cannot be stored by the body for future use.', '["acetyl CoA","proteins","triglycerides","ketone bodies"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 4, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-11T14:46:04.387Z","interval":13,"easeFactor":2.1,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:46:04.387Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:46:04.594Z"'::jsonb),
