('anki-card-1758691277664-79', 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'Factors that lower blood glucose level except: *', 'reduced physical activity', '', '["reduced physical activity","starvation","liver damage","kidney malfunction"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-29T10:26:47.004Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T10:26:47.004Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T10:26:47.004Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758691244118-77', 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'The precursor of arginine which becomes indispensable in conditions of trauma is: *', 'glutamate', 'In the human body, glutamate (derived from glutamine in the intestinal-renal axis) serves as the primary metabolic precursor for the synthesis of arginine. Glutamate is converted into ornithine, which then enters the urea cycle to be synthesized into citrulline, argininosuccinate, and finally, arginine.

While healthy adults can normally synthesize enough arginine internally to meet daily maintenance demands, severe physical trauma, major burns, or sepsis completely exhausts the body''s natural manufacturing capacity. Under these high-stress hypermetabolic states, the rate of internal arginine production from its glutamate pathway falls short of the massive demands needed for wound healing (proline synthesis), cellular immune function (T-cell support), and vascular tone (nitric oxide generation). Therefore, arginine transforms into a conditionally indispensable (essential) amino acid that must be supplied directly through the clinical diet or specialized formula.

• Phenylalanine: An indispensable amino acid that acts as the primary precursor for tyrosine, not arginine.
• Methionine: An indispensable sulfur-containing amino acid that serves as the precursor for cysteine, not arginine.
• Serine: A dispensable amino acid synthesized from 3-phosphoglycerate (a glycolytic intermediate) that functions primarily in glycine and cysteine pathways.', '["glutamate","serine","phenylalanine","methionine"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, 'Arginine is synthesized endogenously from glutamate (and glutamine) through the intestinal-renal axis via intermediate molecules like ornithine and citrulline. Under normal physiological conditions, adults can produce sufficient amounts of arginine. However, during periods of physical trauma, severe burns, major surgery, or sepsis, the body''s metabolic demand for arginine dramatically outpaces its rate of synthesis. As a result, arginine becomes a conditionally indispensable (essential) amino acid that must be supplied through the diet or specialized nutrition, heavily relying on its structural precursor, glutamate.', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-29T12:48:22.898Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-28T12:48:22.898Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-28T12:48:23.088Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758690333059-30', 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'The combination of processes by which a living organism receives and utilizes the materials needed to maintain its functions and for the growth and renewal of its components. *', 'nutrition', '', '["metabolism","absorption","nutrition","digestion"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-29T12:08:54.027Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T12:08:54.027Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T12:08:54.233Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758691307848-81', 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'An enzyme that is common in both glycolysis and gluconeogenesis. *', 'aldolase', 'Aldolase catalyzes a reversible reaction in glycolysis and gluconeogenesis, breaking down (or assembling) fructose-1,6-bisphosphate into dihydroxyacetone phosphate (DHAP) and glyceraldehyde 3-phosphate (G3P).

• Fructose biphosphatase (fructose-1,6-bisphosphatase), phosphofructokinase-1 (PFK-1), and glucokinase are unidirectional, regulatory enzymes unique to either gluconeogenesis or glycolysis, respectively, to prevent a futile cycle.', '["aldolase","glucokinase","phosphofructokinase-1","fructose biphosphatase"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 3, 'Glycolysis (the breakdown of glucose) and gluconeogenesis (the synthesis of glucose) share many of the same enzymes. These are the reversible enzymes that can catalyze a reaction in both directions depending on cellular concentration gradients. Aldolase is a highly reversible enzyme. In glycolysis, it splits Fructose-1,6-bisphosphate into two 3-carbon pieces (DHAP and GAP). In gluconeogenesis, it acts in reverse, combining those same two 3-carbon pieces back together to form Fructose-1,6-bisphosphate.', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-04T08:09:25.517Z","interval":6,"easeFactor":2.1,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:09:25.517Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:09:25.840Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758691076310-67', 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'Most vitamins: *', 'are precursors to coenzymes.', '', '["are covalently linked to proteins without modification.","are precursors to coenzymes.","consist of amino acids, fatty acids or sugars.","are synthesized by humans."]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-29T14:59:06.603Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T14:59:06.603Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T14:59:06.909Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758691057742-66', 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'A deficiency of this B vitamin shows similar signs and symptoms like vitamin B12: *', 'folate', '', '["pantothenic acid","thiamin","folate","niacin"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-29T14:05:26.050Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T14:05:26.050Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T14:05:26.445Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758689902277-8', 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'The science that investigates how the different nutrients influence the activities of genes: *', 'nutrigenomics', '', '["nutrigenetics","nutrigenomics","epigenetics","genomics"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-01T12:34:31.909Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T12:34:31.909Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T12:34:31.909Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758690245279-25', 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'Vitamins that help in cell division: *', 'folate & B12', 'Both folate (vitamin B9) and vitamin B12 (cobalamin) are essential coenzymes required for the synthesis of nucleic acids (DNA and RNA).

Before a cell can divide, it must perfectly replicate its entire DNA strands. Folate is a crucial building block for this replication process. Vitamin B12 acts as the mandatory key that unlocks folate, converting it into its active form inside the body.

If either vitamin is missing, cell division stalls. This is most visibly seen in fast-dividing tissues like bone marrow, where a lack of cell division leads to megaloblastic anemia (large, immature, undivided red blood cells).', '["folate & biotin","thiamin & riboflavin","niacin & B12","folate & B12"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-29T11:22:06.218Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-28T11:22:06.218Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-28T11:22:06.394Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758690276245-27', 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'The most abundant protein in the human blood plasma: *', 'albumin', '', '["hemoglobin","protacyclin","albumin","insulin"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-29T15:06:41.325Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T15:06:41.325Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T15:06:41.557Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758689917813-9', 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'When using a Biuret’s test, which macromolecule/s will produce a positive reaction? *', 'protein', '', '["fat","all of the above","carbohydrate","protein"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-29T11:44:52.690Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T11:44:52.690Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T11:44:52.918Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758690047575-15', 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'The largest, least dense lipoprotein that carries the greatest number of triglycerides. *', 'chylomicron', '', '["VLDL","chylomicron","HDL","LDL"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-29T10:51:16.182Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T10:51:16.182Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T10:51:16.423Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758690613431-46', 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'It is a part of CoA: *', 'pantothenic acid', '', '["pantothenic acid","biotin","thiamin","folate"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-29T11:18:05.869Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T11:18:05.869Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T11:18:05.869Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758689696588-0', 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'In collagen synthesis, ____ acts as a reducing agent to convert oxidized iron atom back to its reduced state. *', 'ascorbic acid', 'During collagen synthesis, two critical enzymes—prolyl hydroxylase and lysyl hydroxylase—are responsible for adding hydroxyl (-OH) groups to proline and lysine amino acids. This structural modification allows collagen strands to cross-link properly, forming a stable triple-helix network.

These hydroxylase enzymes require iron in its active, reduced ferrous state (Fe²⁺) to operate. During the chemical reaction, the iron atom naturally becomes oxidized into its inactive ferric state (Fe³⁺). Ascorbic acid (Vitamin C) acts as the essential electron donor or reducing agent, transferring electrons to convert the inactive ferric iron back into its active ferrous state. Without enough vitamin C, the iron stays oxidized, collagen remains under-hydroxylated, and connective tissues weaken (resulting in scurvy).', '["ascorbic acid","pantothenic acid","pyridoxine","folic acid"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-29T12:46:38.676Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-28T12:46:38.676Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-28T12:46:38.871Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758691491756-89', 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'The following have an antioxidant function except for: *', 'Zn', 'Vitamin C and carotenoids are classic direct non-enzymatic antioxidants because they physically neutralize free radicals by donating electrons. Selenium (Se) is a direct component of the essential antioxidant enzyme glutathione peroxidase, which actively breaks down toxic peroxides.

In contrast, Zinc itself does not directly capture free radicals. Instead, it plays an indirect role by acting as a structural co-factor for the enzyme copper-zinc superoxide dismutase (CuZnSOD) and stabilizing cell membranes against lipid peroxidation. Because it serves as a mineral co-factor rather than acting as a direct antioxidant chemical or molecule on its own, it stands out as the standard textbook exception in this specific group.', '["Se","Zn","vitamin C","carotenoids"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 4, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-11T08:08:24.208Z","interval":13,"easeFactor":2.1,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:08:24.208Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:08:24.524Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758691141221-71', 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'When digesting a complex carbohydrate, water is added and simple sugars are obtained through what process? *', 'hydrolysis', '', '["condensation","hydrolysis","photosynthesis","dehydration"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-29T11:09:04.585Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T11:09:04.585Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T11:09:04.857Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758691261768-78', 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'Hydrochloric acid in the stomach: *', 'denatures proteins and activates pepsin', '', '["condenses proteins and facilitates digestion","emulsifies proteins and releases peptidase","hydrolyzes proteins and denatures pepsin","denatures proteins and activates pepsin"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-01T11:48:17.035Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T11:48:17.035Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T11:48:17.035Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758691109393-69', 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'Normal blood osmolality: *', '300 mOsm', '', '["400 mOsm","300 mOsm","500 mOsm","200 mOsm"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-01T11:38:32.970Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T11:38:32.970Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T11:38:32.970Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758691394362-86', 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'B vitamins involved in hematopoiesis except:', 'B3', '', '["B12","B6","B3","folate"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-01T10:35:08.588Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T10:35:08.588Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T10:35:08.588Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758691644649-98', 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'It is a branched-chain amino acid: *', 'isoleucin', 'Isoleucine is one of the three classic branched-chain amino acids (BCAAs), alongside leucine and valine. These amino acids are chemically distinguished by an aliphatic, non-linear side chain featuring a central branch point.

Unlike most other amino acids that are metabolized primarily in the liver, BCAAs are unique because they bypass initial liver breakdown and are taken up directly by skeletal muscle tissue. There, they serve as a critical substrate for energy production and play a major role in stimulating muscle protein synthesis during periods of recovery or metabolic stress.

• Alanine: A dispensable (non-essential) amino acid with a simple, straight-chain methyl side group. It is heavily involved in the glucose-alanine cycle to transport nitrogen from muscles to the liver.
• Lysine: An indispensable (essential) amino acid with a straight, basic hydrocarbon side chain ending in an amino group, not a branched-chain configuration.
• Glutamine: A conditionally indispensable amino acid with a straight-chain amide side group. It is the most abundant free amino acid in the human body, acting as a premier fuel source for rapidly dividing immune cells and enterocytes in the gut.', '["glutamine","alanine","lysine","isoleucin"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, 'There are only three BCAAs among the proteinogenic amino acids: leucine, isoleucine, and valine. All three are essential amino acids, meaning the body cannot synthesize them, and they must be obtained through the diet.', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-29T14:18:30.133Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-28T14:18:30.133Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-28T14:18:30.315Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758690681661-49', 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'Principal organs of metabolism are: *', 'digestive organs, liver, pancreas, circulatory system, and kidneys', '', '["stomach, heart, lungs, liver, and brain","digestive organs, liver, pancreas, circulatory system, and kidneys","brain, digestive system, heart, stomach, and lungs","lungs, blood stream, pancreas, liver, and heart"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-29T11:43:21.190Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T11:43:21.190Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-23T17:47:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T11:43:21.440Z"'::jsonb),
