('anki-card-1758080023024-81', 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'The most important nutritional consideration in treating patients with kidney stones is to:*', 'Increase fluid intake', '', '["Limit calcium intake","Restrict all end products of protein metabolism","Restrict all food sources of calcium, oxalic acid, and prunes","Increase fluid intake"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758080049657-82', 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'A patient with Type 1 diabetes presents to the emergency room with dehydration and Kussmaul respirations. Urinalysis reveals ketonuria; lab results show blood glucose of 525 and pCO2 of 59.This patient is experiencing*', 'Metabolic acidocis', '', '["Respiratory acidosis","Respiratory alkalosis","Metabolic acidocis","Metabolic alkalosis"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758080065872-83', 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'A chronic COPD patient with carbon dioxide retention would have which one of the following acid-base imbalances?*', 'Respiratory acidosis', '', '["Respiratory acidosis","Respiratory alkalosis","Metabolic acidosis","Metabolic alkalosis"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758080080071-84', 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'When pCO2 is 28, bicarbonate is 32, and pH is > 7.45, how do the kidneys compensate to assure acid-base balance?*', 'Excrete bicarbonate', '', '["Conserve bicarbonate","Conserve sodium ions","Excrete bicarbonate","Conserve carbon dioxide"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758080108453-85', 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'Which of the following nutrition measures is most important for the person with acute respiratory failure*', 'A diet prescription that is low in carbohydrate and high in fat than a typical diet following acute stress', '', '["High volumes of fluids pr electrolytes to clean the lungs of fluids","A diet prescription that is low in carbohydrate and high in fat than a typical diet following acute stress","Attention to ensuring an adequate but not excessive energy intake","A high kilocalorie, high protein diet to support wearing from mechanical ventilation"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758080126420-86', 'anki-deck-1783610445035-1790433132436-zkpto', 'Factors that frequently contribute in wasting the patients with COPD include*', 'Anorexia, medications and respiratory infections', '', '["Anorexia, medications and respiratory infections","Dehydration, fat malabsorption and lactose intolerance","Essential fatty acids deficiencies and potassium imbalances","Vitamin K deficiencies, dysphagia and low fiber,low potassium diets"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
