('anki-card-1758604762657-95', 'anki-deck-1783610421391-1790433139851-sw8ch', 'What is the best strategy in feeding the child with cerebral palsy with exaggerated bite reflex?*', 'Once your child can grasp a spoon and guide it to his/her mouth, start introducing finger foods, such as crackers, grapes, and bread.', '', '["Once your child can grasp a spoon and guide it to his/her mouth, start introducing finger foods, such as crackers, grapes, and bread.","Smelling, touching, and learning about food helps children get a better sense of eating, and ultimately helps the feeding process.","The spoon should never be larger than the tongue of the child, girl or young person.","When the child is biting down, apply light pressure on the bottom of their chin and wait to feel their jaw drop and then remove the spoon or cup from their mouth."]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:28.720Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
