('anki-card-1756171830367-49', 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'In foodservice facilities and layout, supporting services include the following, except:', 'None of the above', 'It includes all plus an area for steam hose use to wash and sanitize carts, etc.', '["None of the above","Office","Janitor''s closet/storage","Trash and waste storage"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T15:02:15.456Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T15:02:15.456Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T15:02:15.456Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756171777003-48', 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'The main goal of staff orientation program:', 'communicate information and create response to the company and the job', 'Staff orientation is done to help recently hired staff in adjusting to their new employer. It gives staff members the fundamental organizational knowledge and serves as a venue for the employees to solicit responses about their new team, division, and job within the firm.', '["communicate information and create response to the company and the job","establish a system of discipline and rewards for the staff","establish training plan and method for evaluation progress","assess the reaction of other workers to the new worker"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-01T20:00:00.000Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T16:31:48.352Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756171695272-47', 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'A function of management that involves developing in broad outline the activities required to accomplish the objectives of the organization and the most effective ways of doing so. It is a continuous process and requires that management be diligent in conducting periodic reviews of all plans to ensure that they are still appropriate as conditions change.', 'Planning', 'In management theory, planning is universally recognized as the foundational function that involves determining the organization''s goals and charting out a broad outline of activities and strategies to achieve them.

Because business and environmental conditions constantly shift, planning cannot be a one-time task. It requires an ongoing, continuous process where managers regularly review, adjust, and adapt their roadmaps to ensure the organization stays on track.

• Marketing: The function focused on identifying, anticipating, and satisfying customer needs through product design, pricing, promotion, and distribution.
• Finance: The function responsible for managing the organization''s monetary resources, budgeting, and capital allocations.
• Operations: The function that deals with the daily execution, transformation of inputs into outputs, and physical manufacturing or service delivery processes.', '["Marketing","Finance","Planning","Operations"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T15:01:27.109Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T15:01:27.109Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T15:01:27.319Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756171567728-46', 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'Decision-making guides that are written to ensure that all actions taken by organization members are consistent with the organization''s strategy and objectives.', 'Policies', 'In organizational management and foodservice planning, policies function as comprehensive, high-level decision-making guides. Rather than telling employees exactly what to do step-by-step, they establish a reliable boundaries framework. This ensures that every independent decision or action made by staff members stays completely aligned with the company’s broad strategy, vision, and core objectives.

• Rules: These are strict, specific, and inflexible directives that dictate exactly what must or must not be done in a given situation (e.g., "No smoking in the kitchen"). They leave zero room for individual decision-making or managerial discretion.
• Operating plans: These are short-term, detailed tactical blueprints that outline specific tasks, timelines, schedules, and budgets to execute operations over a precise period (such as weekly or monthly outputs).
• Standing plans: This is a broad, overarching category of plans designed to be used repeatedly for recurring organizational activities. Standing plans include policies, procedures, and rules collectively, making it too broad of a classification to serve as the definition for a targeted decision-making guide.', '["Rules","Standing plans","Policies","Operating plans"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T15:05:26.186Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T15:05:26.186Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T15:05:26.186Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756171503981-45', 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'German global online food delivery marketplace that allows customers to directly order meals online or via mobile.', 'Foodpanda', 'Foodpanda is an online food and grocery delivery platform brand owned by Delivery Hero, which is headquartered in Berlin, Germany and operates with 20 brands in about 50 countries across four continents. The Foodpanda brand, currently used in Asia, Bulgaria and Romania, was acquired by Delivery Hero in December 2016.

• Honestbee was an online grocery and food delivery service based in Singapore.
• Munchpunch is a food discovery and restaurant directory website based in the Philippines.
• AmazonFresh is a grocery delivery service owned by the American tech giant Amazon.', '["Foodpanda","Honestbee","Munchpunch","Foodpanda"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T15:04:30.510Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T15:04:30.510Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T15:04:30.510Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756171451617-44', 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'The main bases for space allocation:', 'Menu', 'Menu serves as the basis for physical factors like equipment, kitchen space, layout and sanitation.', '["Menu","Type of equipment material","Quantity of equipment","Manpower"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T15:04:21.514Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T15:04:21.514Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T15:04:21.514Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756171408600-43', 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'An unpaid form of promotion in which satisfied customers tell other people how much a product or service is favored.', 'Word-of-mouth', 'Word-of-mouth (WOM) marketing relies entirely on authentic human recommendations. It is completely unpaid because it happens naturally when satisfied customers organically share their positive experiences, reviews, or favorite products with friends, family, or colleagues.', '["Social media advertising","Personal selling","Radio commercials","Word-of-mouth"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T15:04:17.014Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T15:04:17.014Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T15:04:17.014Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756171319039-42', 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'A way of thinking that there is always a better way to eliminate any uneconomical use of resources:', 'Work simplification', 'Work Simplification is the systematic use of common sense in the quest for better and easier methods of accomplishing the work.', '["Work simplification","Motion economy","Productivity","Efficiency Performance"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T15:03:41.572Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T15:03:41.572Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T15:03:41.572Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756171263809-41', 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'Under PD 856, the minimum kitchen size for a 40 m² dining area is (m²):', '10', 'Rule: The kitchen area must be at least 1/4 (25%) of the total dining area, but it cannot fall below a baseline minimum of 9.30 m² (100 sq. ft.).

Calculated Kitchen Area = 40 m² x 0.25 = 10 m²', '["10","5","15","20"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T14:59:57.123Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:59:57.123Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:59:57.123Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756171213345-40', 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'The third step in a three-stage hand-washing dishes is:', 'Sanitizing', 'There are three parts to hand-washing dishes: wash, rinse, and sanitize. In order to accomplish all three, your facility must have a three-compartment dishwashing sink. The sink must be clean and sanitized before beginning the washing process.', '["Sanitizing","Rinsing","Drying","Air-drying"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T14:59:53.455Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:59:53.455Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:59:53.455Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756171114365-38', 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'According to the Labor Code of the Philippines, night shift differential means:', 'Employee compensation not less than 10% of the regular wage per hour of work between 10pm-6am', '', '["Employee compensation not less than 5% of the regular wage per hour of work between 11pm-5am","Employee compensation not less than 5% of the regular wage per hour of work between 10pm-6am","Employee compensation not less than 10% of the regular wage per hour of work between 11pm-5am","Employee compensation not less than 10% of the regular wage per hour of work between 10pm-6am"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T14:59:22.908Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:59:22.908Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:59:22.908Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756170963755-36', 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'A line type of organization is applicable to a dietary department primarily because it:', 'shows the relationship of each position in the over-all plan and function of the department', 'In dietary department, lines of authority should be clearly drawn.', '["shows the relationship of each position in the over-all plan and function of the department","provides information on the number of employees required to do each job","justifies request for additional employees for each task or work","all of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T14:59:16.022Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:59:16.022Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:59:16.022Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756170847012-35', 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'A detailed floor plan showing arrangement of equipment for accomplishing work according to logical sequence of operation.', 'layout', 'Layout – a detailed floor plan showing arrangement of equipment for accomplishing work according to logical sequence of operation. It refers to the process of arranging the physical facilities which includes a design drawn on paper to show structural components such as walls, windows, door, etc.', '["layout","floor plan","blueprint","work center"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T14:58:55.877Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:58:55.877Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:58:55.877Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756170798113-34', 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'An organized list of duties, skills, and responsibilities required in a specific position.', 'Job description', 'Job description is an organized list of duties, skills and responsibilities required in a specific position. This should be written for every position and should be reviewed and updated periodically.', '["Job description","Job analysis","Job specification","Job requirements"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T14:58:44.685Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:58:44.685Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:58:44.685Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756170753585-33', 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'A set of waste management practices which aims to safely and effectively handle the municipal solid waste stream with the least adverse impact on human health and the environment.', 'Integrated Solid Waste Management', 'Integrated Solid Waste Management is a set of waste management practices which aims to safely and effectively handle the municipal solid waste stream with the least adverse impact on human health and the environment. 

• Republic Act No. 9003 “Ecological Solid Waste Management Act of 2000”. 
• Zero Waste Management Strategy - aims to achieve zero waste of resources; to eliminate solid waste, hazardous waste, emissions, toxic wastes and others; to eliminate waste at source and at all points down the production and supply chains rather than management of the wastes created in the process.', '["Integrated Solid Waste Management","RA No. 9003","Reuse, Reduce, Recycle","Zero Waste Management Strategy"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T14:58:28.225Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:58:28.225Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:58:28.225Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756170660369-32', 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'The most practical type of storage in small stores is:', 'Reach-in chiller', 'Reach-in units are used to store food products at point-of-use or used in central storage units in small operations.', '["Reach-in chiller","Blast chiller","Walk-in chiller","Chest freezer"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-01T20:00:00.000Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T16:29:05.554Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756170621472-31', 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'Theory of management that contains the doctrine of interdependecy and wholism.', 'Systems approach', 'Systems approach has a set of interdependent parts that work together to achieve a common goal. Interdependency is the key concept in systems theory.', '["Systems approach","Classical","Contingency","Human relations"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-01T20:00:00.000Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T16:31:08.456Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756170564707-30', 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'This refers to the amount of product that should be on hand at any given time.', 'Par stock', 'Par Stock – amount of product that should be on hand between one delivery and the next. This represents the ideal or standard operating quantity of an item that must be physically physically present in stock at any given time to fulfill normal customer demand between delivery cycles. When stock levels drop below this baseline figure, it automatically triggers a reorder to bring the inventory back up to par.

• Minimum stock: This is the absolute safety threshold or "buffer" limit below which inventory should never fall to avoid severe stockouts or operational emergencies.
• Ending stock: The actual physical quantity of product remaining on hand at the exact conclusion of an accounting or inventory reporting period.
• Perpetual inventory: A continuous tracking method or accounting ledger system that automatically registers adjustments to stock balances in real time as items are bought or sold.', '["Par stock","Perpetual inventory","Minimum stock","Ending stock"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T14:54:40.960Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:54:40.960Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:54:40.960Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756170514010-29', 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'According to the Labor Code of the Philippines, service charge is to be distributed as follows:', '85% for all covered employees; 15% to management', 'Service charges and pooled tips – eighty-five percent (85%) equally shared by the employees, fifteen percent (15%) retained by the management.

Although recent:
Under Article 96 of the Labor Code of the Philippines (as amended by Republic Act No. 11360 and DOLE Department Order No. 242, Series of 2024), service charges collected by hotels, restaurants, and similar establishments are distributed as follows:
• 100% Full Distribution: All collected service charges must be distributed completely and equally among covered employees. Management can no longer retain a percentage.', '["85% for all covered employees; 15% to management","90% for all covered employees; 10% to management","Equal distribution among all employees including rank-and-file and management","10% for all rank-and-file employees; 90% to management"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T14:53:32.463Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:53:32.463Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:53:32.463Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756170251424-28', 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'Simulation type of training:', 'vestibule', 'Vestibule training is one of the on-the-job training where technical staff is trained on how to use tools and machinery by creating a simulated workplace. This training is also termed as ''near the job training'' in which a simulated work setup is created near the main production plant.', '["vestibule","on-the-job","mentoring","apprenticeship"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T14:53:27.155Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:53:27.155Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:53:27.155Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756170213857-27', 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'A collection of data about the market and other factors. It is conducted to determine if the project is worth pursuing.', 'Feasibility study', 'A feasibility study is acollection of data about the market and other factors. It is conducted to determine if the project is worth pursuing. It includes: The Prospectus, Research on the proposed site, Design trends, Market research, Community growth, Competition in the area, Financial goals, and Standard Operating Procedures.', '["Feasibility study","Market survey","Market acceptability","Consumer demand survey"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T14:53:22.818Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:53:22.818Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:53:22.818Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756170155445-26', 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'Breakdown of task into organized activity considering time and sequence of operation:', 'Work schedule', 'Work schedule – an outline of work to be performed, procedures to be used, and time schedule for a particular position. Workers may be scheduled successfully only after thorough analysis and study of the jobs to be done, the working conditions, and the probable efficiency of the employees.', '["Work schedule","Organizational chart","Daily Tally sheet","Evaluation sheet"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T14:53:17.371Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:53:17.371Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:53:17.371Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756170100698-25', 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'Japanese style of management in which workers are seen as the key to increased productivity:', 'Theory Z', 'William Ouchi’s Theory Z makes certain assumptions about workers. One assumption is that they seek to build cooperative and intimate working relationships with their coworkers. In other words, employees have a strong desire for affiliation. Another assumption is that workers expect reciprocity and support from the company. 

According to Theory Z, people want to maintain a work-life balance, and they value a working environment in which things like family, culture, and traditions are considered to be just as important as the work itself. Under Theory Z management, not only do workers have a sense of cohesion with their fellow workers, they also develop a sense of order, discipline, and a moral obligation to work hard. 

Finally, Theory Z assumes that given the right management support, workers can be trusted to do their jobs to their utmost ability and look after for their own and others’ well-being.', '["Theory Z","Theory X","Theory Y","Total Quality Management"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-01T20:00:00.000Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T16:26:16.259Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756169252803-24', 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'Another name for family style of service.', 'Compromise', 'Family or compromise style of service is a compromise between the Russian and English styles; some foods are served directly from the kitchen on individual dishes and some are served at the table. It is best used in small groups, not more than eight.', '["Compromise","Continental","English","Apartment"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-01T20:00:00.000Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T16:42:29.819Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756169221053-23', 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'System that identifies specific hazard and measures for their control to ensure the safety of food.', 'HACCP', 'HACCP stands for Hazard Analysis and Critical Control Points which is a systematic system that identifies specific hazards and measures for their control to ensure food safety. This focuses more on prevention rather than relying mainly on end-product testing.', '["HACCP","Codex","Food safety","GMP"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T14:52:54.953Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:52:54.953Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:52:54.953Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756169166923-22', 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'Income less cost of good sold is known as the:', 'Gross profit', 'Gross Profit = Sales/Income - Cost of Goods Sold (COGS)

To arrive at Net Profit/Loss, the operating expenses and other applicable expenses (such as interest and taxes) are then deducted from the gross profit: Sales/Income – COGS = Gross Profit 

Gross Profit – Operating and Other Expenses = Net Profit/Loss', '["Gross profit","Net profit/loss","Food cost","Prime cost"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T14:52:47.839Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:52:47.839Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:52:47.839Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756169123407-21', 'anki-deck-1783609175539-1790433140277-2y6kw', 'Which is not a factor choice of distribution system?', 'Consumer''s capacity to pay', 'In foodservice systems management, selecting the appropriate distribution and delivery system (the method of getting cooked food from the kitchen to the point of service) is an operational and architectural decision. It is dictated by structural, physical, and logistical factors within the establishment:

• Type of foodservice system: Whether an operation is Conventional, Commissary, Ready-Prepared, or Assembly/Serve directly dictates the assembly and distribution infrastructure required.
• Size and layout of the facility: A multi-story hospital or large campus requires decentralized distribution (e.g., using rethermalization carts or satellite pantries), whereas a compact single-room diner can use a simple centralized counter distribution system.
• Style of service: Self-service cafeterias, tray service, banquets, and vending machines each require distinct holding, temperature control, and physical transport distribution methods.

While the target consumer''s financial capacity heavily influences menu pricing, decor tiering, food service classifications, and ingredient sourcing, it does not mechanically alter or dictate the internal engineering or logistical choice of the physical distribution system inside the facility.', '["Type of foodservice system","Size and lay out of facility","Style of service","Consumer''s capacity to pay"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T14:52:15.043Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:52:15.043Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.104Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T14:52:15.043Z"'::jsonb),
