('anki-card-1788430529724-7', 'anki-deck-1788430296776-1790433145942-55yvl', 'A foodservice operation orders 40 kg of ground beef. The specification requires 80% lean meat, delivery at 5°C or below, and packaging free from tears or leakage. The supplier delivers 40 kg of meat at 10°C, but several packages are leaking. Which purchasing principle is MOST directly violated?', 'Right quality', 'Quantity is correct, but temperature and packaging condition fail to meet the established quality specifications.', '["Right quality","Right quantity","Right quality","Right price"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-28T15:38:15.467Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T15:38:15.467Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.599Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T15:38:15.467Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788430407123-2', 'anki-deck-1788430296776-1790433145942-55yvl', 'A hospital is designing a menu for patients requiring therapeutic diets. The menu committee wants to ensure that meals are nutritionally appropriate while also considering food preferences, cultural acceptability, cost, and production capabilities.', 'Integrate nutritional, operational, economic, and patient-related considerations.', 'Effective institutional menu planning requires balancing nutritional adequacy, acceptability, cost, availability, equipment, labor, and therapeutic requirements.', '["Integrate nutritional, operational, economic, and patient-related considerations.","Design the menu based primarily on ingredient cost.","Use the same menu for all patients to simplify production.","None of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-28T15:41:52.836Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T15:41:52.836Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.599Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T15:41:52.836Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788430554378-8', 'anki-deck-1788430296776-1790433145942-55yvl', 'A long-term care facility develops an eight-week menu. During lunch, residents receive the same entrée, vegetable, dessert, and beverage selected by the facility, with no choices offered within any menu category. However, the menu changes from Week 1 to Week 8 and then repeats. Which classification BEST describes the menu?', 'Non-selective cycle menu', 'The menu is non-selective because residents have no choices, and it is a cycle menu because the planned menu repeats after a specified period.', '["Non-selective cycle menu","Selective cycle menu","Non-selective cycle menu","Limited selective menu"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-28T15:36:57.049Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T15:36:57.049Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.599Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T15:36:57.049Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788430576033-9', 'anki-deck-1788430296776-1790433145942-55yvl', 'A receiver is given a purchase order that does not contain the quantities ordered. The receiver independently counts, weighs, and inspects every delivered item before comparing the results with the supplier’s invoice and purchase records. Which receiving method is being used?', 'Blind-check receiving', 'In blind receiving, the receiver does not initially see the quantities ordered and must independently determine the quantity and condition of the products before comparison with purchasing documents.', '["Blind-check receiving","Open-check receiving","Blind-check receiving","Invoice receiving"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-28T15:37:39.715Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T15:37:39.715Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.599Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T15:37:39.715Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788430350716-0', 'anki-deck-1788430296776-1790433145942-55yvl', 'A foodservice operation uses the following inventory data:
• Beginning inventory = ₱25,000
• Purchases = ₱95,000
• Ending inventory = ₱20,000
• Spoilage = ₱4,000
If spoilage is recorded as food used rather than inventory remaining, what is the adjusted food cost including spoilage?', '₱104,000', 'Cost of food used:

₱25,000 + ₱95,000 − ₱20,000 = ₱100,000

Adding spoilage: ₱100,000 + ₱4,000 = ₱104,000 (Spoilage can significantly affect food cost)', '["₱104,000","₱96,000","₱100,000","₱90,000"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 4, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-14T13:06:09.460Z","interval":16,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T13:06:09.460Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.599Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T13:06:09.645Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788430431523-3', 'anki-deck-1788430296776-1790433145942-55yvl', 'A delivery arrives at a foodservice operation. The invoice indicates 20 cases of milk, but the receiver counts only 18 cases. Two cases are also found to have damaged packaging. What should the receiver do FIRST?', 'Document the quantity and condition discrepancy and follow the operation''s receiving procedure.', 'Receiving requires verification of quantity, quality, and condition against purchasing documents. Discrepancies should be documented and handled according to established procedures.', '["Document the quantity and condition discrepancy and follow the operation''s receiving procedure.","Accept all 20 cases and report the discrepancy at the end of the day.","Accept the shipment because the supplier''s invoice is the official record."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-28T15:40:46.480Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T15:40:46.480Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.599Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T15:40:46.480Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788430453579-4', 'anki-deck-1788430296776-1790433145942-55yvl', 'During monitoring, a foodservice employee discovers that a batch of cooked ground beef has reached only 65°C, below the established critical limit. What is the MOST appropriate immediate response?', 'Increase the cooking process until the established critical limit is achieved.', 'A deviation from a critical limit requires corrective action. If the food can still safely undergo the control step, it should be processed until the critical limit is achieved.', '["Increase the cooking process until the established critical limit is achieved.","Serve the food because it has already been cooked.","Place the food in refrigeration and serve it tomorrow."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-28T15:41:30.406Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T15:41:30.406Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.599Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T15:41:30.406Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788430478816-5', 'anki-deck-1788430296776-1790433145942-55yvl', 'A foodservice manager discovers that one of the following foods was left unrefrigerated for several hours. Which food has the highest risk for bacterial growth, assuming all were initially free of pathogens?', 'Cooked chicken breast', 'Cooked chicken provides several favorable conditions described by FAT TOM: food, available moisture, nutrients, and a favorable temperature/pH environment. The other foods have characteristics such as low moisture or high salt that inhibit microbial growth.', '["Cooked chicken breast","Peanut butter","Salted dried fish","Pepper"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-28T15:35:21.916Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T15:35:21.916Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.599Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T15:35:21.916Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788430504953-6', 'anki-deck-1788430296776-1790433145942-55yvl', 'During HACCP development for a foodservice operation, the team determines that chicken must reach an internal temperature of at least 74°C for the specified cooking process. Which HACCP principle is being applied when this temperature is established as the criterion that separates safe from unsafe processing?', 'Establishing critical limits', 'A critical limit is a measurable criterion that must be met at a CCP to control a significant hazard. Temperature and time are common examples.', '["Establishing critical limits","Conducting a hazard analysis","Identifying critical control points","Establishing critical limits"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-28T15:41:05.930Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T15:41:05.930Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.599Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T15:41:05.930Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788430372237-1', 'anki-deck-1788430296776-1790433145942-55yvl', 'A hospital prepares large batches of entrées in a centralized production area. The food is cooked, portioned, rapidly chilled, stored under refrigeration for several days, and reheated shortly before being served to patients. Which foodservice system is best described by this operation?', 'Ready-prepared system', 'In a ready-prepared system, food is prepared in advance, then chilled or frozen for storage and subsequently reheated and served. The key distinguishing feature is the time separation between production and service.', '["Ready-prepared system","Conventional system","Assembly-serve system","Commissary system"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-28T15:39:22.587Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T15:39:22.587Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.599Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T15:39:22.587Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788431128986-9', 'anki-deck-1788430913642-1790433139833-ykmiq', 'It is the process of getting the right product into a facility at the right time and in a form that meets pre-established standards for quantity, quality, and price.', 'Purchasing', 'In foodservice and meal management systems, Purchasing (or procurement) is officially defined as the administrative process of securing the right product, in the right amount, at the right time, from the right supplier, and at the right price. It includes the strategic decision-making involved in establishing product specifications and negotiating market costs prior to the delivery of goods.

• Food Production: The operational stage where raw or prepared ingredients are transformed into finished menu items using various cooking methods.
• Receiving: The specific operation where a facility inspects delivered goods to ensure they match the exact quality, quantity, and price specs previously agreed upon during the purchasing stage. (While Receiving physically "gets" the product into the building, Purchasing is the entire managerial process that orchestrates it).
• Menu planning: The foundational phase where food items are selected and designed on paper based on the nutritional and financial goals of the facility.', '["Menu planning","Food Production","Receiving","Purchasing"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-12-05T13:05:18.762Z","interval":37,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T13:05:18.762Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.654Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T13:05:18.951Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788431045360-6', 'anki-deck-1788430913642-1790433139833-ykmiq', 'What is the right temperature for dry storage?', '60 – 70ºF', 'In foodservice and meal management, dry storage areas are designed to preserve dry staples and canned goods by protecting them from heat and moisture.

Standard foodservice guidelines specify that dry storage temperatures should ideally be maintained between 50ºF and 70ºF (10ºC to 21ºC).

60 – 70ºF fits securely within this recommended parameters. Keeping the room within this temperature range slows chemical reactions, prevents premature food spoilage, and extends the overall shelf life of dry goods.

• 29 to 33ºF: This represents the temperature range used for chilled or super-chilled food storage (such as fresh fish, meat, or poultry holding sections), which is just slightly above or at freezing point.
• 34 – 40ºF: This is the standard operational temperature range for refrigeration / cold storage to prevent bacterial multiplication in perishable commodities.
• 0 to -10ºF: This is the legal threshold required for freezer storage to ensure food remains solidly frozen and safe over long periods.', '["34 – 40ºF","0 to -10ºF","60 – 70ºF","29 to 33ºF"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-12-05T13:06:06.624Z","interval":37,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T13:06:06.624Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.654Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T13:06:06.815Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788431111211-8', 'anki-deck-1788430913642-1790433139833-ykmiq', 'It is a prediction of food needs for a day or other specific period of time.', 'Forecasting', 'In foodservice and operations management, forecasting is defined as the process of predicting or estimating future food needs for a day or another specific period of time. 

It serves as a data-driven tool to ensure the purchasing department orders the correct volume of ingredients and the kitchen staff prepares the right amount of food, which directly minimizes food waste and prevents overproduction.

• Organizing: The management function focused on assembling resources, assigning tasks, and establishing structure to carry out plans.
• Planning: The broader process of defining objectives and determining the overall courses of action to meet them. While planning is based on a forecast, the act of predicting specific time-bound needs is forecasting itself.
• Managing: The overarching process of directing, controlling, and coordinating an organization or system.', '["Forecasting","Planning","Organizing","Managing"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T15:13:21.881Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T15:13:21.881Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.654Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T15:13:21.980Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788430985692-3', 'anki-deck-1788430913642-1790433139833-ykmiq', 'What is considered the catalyst that drives all food service operational functions?', 'Menu', 'The menu is considered the primary driver, catalyst, and focal point of the entire foodservice operation. It dictates every other function within the system, including:

• Purchasing and Procurement: What raw materials and ingredients need to be ordered.
• Equipment and Space Requirements: The types of ovens, prep stations, or storage needed to prepare the items.
• Manpower and Labor: The skill level and number of staff required for preparation and service.
• Budget and Food Cost: The pricing strategy, financial targets, and cost control measures.', '["Food cost","Manpower","Menu","Materials"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T15:12:35.003Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T15:12:35.003Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.654Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T15:12:35.106Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788431095035-7', 'anki-deck-1788430913642-1790433139833-ykmiq', 'Compute the percent shrinkage of pork, casim (raw weight: 850 g, cooked weight: 600 g).', '29.41%', 'Percent Shrinkage: (raw weight - cooked weight) / raw weight * 100= (850 g - 600 g) / 850 g * 100 = 29.41%', '["29.41%","25.00%","38.30%","41.67%"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T15:13:06.417Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T15:13:06.417Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.654Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T15:13:06.514Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788430950542-1', 'anki-deck-1788430913642-1790433139833-ykmiq', 'Which is the least factor to consider in meal planning?', 'Client''s preference', '', '["Nutritive value","Client''s preference","Food budget and cost","Number and type of clientele"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T15:12:40.346Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T15:12:40.346Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.654Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T15:12:40.440Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788430933252-0', 'anki-deck-1788430913642-1790433139833-ykmiq', 'What is the Temperature Danger Zone?', '41 to -140ºF', 'The Temperature Danger Zone represents the environmental range where foodborne pathogenic bacteria (such as Salmonella, E. coli, and Staphylococcus aureus) reproduce most rapidly. Under optimal conditions inside this window, bacterial populations can double in number in as little as 10 to 20 minutes.

To protect public health, regulatory standards mandate keeping cold foods strictly below 41ºF and hot foods above 140ºF (or 135ºF depending on the specific municipal framework) to prevent bacteria from reaching dangerous, illness-causing thresholds.', '["0 to -10ºF","41 to -140ºF","161 – 212ºF","32 – 40ºF"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T15:12:52.981Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T15:12:52.981Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.654Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-27T15:12:53.079Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788431026511-5', 'anki-deck-1788430913642-1790433139833-ykmiq', 'The following is the importance of food safety, except:', 'To reverse the spread of diseases', 'Food safety is a preventive discipline, not a curative treatment. While proper food handling, sanitation, and temperature control work effectively to prevent the transmission of foodborne pathogens, food safety measures alone cannot "reverse" or cure the spread of diseases once a population or individual is infected. Dealing with the active spread or reversal of clinical diseases falls under the scope of medical treatments, epidemiology, pharmaceutical interventions, and clinical healthcare protocols.

• To create and maintain healthful and hygienic conditions for the family: This is a fundamental, domestic goal of everyday food hygiene to protect household health.
• To gain market access: Under national regulations such as the Food Safety Act of 2013 (RA 10611), ensuring rigid food safety compliance is a legal mandatory prerequisite to protect consumer health and facilitate market access for local commercial food products globally and locally.
• To prevent food contamination and food spoilage: This is a primary technical purpose of food safety frameworks—keeping biological, chemical, and physical hazards out of the food supply chain.', '["To create and maintain healthful and hygienic conditions for the family","To prevent food contamination and food spoilage","To reverse the spread of diseases","To gain market access"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-12-05T13:05:46.716Z","interval":37,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T13:05:46.716Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.654Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T13:05:46.907Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788431002781-4', 'anki-deck-1788430913642-1790433139833-ykmiq', 'The following is the purpose of producing quality foods in large volumes, except:', 'Improve aesthetic quality', 'In quantity food production (such as institutional catering or commercial food service), food items must be processed in bulk to feed a large number of people efficiently. While massive industrial production successfully drives safety, flavor modification, and nutrient conservation via standardized operational formulas, it strips away the ability to execute delicate, artistic, or customized plating.

Producing food in massive batches requires prioritizing uniform output speed, thermal safety, and broad scale-stability over intricate visual designs. Because bulk distribution environments (like hospital lines, cafeteria trays, or packaging conveyor belts) inherently limit individual presentation, enhancing or customizing the refined aesthetic beauty of a dish is generally not an achievable technical objective or purpose of mass cooking.', '["Improve aesthetic quality","Develop, enhance, or alter flavor","Minimize quality losses","Destroy harmful microorganisms"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-12-05T13:05:42.423Z","interval":37,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T13:05:42.423Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.654Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T13:05:42.606Z"'::jsonb)
