Hypertensive Stage II: >160/>100', '', '["Normal: 80\n\nPrehypertensive: 120-139/80-89\n\nHypertensive Stage I: 140-159/90-99\n\nHypertensive Stage II: >160/>100","Congestive Heart Failure","Cerebrovascular accident","Gastrosucchorrhea"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-31T16:26:18.157Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.35,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-28T16:26:18.157Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.801Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-28T16:26:18.332Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756794842762-78', 'anki-deck-1783610598974-1790433142628-tj9iq', 'A procedure when the entire colon is bypassed, and opening is created from the ileum that is attached directly to the anus.', 'Ileorectal anastomosis', 'An anastomosis is a surgical term that means connecting or joining two distinct structures inside the body.

When the entire colon is removed or bypassed, the small intestine (specifically the ileum) must be carefully brought down and surgically sewn directly to the remaining rectum or anus to allow waste to leave the body naturally without needing a permanent external pouch or stoma bag.', '["Tonsillectomy","Cholecystectomy","Hemorrhoidectomy","Ileorectal anastomosis"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-31T11:16:00.045Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.35,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-28T11:16:00.045Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.801Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-28T11:16:00.218Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756794802081-77', 'anki-deck-1783610598974-1790433142628-tj9iq', 'Pertains to the surgical removal of hemorrhoids.', 'Hemorrhoidectomy', '', '["Tonsillectomy","Cholecystectomy","Hemorrhoidectomy","Ileorectal anastomosis"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-24T13:42:10.774Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:42:10.774Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.801Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:42:10.774Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756791940777-41', 'anki-deck-1783610598974-1790433142628-tj9iq', 'A symptom of several disease.', 'Diarrhea', 'Diarrhea is not a disease itself; it is a clinical symptom triggered by a wide variety of underlying localized or systemic pathologies.

It serves as a primary warning sign for numerous distinct conditions across the diagnostic spectrum, including bacterial or viral infections (food poisoning), inflammatory bowel diseases (Crohn''s or Ulcerative Colitis), malabsorption disorders (Celiac disease), metabolic conditions (hyperthyroidism), and functional bowel issues (IBS).

From a board exam standpoint, identifying diarrhea as a cross-categorical symptom is essential because its presence across multiple diseases uniformly dictates immediate nutritional interventions—specifically managing rapid fluid losses, replacing lost electrolytes, and mitigating the risk of acute malnutrition.', '["Diarrhea","Constipation","Diverticulosis","Diverticula"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-31T15:24:41.171Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.35,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-28T15:24:41.171Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.801Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-28T15:24:41.360Z"'::jsonb),
