('anki-card-1788373790699-18', 'anki-deck-1788373344910-1790433142628-l4qb7', 'An 82-year-old man with poor dentition, constipation, and decreased taste sensation consumes mainly soft, low-fiber foods. Which physiological factor most significantly contributes to his constipation?', 'Decreased GI motility combined with inadequate fiber and fluid intake', '', '["Hypogeusia and hyposmia reduce appetite, leading to decreased gastric secretions","Limited caloric intake reduces intestinal bulk and slows peristalsis","Decreased GI motility combined with inadequate fiber and fluid intake","Reduced pancreatic enzyme secretion prevents carbohydrate digestion and stool formation"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-24T13:39:54.587Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:39:54.587Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.825Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:39:55.168Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788373417625-2', 'anki-deck-1788373344910-1790433142628-l4qb7', 'You are counseling the parents of an 8-year-old girl who exhibits early signs of body image concerns and requests to begin dieting despite having a normal BMI for her age. Her mother mentions she had struggles with her own weight as a child. Considering the developmental context and evidence on feeding practices, what is the most appropriate nutrition counseling approach?', 'Counsel parents to avoid restrictive feeding practices, emphasize normal body changes during preadolescence, and model positive attitudes toward food and body image', '', '["Counsel parents to avoid restrictive feeding practices, emphasize normal body changes during preadolescence, and model positive attitudes toward food and body image","Suggest the family focus exclusively on increasing physical activity without addressing dietary or psychological concerns","Recommend comprehensive metabolic testing and micronutrient supplementation to address potential nutritional imbalances","Support the family''s dieting approach and implement calorie-restricted meal plans to prevent future obesity"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-24T13:30:00.669Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:30:00.669Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.825Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:30:01.209Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788373768245-17', 'anki-deck-1788373344910-1790433142628-l4qb7', 'An 78-year-old male presents with fatigue and dyspnea. Lab results show low hemoglobin and B₁₂ levels. His stomach biopsy reveals atrophy of gastric mucosa. Which physiological change best explains his condition?', 'Decreased intrinsic factor production impairs B₁₂ absorption in the ileum', '', '["Reduced iron absorption due to decreased stomach acid leads to iron deficiency anemia","Decreased pepsinogen secretion prevents protein breakdown needed for B₁₂ binding","Insufficient dietary B₁₂ intake from limited meat consumption causes pernicious anemia","Decreased intrinsic factor production impairs B₁₂ absorption in the ileum"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-24T13:28:22.739Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:28:22.739Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.825Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:28:23.028Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788373443628-3', 'anki-deck-1788373344910-1790433142628-l4qb7', 'A school nutrition program is evaluating its canteen offerings. Currently, 60% of items sold fall into the RED category (high sodium, sugar, and saturated fat). The program director argues that removing these items will reduce canteen revenue and student satisfaction. Using principles of nutrition assessment and public health nutrition, which evidence-based argument best supports the need for menu revision?', 'The current menu contradicts the school''s nutrition education mission and contributes to rising childhood obesity and overweight trends documented in surveillance data, undermining long-term student health outcomes', '', '["Menu changes in a single school canteen will have negligible impact on regional obesity trends, so revision is not justified","Students who choose unhealthy foods are responsible for their own health outcomes; the school should not restrict their autonomy","The canteen''s financial sustainability is more important than menu composition; student preferences should determine food availability","The current menu contradicts the school''s nutrition education mission and contributes to rising childhood obesity and overweight trends documented in surveillance data, undermining long-term student health outcomes"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-24T13:23:41.752Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:23:41.752Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.825Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:23:42.280Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788373469747-4', 'anki-deck-1788373344910-1790433142628-l4qb7', 'A 10-year-old child with cystic fibrosis is enrolled in a school feeding program designed to provide one-third of daily recommended nutrient intake. Standard school meals provide approximately 2,060 kcal and 43g protein daily for this age group. Considering the pathophysiology of cystic fibrosis and evidence-based nutrition management, what is the most significant limitation of the current school feeding program for this child?', 'The standard meal energy and protein amounts are insufficient because CF requires two to four times usual recommendations to compensate for malabsorption; additional medical nutrition therapy and enzyme supplementation are necessary', '', '["The standard school meal is adequate; CF management requires only regular medication compliance without nutritional modification","The standard meal energy and protein amounts are insufficient because CF requires two to four times usual recommendations to compensate for malabsorption; additional medical nutrition therapy and enzyme supplementation are necessary","All children with chronic conditions require identical meal modifications; the school should implement the same increased portions for every student","Enzyme supplementation alone will normalize nutrient absorption, so the standard meal amounts are sufficient"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-24T13:29:33.575Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:29:33.575Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.825Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:29:33.856Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788373699913-14', 'anki-deck-1788373344910-1790433142628-l4qb7', 'A 38-year-old client with hypertension and obesity reports consuming alcohol daily and minimal physical activity. According to the document, which consequence of this lifestyle pattern poses the greatest nutritional risk?', 'Alcohol provides empty calories while displacing nutrient-dense foods, compounding obesity and CVD risk', '', '["Alcohol provides empty calories while displacing nutrient-dense foods, compounding obesity and CVD risk","Physical inactivity alone causes malabsorption independent of alcohol intake","Alcohol consumption has no documented impact on nutrient absorption","Alcohol contains complete proteins essential for muscle maintenance"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-24T13:38:53.713Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:38:53.713Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.825Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:38:54.047Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788373396201-1', 'anki-deck-1788373344910-1790433142628-l4qb7', 'A 9-year-old boy presents with poor appetite and frequent school absences. Upon assessment, you discover he participates in multiple after-school activities with minimal rest periods. His parents report he skips breakfast regularly and often trades his packed lunch with classmates. Based on nutritional assessment principles for school-age children, which intervention would most effectively address the root cause of his inadequate nutrient intake?', 'Educate the family on balancing academic, physical, and rest activities while establishing a structured meal schedule that includes breakfast and monitored lunch consumption', '', '["Educate the family on balancing academic, physical, and rest activities while establishing a structured meal schedule that includes breakfast and monitored lunch consumption","Increase the frequency and variety of sweets in packed lunches to make them more appealing and less likely to be traded","Restrict the child''s participation in after-school activities until appetite improves and weight gains are documented","Recommend high-calorie nutritional supplements to compensate for missed meals and increase overall energy intake"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-24T13:37:57.093Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:37:57.093Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.825Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:37:57.409Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788373375295-0', 'anki-deck-1788373344910-1790433142628-l4qb7', 'During a nutrition education session, a school-age child states, ''I don''t like vegetables, so I''ve never tried broccoli.'' When offered steamed broccoli once, she refused it immediately. Her parent conclude the child will never accept vegetables and stops offering them. From a developmental and behavioral nutrition perspective, what is the most significant error in the parent''s reasoning?', 'Research demonstrates that children typically require 8 - 10 exposures to new foods before acceptance; one exposure is insufficient to establish a lasting food preference, and repeated exposure with positive reinforcement is necessary', '', '["The child simply lacks motivation to try new foods; if she wanted to eat vegetables, she would accept them on first offering","Because children naturally prefer sweet and salty tastes, they are biologically incapable of developing preferences for bitter or mild-flavored vegetables","Research demonstrates that children typically require 8 - 10 exposures to new foods before acceptance; one exposure is insufficient to establish a lasting food preference, and repeated exposure with positive reinforcement is necessary","Children''s taste preferences are genetically determined at birth; environmental exposure has minimal influence on food acceptance"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-24T13:41:11.621Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:41:11.621Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.825Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:41:12.001Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788373744407-16', 'anki-deck-1788373344910-1790433142628-l4qb7', 'During a nutrition screening, an 80-year-old widow scores 7 on the Nutrition Screening Initiative checklist. She reports eating alone, taking 4 medications daily, and losing 8 pounds in 6 months. What is the most critical next step?', 'Refer for comprehensive nutritional assessment and evaluate for depression and social isolation', '', '["Refer for comprehensive nutritional assessment and evaluate for depression and social isolation","Order laboratory tests for malabsorption and refer to gastroenterology for evaluation","Discontinue all medications and substitute with herbal alternatives to improve appetite","Immediately prescribe high-calorie supplements and increase meal frequency to 5 meals daily"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-24T13:40:10.320Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:40:10.320Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.825Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:40:11.064Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788373721620-15', 'anki-deck-1788373344910-1790433142628-l4qb7', 'A 72-year-old female with hypertension and osteoporosis requires nutritional counseling. Based on age-related physiological changes and her conditions, which dietary recommendation is most appropriate?', 'Increase calcium intake to 800 mg/day and reduce sodium to prevent bone loss and manage blood pressure', '', '["Increase protein to 2.5 g/kg/day to maximize muscle synthesis and prevent sarcopenia","Increase calcium intake to 800 mg/day and reduce sodium to prevent bone loss and manage blood pressure","Recommend vitamin A supplementation above RDA to enhance immune function","Maintain high-calorie intake of 2,500 kcal/day to prevent weight loss and muscle wasting"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-24T13:37:17.527Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:37:17.527Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.825Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:37:17.890Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788373679407-13', 'anki-deck-1788373344910-1790433142628-l4qb7', 'A 28-year-old female client reports chronic stress, limited time for meal preparation, and reliance on processed snacks. Based on adult nutrition factors, which social-economic factor most directly impacts her nutritional status?', 'Work-life balance demands reduce time for food preparation, leading to nutrient-poor food choices', '', '["Processed foods provide all necessary nutrients if consumed in adequate quantity","Psychological stress increases metabolic rate, eliminating need for dietary counseling","Her age group naturally requires fewer micronutrients than older adults","Work-life balance demands reduce time for food preparation, leading to nutrient-poor food choices"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-24T13:39:13.961Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:39:13.961Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.825Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:39:14.291Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788373655137-12', 'anki-deck-1788373344910-1790433142628-l4qb7', 'A 60-year-old client with arthritis reports difficulty shopping and preparing meals, reduced food intake, and declining nutrient absorption. Which factor requires the most immediate nutritional intervention?', 'Functional limitations affecting food access combined with chronic illness reducing nutrient absorption', '', '["Advanced age automatically requires 50% reduction in all nutrient intakes","Arthritis pain is unrelated to nutritional status and requires only pain management","Functional limitations affecting food access combined with chronic illness reducing nutrient absorption","Increased food quantity compensates for impaired absorption in older adults"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-24T13:40:51.543Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:40:51.543Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.825Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:40:51.827Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788373633197-11', 'anki-deck-1788373344910-1790433142628-l4qb7', 'A 45-year-old male client reports decreased appetite, unintentional weight loss, and difficulty swallowing. Based on adult nutrition physiology, which physiological change most likely contributes to these symptoms?', 'Slowed gastric emptying and diminished taste and smell sensations', '', '["Requires immediate pharmacological intervention without dietary modification","Slowed gastric emptying and diminished taste and smell sensations","Elevated estrogen levels causing digestive distress","Increased metabolic rate requiring excessive caloric intake"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-24T13:33:07.271Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:33:07.271Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.825Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:33:07.675Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788373610875-10', 'anki-deck-1788373344910-1790433142628-l4qb7', 'A 52-year-old female client in early menopause reports weight gain despite unchanged eating habits and increased fatigue. Which nutritional intervention strategy would best address her underlying physiological changes?', 'Increase calcium and vitamin D intake; maintain protein at 10-15% of calories; encourage regular physical activity', '', '["Focus solely on carbohydrate reduction; avoid protein supplementation","Increase estrogen replacement therapy without dietary modifications","Reduce total caloric intake by 50% and eliminate all dietary fats","Increase calcium and vitamin D intake; maintain protein at 10-15% of calories; encourage regular physical activity"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-24T13:28:57.687Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:28:57.687Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.825Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:28:58.026Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788373593617-9', 'anki-deck-1788373344910-1790433142628-l4qb7', 'You are counseling a 14-year-old boy who is an endurance athlete with a BMI at the 50th percentile. He reports consuming 83% of his meals from fast food establishments and expresses concern about his energy levels during training. His current energy intake is approximately 2,500 kcal/day. What is the most appropriate nutritional intervention considering his developmental stage, athletic demands, and current eating pattern?', 'Assess his actual energy requirements based on his growth spurt phase and activity intensity; educate him on nutrient-dense alternatives that are convenient, portable, and can be incorporated into his current fast-food pattern rather than complete dietary overhaul', '', '["Focus exclusively on increasing protein intake to 100+ grams per day to maximize muscle mass, as bone health is not a concern for male athletes","Recommend complete elimination of fast food and preparation of home-cooked meals to ensure nutrient density","Assess his actual energy requirements based on his growth spurt phase and activity intensity; educate him on nutrient-dense alternatives that are convenient, portable, and can be incorporated into his current fast-food pattern rather than complete dietary overhaul","Maintain current intake at 2,500 kcal/day since his BMI is normal and energy requirements are the same as non-athletes"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-24T13:27:49.175Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:27:49.175Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.825Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:27:49.591Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788373570046-8', 'anki-deck-1788373344910-1790433142628-l4qb7', 'During a nutrition counseling session, a 16-year-old male who is 1.65 m tall and weighs 72 kg (BMI approximately 26.4 kg/m²) reports consuming high amounts of omega-6 fatty acids from snacks and fast foods but minimal omega-3 intake. His parents express concern about his overweight status and sedentary behavior. According to current adolescent nutrition guidelines and considering his developmental stage, what is the most evidence-based approach to address his nutritional and lifestyle concerns?', 'Implement a multifaceted intervention addressing the omega-6 to omega-3 ratio (targeting 4:1), reduce total fat intake to no more than 30% of total energy requirements with saturated fat below 10%, increase physical activity, and involve him in goal-setting to promote autonomy and long-term behavior change', '', '["Prescribe intensive exercise regimens immediately without considering his current sedentary status or psychosocial readiness, as physical activity has no psychological benefits in adolescence","Focus exclusively on total caloric reduction without addressing fat composition, since the type of fat consumed does not affect adolescent health outcomes","Implement a multifaceted intervention addressing the omega-6 to omega-3 ratio (targeting 4:1), reduce total fat intake to no more than 30% of total energy requirements with saturated fat below 10%, increase physical activity, and involve him in goal-setting to promote autonomy and long-term behavior change","Recommend complete elimination of all dietary fats to rapidly reduce his BMI, as all fats contribute equally to weight gain"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-24T13:23:09.033Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:23:09.033Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.825Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:23:09.398Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788373544875-7', 'anki-deck-1788373344910-1790433142628-l4qb7', 'A 15-year-old female presents to your clinic with complaints of fatigue, shortness of breath, and poor academic performance. Her dietary history reveals she follows a strict vegan diet and frequently skips breakfast. Her BMI is within normal range. Based on your nutritional assessment, which micronutrient deficiency is most likely contributing to her symptoms, and what is the primary dietary reason for this deficiency?', 'Iron deficiency anemia due to inadequate intake of heme iron from animal sources combined with poor bioavailability of nonheme iron from plant-based foods, exacerbated by breakfast skipping which reduces overall nutrient intake', '', '["Zinc deficiency, because plant-based sources contain inhibitors that completely prevent zinc absorption","Iron deficiency anemia due to inadequate intake of heme iron from animal sources combined with poor bioavailability of nonheme iron from plant-based foods, exacerbated by breakfast skipping which reduces overall nutrient intake","Calcium deficiency, because dairy products are the primary source of bioavailable calcium","Protein deficiency, because vegans cannot obtain adequate protein from plant sources alone"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-24T13:32:47.877Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:32:47.877Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.825Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:32:48.656Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788373520954-6', 'anki-deck-1788373344910-1790433142628-l4qb7', 'A 13-year-old girl at Tanner Stage 3 presents with irregular menstrual periods and reports consuming approximately 1,200 kcal/day from her diet consisting mainly of salads, diet sodas, and occasional fruits. She expresses dissatisfaction with her body shape despite having a BMI at the 75th percentile. Which developmental and nutritional factors should guide your intervention strategy?', 'Recognize this as a critical period for bone mass accretion and psychosocial development; address both the inadequate energy intake and body image concerns through empowering, non-judgmental counseling that involves her in decision-making while monitoring for progression toward clinical eating disorder', '', '["Recognize this as a critical period for bone mass accretion and psychosocial development; address both the inadequate energy intake and body image concerns through empowering, non-judgmental counseling that involves her in decision-making while monitoring for progression toward clinical eating disorder","Focus only on her current BMI percentile and reassure her that her eating pattern is acceptable since she is not yet overweight","Attribute her irregular menses solely to normal puberty and avoid nutrition intervention, as menstrual irregularity always resolves independently","Support her current 1,200 kcal intake as appropriate for weight maintenance and encourage continued restriction if she continues to express body dissatisfaction"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-24T13:37:35.475Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:37:35.475Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.825Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:37:35.784Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788373494235-5', 'anki-deck-1788373344910-1790433142628-l4qb7', 'A 17-year-old pregnant adolescent presents for nutrition counseling. She is 1.48 m tall, weighs 58 kg pre-pregnancy (BMI 26.5 kg/m²), and is currently at 20 weeks gestation. Her dietary assessment reveals low calcium intake, inadequate protein consumption, and iron-deficiency anemia (Hgb 10.2 g/dL). She reports limited financial resources and attends school intermittently. Based on a comprehensive understanding of adolescent pregnancy risks and her specific circumstances, what is your priority nutrition intervention?', 'Address iron deficiency anemia immediately as it increases risk for prolonged labor and adverse outcomes; simultaneously ensure adequate calcium and protein intake to support both her continued growth and fetal development; provide practical, affordable food guidance considering her resource limitations and school schedule', '', '["Treat iron deficiency anemia as an isolated concern without addressing concurrent calcium and protein needs, as these nutrients do not affect pregnancy outcomes in adolescents","Focus intervention solely on her height and pelvic size as these are the primary determinants of obstetric risk in adolescent pregnancy","Provide standard adult pregnancy nutrition guidelines without modification, since adolescent and adult pregnant individuals have identical nutritional requirements and risk profiles","Address iron deficiency anemia immediately as it increases risk for prolonged labor and adverse outcomes; simultaneously ensure adequate calcium and protein intake to support both her continued growth and fetal development; provide practical, affordable food guidance considering her resource limitations and school schedule"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-24T13:30:28.712Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-23T13:30:28.712Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.825Z"'::jsonb, '"20