('anki-card-1757829525347-130', 'anki-deck-1783610400188-1790433145939-pouc6', 'Animal cell membranes are mainly composed of a phospholipid bilayer.  What happens to a triglyceride to form a phospholipid?', 'Loss of one fatty acid and gain of one inorganic phosphate group', '', '["Gain of two inorganic phosphates","Loss of one fatty acid and gain of one inorganic phosphate group","All three fatty acids replaced by inorganic phosphates","Gain of two organic phosphate"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.865Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757829572127-132', 'anki-deck-1783610400188-1790433145939-pouc6', 'The enzyme pepsin is not denatured in the stomach despite the very acidic environment attributed to hydrochloric acid (HCl).
How can this be?', 'pepsin is secreted in its precursor form (pepsinogen)', '', '["pepsin is the only protein-enzyme that functions best in an acidic environment","pepsin is able to resist dentauration by increasing  the pH within the stomach, making it less acidic","pepsin is also digested along with other proteins in the stomach","pepsin is secreted in its precursor form (pepsinogen)"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.865Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757829594410-133', 'anki-deck-1783610400188-1790433145939-pouc6', 'A bruise, medically known as contusion, is made when a certain external area of the body is hit by something really hard, and
the capillaries in that area collapse.  It first appears on the skin with a violet color. After a few days, it becomes greenish in color.
A few more days after, it appears yellowish in color, until it eventually fades and disappears. What causes this bruise to appear
greenish in color?', 'biliverdin', '', '["biliverdin","hemoglobin","bilirubin","stercobilin"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.865Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757829616126-134', 'anki-deck-1783610400188-1790433145939-pouc6', 'Which of the following is not a form of feedback inhibition?', 'Continuous exposure to a delectable aroma of food causes secretion of saliva and movement of the gastrointestinal tract.', '', '["An increase in T3 and T4 stops the release of TSH and TRH from the hypothalamus and pituitary gland.","Continuous exposure to a delectable aroma of food causes secretion of saliva and movement of the gastrointestinal tract.","An elevation of estrogen and progesterone ceases the secretion of FSH and LH by the anterior pituitary gland.","All of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.865Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757829642209-135', 'anki-deck-1783610400188-1790433145939-pouc6', 'Ammonia is a nitrogenous waste product of protein metabolism, and is harmful especially in high concentrations in the human
body. Urea cycle is a means to detoxify and to prevent the accumulation of amonia in the body by converting it to urea, and
eventually excreted in the urine.  How many moles of nitrogen enter the urea cycle in every turn?', '2', '', '["4","2","1","3"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.865Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757829662308-136', 'anki-deck-1783610400188-1790433145939-pouc6', 'Insulin is a peptide hormone produced in the pancreas by the beta cells.  It aims to lower the glucose (sugar) levels in the blood,
and is normally secreted every after meals.  Their action is to activate the transporters of glucose found on the surface of the
cells, so that the cells can take up glucose from the blood and into the cells.  What glucose transporter is regulated by the action
