('anki-card-1757930964622-16', 'anki-deck-1783609398838-1790433146200-hye2o', 'If one identical twin who leads a sedentary lifestyle has a RENI of 1.3mg of B2, what would be the approximate recommendation for the other twin who engages in regular physical activity?*', '3mg', '', '["3mg","6mg","9mg","6mg"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.883Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757930947338-15', 'anki-deck-1783609398838-1790433146200-hye2o', 'Which of the following is a characteristic of thiamin stability in relation to cooking method?*', 'Steaming the food can lead to substantial thiamin loss due to high heat needed to form the steam.', '', '["Microwaving the food conserves much of the thiamin.","Prolonged heating of the food has little, if any, affect on the vitamin.","Boiling the food tends to conserve thiamin by a forming stable, hydrated complex.","Steaming the food can lead to substantial thiamin loss due to high heat needed to form the steam."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.883Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757930932939-14', 'anki-deck-1783609398838-1790433146200-hye2o', 'Which of the following diets is likely to lead to beriberi?*', 'High intakes of polished rice', '', '["Low intakes of whole grains","High intakes of polished rice","High intakes of unrefined rice","Low intakes of enriched grains"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.883Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757930921275-13', 'anki-deck-1783609398838-1790433146200-hye2o', 'Which of the following explains why B vitamins deficiencies lead to lack of energy?*', 'Coenzymes needed for energy metabolism are produced in insufficient amounts.', '', '["B vitamins are a source of kcalories.","Absorption of carbohydrates and fats is decreased.","Oxygen for energy metabolism cannot be transported to the cells.","Coenzymes needed for energy metabolism are produced in insufficient amounts."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.883Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757930908108-12', 'anki-deck-1783609398838-1790433146200-hye2o', 'Which of the following is not a general characteristic of the fat-soluble vitamin?*', 'Excesses are eliminated from the kidneys.', '', '["Excesses are eliminated from the kidneys.","Absorption is via the lymphatic circulation.","Several of them require protein carriers for transport.","They can be stored in relatively large amounts in certain body tissues."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.883Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757930891975-11', 'anki-deck-1783609398838-1790433146200-hye2o', 'Which of the following vitamins would be removed in the production of skim milk?*', 'Vitamin A', '', '["Thiamin","Vitamin A","Riboflavin","Vitamin B12"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.883Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757930877793-10', 'anki-deck-1783609398838-1790433146200-hye2o', 'General characteristics of water-soluble vitamins include all of the following except*', 'They must be consumed daily.', '', '["They must be consumed daily.","Toxic levels in the body are rarely found.","They are absorbed directly into the blood.","Excesses are eliminated from the kidneys."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.883Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757930864927-9', 'anki-deck-1783609398838-1790433146200-hye2o', 'Which of the following is a feature of the waist-to-hip ratio indicator?*', 'It is most useful in accessing changes in body fat.', '', '["It correlates very closely to underwater weighing.","It is most useful in accessing changes in body fat.","It is calculated by dividing the waist circumference by the square of the hip dimension.","It generally remains constant despite weight loss-induced changes in body fat distribution"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.883Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
