('anki-card-1756219566547-64', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'It refers to the behaviors that can lead to good health and improve cleanliness.', 'hygiene', 'Hygiene encompasses practices and behaviors that promote health and cleanliness, such as handwashing, personal grooming, maintaining clean environments, and following proper food handling practices. It is essential for preventing the spread of diseases and maintaining overall well-being.', '["sanitation","cleaning","disinfection","hygiene"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:09:46.121Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:09:46.121Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:09:46.121Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756218094599-44', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Typically refers to dishes originating from or in the style of Nice, France. It can include various salads, seafood dishes, or other regional specialties.', 'Nicoise', '• Hors d’oeuvres: Refers to small dishes served before a main meal to stimulate the appetite. It can include a variety of items such as finger foods, dips, spreads, or small hot and cold dishes.
• Canapés: Small pieces of bread or pastry topped with savory garnishes, often served as appetizers.
• Macedoine: A culinary term that typically refers to a mixture or salad containing small diced vegetables or fruits.', '["Canapes","Hors d''oeuvres","Macedoine","Nicoise"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T13:05:12.517Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:05:12.517Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:05:12.517Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756218046584-43', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'A culinary term that typically refers to a mixture or salad containing small diced vegetables or fruits.', 'Macedoine', 'Hors d’oeuvres (Correct answer): Refers to small dishes served before a main meal to stimulate the appetite. It can include a variety of items such as finger foods, dips, spreads, or small hot and cold dishes.

Canapés: Small pieces of bread or pastry topped with savory garnishes, often served as appetizers.

Niçoise: Typically refers to dishes originating from or in the style of Nice, France. It can include various salads, seafood dishes, or other regional specialties.', '["Canapes","Hors d''oeuvres","Macedoine","Nicoise"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:16:30.030Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:16:30.030Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:16:30.030Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756218001337-42', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Assorted appetizers taken before the main dishes:', 'Hors d''oeuvres', 'Hors d’oeuvres refers to small dishes served before a main meal to stimulate the appetite. It can include a variety of items such as finger foods, dips, spreads, or small hot and cold dishes.

• Canapés: Small pieces of bread or pastry topped with savory garnishes, often served as appetizers.
• Macedoine: A culinary term that typically refers to a mixture or salad containing small diced vegetables or fruits.
• Niçoise: Typically refers to dishes originating from or in the style of Nice, France. It can include various salads, seafood dishes, or other regional specialties.', '["Canapes","Hors d''oeuvres","Macedoine","Nicoise"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T13:18:57.638Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:18:57.638Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:18:57.638Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756217887157-41', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'The fizz or bubbles in sparkling water is attributed to:', 'carbon dioxide', 'Carbon dioxide (CO2) is dissolved under pressure in sparkling water. When the pressure is released, such as when the bottle is opened or the water is poured, the dissolved CO2 escapes as bubbles, creating the characteristic fizziness or effervescence in the water.

• Carbon carbonate: This is not a correct term; carbonates are compounds involving carbon and oxygen, but not directly related to the fizz in sparkling water.
• Oxygen bromide: These are two separate chemical elements and do not contribute to the fizz in sparkling water.
• Galactose: A type of sugar found in dairy products and some plants, not related to the fizz in sparkling water.', '["carbon carbonate","carbon dioxide","oxygen bromide","galactose"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:16:22.863Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:16:22.863Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:16:22.863Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756217843194-40', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'The second-in-command in the kitchen, assisting the Executive Chef in managing kitchen staff, overseeing food production, and ensuring kitchen opertions run smoothly.', 'Sous Chef', '', '["Garde manger","Sommelier","Executive Chef","Sous Chef"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T13:59:35.411Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:59:35.411Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:59:35.411Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756217770546-39', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'A wine steward or wine expert responsible for selecting and serving wines in a restaurant.', 'Sommelier', '• Executive Chef: In the traditional kitchen brigade system, which was developed by Georges Auguste Escoffier, the Executive Chef holds the highest authority and responsibility in the kitchen. This role involves overseeing all aspects of the kitchen operations, including menu planning, food preparation, kitchen staff management, and ensuring culinary standards and quality control.

• Garde Manger: The Garde Manger, also known as the pantry chef, is responsible for cold food preparation, such as salads, appetizers, and sometimes desserts.

• Sous Chef: The second-in-command in the kitchen, assisting the Executive Chef in managing kitchen staff, overseeing food production, and ensuring kitchen operations run smoothly.', '["Garde manger","Sommelier","Executive Chef","Sous Chef"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T13:17:38.628Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:17:38.628Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:17:38.628Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756217741016-38', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Also known as the pantry chef, is responsible for cold food preparation, such as salad, appetizers, and sometimes desserts.', 'Garde manger', '', '["Garde manger","Sommelier","Executive Chef","Sous Chef"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T13:27:05.181Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:27:05.181Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:27:05.181Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756217699951-37', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Head of the kitchen brigade system.', 'Executive Chef', 'In the traditional kitchen brigade system, which was developed by Georges Auguste Escoffier, the Executive Chef holds the highest authority and responsibility in the kitchen. This role involves overseeing all aspects of the kitchen operations, including menu planning, food preparation, kitchen staff management, and ensuring culinary standards and quality control.

• Garde Manger: The Garde Manger, also known as the pantry chef, is responsible for cold food preparation, such as salads, appetizers, and sometimes desserts.
• Sommelier: A wine steward or wine expert responsible for selecting and serving wines in a restaurant.
• Sous Chef: The second-in-command in the kitchen, assisting the Executive Chef in managing kitchen staff, overseeing food production, and ensuring kitchen operations run smoothly.', '["Garde manger","Sommelier","Executive Chef","Sous Chef"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T13:19:34.724Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:19:34.724Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:19:34.798Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756220573567-75', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'A prediction of food needs for a day or other specific period of time.', 'Forecasting', 'Forecasting in the context of food service involves estimating the quantity of food that will be required to meet customer demand over a certain period. This helps in planning and preparing the right amount of food to minimize waste while ensuring that enough food is available to meet customer orders.', '["Purchasing","Forecasting","Production","Recipe writing"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T13:39:17.827Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:39:17.827Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:39:17.827Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756217650552-36', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Tequila-based cocktail with lime juice and triple sec.', 'Margarita', 'Margarita typically consists of tequila, lime juice (often freshly squeezed), and triple sec (an orange-flavored liqueur). It is usually served in a glass with a salted rim. The combination of tequila’s agave flavor, tart lime juice, and sweet triple sec creates a balanced and refreshing cocktail.

• Martini: Typically made with gin and vermouth, garnished with an olive or a lemon twist.
• Tequila Sunrise: Made with tequila, orange juice, and grenadine syrup, creating a layered sunrise effect.
• Daiquiri: A classic cocktail made with rum, lime juice, and simple syrup, served straight up or on the rocks.', '["Martini","Tequila sunrise","Daiquiri","Margarita"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T13:38:21.116Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:38:21.116Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:38:21.116Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756217610571-35', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Drip is a method of making:', 'coffee', 'In coffee brewing, the drip method, also known as drip coffee or filter coffee, involves pouring hot water over ground coffee beans contained in a filter. The water drips through the coffee grounds and filter into a pot or carafe below, extracting flavor and oils from the coffee grounds as it passes through. This method is popular for its simplicity and ability to produce a clean, flavorful cup of coffee.', '["tea","chocolate","coffee","breakfast certial"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:14:47.279Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:14:47.279Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:14:47.279Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756217577340-34', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Inversion of sucrose can be facilitated by adding:', 'acid', 'The inversion of sucrose (the process where sucrose is hydrolyzed into its component sugars glucose and fructose) can be facilitated by adding acid.

Sucrose is a disaccharide composed of glucose and fructose. In the presence of an acid (such as lemon juice or cream of tartar), the acid catalyzes the hydrolysis of sucrose into its monosaccharide components, glucose, and fructose. This process is commonly used in cooking and baking to make syrups, candies, and other confections where the breakdown of sucrose into its sweeter-tasting components (glucose and fructose) enhances sweetness and texture.', '["fat","table sugar","acid","honey"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:09:21.558Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:09:21.558Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:09:21.558Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756217507143-33', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Skill that is most essential for top level management:', 'conceptual', 'Conceptual skill involves the ability to think strategically, understand complex situations, and develop innovative solutions. Top-level managers need strong conceptual skills to envision the organization’s future direction, set goals, and formulate strategic plans.

• Technical skill: Refers to specific knowledge and expertise in a particular field or industry. While technical skills are important for lower levels of management, they become less critical at the top level where managers focus more on overseeing and directing rather than performing technical tasks.
• Human skill: Also known as interpersonal or people skills, human skills involve the ability to work effectively with others, motivate and lead teams, and build relationships. These skills are important at all levels of management but are particularly crucial for middle managers who directly supervise employees.
• Administrative skill: Involves the ability to manage tasks, processes, and resources efficiently. It includes planning, organizing, coordinating, and controlling activities within the organization. Administrative skills are essential for all levels of management but are typically more operational in nature compared to conceptual skills.', '["conceptual","technical","human","administrative"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T13:37:04.046Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:37:04.046Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:37:04.046Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756217430330-32', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Type of organization applicable to a growing organization, with diversified responsibilities, in need of coordinators and specialists to assist.', 'line and staff type', 'Line and staff type of organization combines elements of both line and staff functions. In addition to the direct line of authority (line functions), it includes specialized support and advisory roles (staff functions) such as specialists, coordinators, and support staff to assist the line managers.

• Line type: In a line organization, authority flows in a direct line from top to bottom, with each employee reporting to one supervisor. It is suitable for small organizations with simple structures and clear chains of command.
• Functional type: This refers to organizations where employees are grouped by their specialty areas or functions (e.g., marketing, finance, operations). It is common in larger organizations where efficiency and specialization are key.
• Line and functional type: This is not a standard organizational type. It may refer to a hybrid structure that combines line functions with functional departments.', '["line type","line and staff type","functional type","line and functional type"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T13:06:45.563Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:06:45.563Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:06:45.563Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756217349567-31', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'A parasitic worm that cause trichinellosis when raw or undercooked meat containing encysted larvae is consumed.', 'trichinella spiralis', '• Campylobacter jejuni: A bacterium commonly associated with foodborne illness from consumption of contaminated poultry, unpasteurized milk, and contaminated water.
• E. coli: A bacteria that naturally resides in the intestines of humans and animals. While most strains of E. coli are harmless, certain pathogenic strains, such as E. coli O157:H7, can cause foodborne illness when ingested through contaminated food or water. Fecal contamination of food or water sources can introduce these harmful strains, leading to outbreaks of foodborne illnesses.
• Bacillus cereus: A bacterium that can cause food poisoning through the production of toxins in improperly stored or cooked foods, particularly rice and other starchy foods.', '["campylobacter jejuni","e. coli","bacillus cereus","trichinella spiralis"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T13:46:45.173Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:46:45.173Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:46:45.173Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756220350560-72', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Desirable characteristic of fish:', 'Crystal clear eyes; bright colored gills; whole fins; resilient flesh', 'The desirable characteristics of fresh fish are typically indicated by:

• Crystal clear eyes
• Bright colored (red) gills
• Whole and intact fins
• Resilient and firm flesh', '["Crystal clear eyes; bright colored gills; whole fins; resilient flesh","Sunken eyes; fishy smell; slimy gills; dry fins","Moist eyes; dark colored gills; fresh smell; remains indented when poked","all of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T13:55:27.074Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:55:27.074Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:55:27.074Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756217314869-30', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'A bacterium that can cause food poisoning through the production of toxins in improperly stored cooked foods, particularly rice and starchy foods.', 'bacillus cereus', 'Bacillus cereus is a spore-forming bacterium famously associated with "fried rice syndrome." Its heat-resistant spores can survive the initial cooking process of rice or other starchy foods.

If cooked food is left at room temperature (the temperature danger zone) or improperly stored, these spores germinate, multiply, and produce dangerous toxins.

The emetic (vomiting) toxin produced by Bacillus cereus is highly heat-stable, meaning that even reheating the food thoroughly will not destroy the toxin once it has formed.', '["campylobacter jejuni","e. coli","bacillus cereus","trichinella spiralis"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T13:14:42.220Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:14:42.220Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:14:42.220Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756217213139-29', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'A bacterium commonly associated with foodborne illness from consumption of contaminated poultry, unpasteurized milk and contaminated water.', 'campylobacter jejuni', '• E. coli: A bacteria that naturally resides in the intestines of humans and animals. While most strains of E. coli are harmless, certain pathogenic strains, such as E. coli O157:H7, can cause foodborne illness when ingested through contaminated food or water. Fecal contamination of food or water sources can introduce these harmful strains, leading to outbreaks of foodborne illnesses.
• Bacillus cereus: A bacterium that can cause food poisoning through the production of toxins in improperly stored or cooked foods, particularly rice and other starchy foods.
• Trichinella spiralis: A parasitic worm that causes trichinellosis (trichinosis) when raw or undercooked meat containing encysted larvae is consumed.', '["campylobacter jejuni","e. coli","bacillus cereus","trichinella spiralis"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T13:47:28.511Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:47:28.511Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:47:28.585Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756217160742-28', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Microorganism commonly associated with fecal contamination:', 'e. coli', 'E. coli is a type of bacteria that naturally resides in the intestines of humans and animals. While most strains of E. coli are harmless, certain pathogenic strains, such as E. coli O157:H7, can cause foodborne illness when ingested through contaminated food or water. Fecal contamination of food or water sources can introduce these harmful strains, leading to outbreaks of foodborne illnesses.

• Campylobacter jejuni: A bacterium commonly associated with foodborne illness from consumption of contaminated poultry, unpasteurized milk, and contaminated water.
• Bacillus cereus: A bacterium that can cause food poisoning through the production of toxins in improperly stored or cooked foods, particularly rice and other starchy foods.
• Trichinella spiralis: A parasitic worm that causes trichinellosis (trichinosis) when raw or undercooked meat containing encysted larvae is consumed.', '["campylobacter jejuni","e. coli","bacillus cereus","trichinella spiralis"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T13:12:21.942Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:12:21.942Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:12:21.942Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756217031598-27', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'The flavor and aroma of fruits and vegetables are due to:', 'volatile acids', 'Volatile compounds are organic molecules that can evaporate at room temperature, contributing to the characteristic aroma and flavor of fruits and vegetables.

While pigments, organic acids, and sulfur compounds can also influence the taste and aroma of fruits and vegetables to some extent, volatile compounds play a central role in determining their characteristic flavors and aromas.', '["pigments","organic acids","volatile acids","sulfur compounds"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T13:34:19.111Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:34:19.111Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:34:19.111Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756216915154-26', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Sugar dissolved in water to form a syrup is a:', 'true solution', 'In a true solution, the solute (sugar) is completely dissolved and evenly distributed in the solvent (water) at a molecular level. The sugar molecules become dispersed throughout the water, forming a homogeneous mixture where the sugar molecules are not visible to the naked eye and do not settle out over time.

• Mixture: A combination of substances that are physically combined but not chemically bonded.
• Suspension: A mixture in which particles of a substance are dispersed throughout a liquid but are large enough to settle out over time. This does not describe sugar dissolved in water.
• Colloidal dispersion: A mixture in which particles of one substance are dispersed throughout another substance at the molecular or microscopic level. Sugar dissolved in water does not form a colloidal dispersion because the sugar molecules are dissolved at the molecular level.', '["mixture","true solution","suspension","colloidal dispersion"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T12:56:57.027Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T12:56:57.027Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T12:56:57.027Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756216873288-25', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Example of fixed cost:', 'salaries of the managers', 'A fixed cost is a cost that remains constant regardless of the level of production or sales. Salaries of the managers are typically a fixed cost because managers’ salaries are usually set amounts that do not vary based on the number of customers served or meals prepared.

• Wages of waiters and service personnel: This is generally a variable cost because it can fluctuate with the level of service provided, such as the number of customers served or hours worked.
• Wages of kitchen and dining staff: Similar to waiters and service personnel, wages for kitchen and dining staff can vary based on the level of activity in the restaurant.

Therefore, the correct answer among the options provided is salaries of the managers. Fixed costs remain constant over a specific period regardless of production or sales levels.', '["wages of waiters and service personnel","salaries of the managers","wages of kitchen and dining staff","all of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:04:55.459Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:04:55.459Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:04:55.459Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756220265387-71', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'What do you call it when fruits continue to ripen after harvesting (such as bananas):', 'Climacteric', 'Climacteric fruits are capable of undergoing a ripening process even after being harvested. Bananas are a classic example of climacteric fruits; they are typically harvested while still green and then ripen further during storage due to the production of ethylene gas.', '["Unripe","Artificial ripening process","Degree of maturity","Climacteric"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:00:26.211Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:00:26.211Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:00:26.211Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756216821544-24', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'A dark ale with heavy foam, bitter flavor and lighter body.', 'Porter ale', 'Stout is a type of dark beer known for its rich, roasted malt flavors, which can include notes of coffee, chocolate, and caramel. It often has a creamy, thick foam due to the use of nitrogen or high carbonation levels. Stouts can vary in bitterness, but many varieties have a notable bitterness from roasted malts and hops.

A Porter is also a dark beer similar to Stout but typically lighter in body and with a slightly different malt profile. Both Stouts and Porters can exhibit similar characteristics, but Stouts are generally associated with a heavier body and more pronounced bitterness.', '["Stout ale","Porter ale","Lager beer","Bock beer"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:15:41.370Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:15:41.370Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:15:41.370Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756216781127-23', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Callos is usually made from:', 'Tripe', 'Callos is a classic Spanish-influenced Filipino stew whose primary and defining ingredient is beef tripe (ox tripe). The dish features tenderized tripe, often slow-cooked or pressure-cooked along with ox feet, chorizo de Bilbao, garbanzo beans, and bell peppers in a rich, savory, paprika-infused tomato sauce.', '["Liempo","Tenderloin","Tripe","Brisket"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:16:33.873Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:16:33.873Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:16:33.873Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756216753960-22', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Coriander is also:', 'all of the above', 'In culinary terms, “coriander” refers to the seeds of the coriander plant, which are used as a spice. On the other hand, “cilantro” refers to the leaves and stems of the same plant, which are used as an herb in cooking. Both coriander (seeds) and cilantro (leaves/stems) come from the Coriandrum sativum plant.

Wansoy is the Filipino term for cilantro, specifically referring to the leaves and stems of the coriander plant.

Therefore, the correct answer is all of the above: coriander, cilantro, and wansoy all refer to different parts of the same plant, Coriandrum sativum.', '["cilantro","wansoy","all of the above","none of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T13:51:54.568Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:51:54.568Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:51:54.568Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756216727546-21', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Hygroscopicity is property associated with:', 'sugar', 'Hygroscopicity refers to the ability of a substance to absorb moisture from the air. Sugars, such as sucrose, glucose, and fructose, are known to be hygroscopic, meaning they readily attract and hold water molecules from their surroundings. This property can affect the texture and stability of foods, especially in baked goods and confections.

Water itself is not hygroscopic since it is the substance that other materials absorb. Oils are generally non-hygroscopic.', '["water","sugar","oils","none of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:15:57.492Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:15:57.492Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:15:57.492Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756216685948-20', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'The flour with the highest protein content.', 'bread flour', 'Bread flour is high in protein, usually around 12-14%. The higher protein content contributes to gluten formation, which gives bread its structure and elasticity.

• Cake flour: Cake flour has the lowest protein content, around 7-9%. It is finely milled and has a lower protein content to produce tender cakes with a finer crumb.
• Pastry flour: Pastry flour has a moderate protein content, typically around 9-10%. It strikes a balance between bread flour and cake flour, suitable for making pastries and some breads that require a tender texture.
• All-purpose flour: All-purpose flour is a blend of hard and soft wheat flours, usually containing around 10-12% protein. It can be used for a variety of baking purposes, though it is not as high in protein as bread flour.', '["pastry flour","cake flour","bread flour","all purpose flour"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:15:44.221Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:15:44.221Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:15:44.221Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756216645550-19', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'An act to strengthen the food safery regulatory system in the country:', 'RA 10611', 'RA 10611, also known as the “Food Safety Act of 2013,” aims to protect public health and ensure food safety by providing the legal framework for the regulation, inspection, and monitoring of food products in the Philippines. It consolidates and harmonizes food safety standards and practices, covering the entire food chain from production to consumption.

• PD 856: Presidential Decree No. 856, also known as the “Code on Sanitation of the Philippines,” which covers general sanitation practices including those related to food. 
• EO 51: Executive Order No. 51, which regulates the retail price of certain basic necessities and prime commodities.
• RA 3720: Republic Act No. 3720, also known as the “Food, Drugs, Devices and Cosmetics Act,” which regulates food, drugs, devices, and cosmetics but has been superseded by RA 9711 and RA 10611 in terms of food safety provisions.', '["PD 856","EO 51","RA 3720","RA 10611"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:17:53.015Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:17:53.015Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:17:53.015Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756216601935-18', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'The following wine producing countries are considered to be "old world" wine regions EXCEPT:', 'Argentina', 'The term “Old World” in wine terminology generally refers to wine-producing regions that have a long history of winemaking tradition and are located in Europe. The countries typically included in the Old World wine regions are:
• France
• Italy
• Germany
These countries have deep-rooted histories in winemaking and are known for their traditional wine styles and techniques.

Argentina, on the other hand, is considered a “New World” wine region. The New World refers to wine-producing regions outside of Europe, which have developed their wine industries more recently and often have different winemaking styles and practices compared to the Old World.', '["France","Italy","Germany","Argentina"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T13:15:41.172Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:15:41.172Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:15:41.172Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756216557621-17', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Produced by fermentation involving lactic acid bacteria.', 'yogurt', 'Yogurt is made by fermenting milk with lactic acid bacteria, such as Lactobacillus bulgaricus and Streptococcus thermophilus, which convert lactose (milk sugar) into lactic acid, giving yogurt its tangy flavor.

• Vinegar: Produced by the fermentation of ethanol (alcohol) into acetic acid by acetic acid bacteria, not lactic acid bacteria.
• Coffee: Not produced by lactic acid fermentation. While some lactic acid bacteria may be involved during the fermentation process of coffee beans, the final product is not a result of lactic acid fermentation.
• Beer: Produced by the fermentation of sugars by yeast (Saccharomyces cerevisiae) into alcohol and carbon dioxide. Lactic acid bacteria are not typically involved in the main fermentation process, although they can be involved in sour beers.', '["vinegar","yogurt","coffee","beer"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T13:42:19.056Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:42:19.056Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:42:19.056Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756216507340-16', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Addition of salt or sugar to a liquid will affect its boiling point by:', 'increasing boiling point', 'When a non-volatile solute (such as salt or sugar) is dissolved in a solvent (such as water), it disrupts the formation of solvent molecules at the surface, which are responsible for vapor pressure and boiling.

The presence of the solute lowers the vapor pressure of the solvent. According to Raoult’s Law, the boiling point of a solution is higher than that of the pure solvent, depending on the concentration of the solute.

Therefore, adding salt or sugar to a liquid (such as water) will increase its boiling point compared to pure water.', '["increasing boiling point","decreasing boiling pint","increase and then decrease boiling point","no effect"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:16:50.038Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:16:50.038Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:16:50.038Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756216452975-15', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Burong Talangka is an example of:', 'Fermented product', 'Burong Talangka is a Filipino delicacy made from fermented rice and field crabs (talangka). The fermentation process involves the natural breakdown of carbohydrates by microorganisms (often lactic acid bacteria) present in the rice, which produces acids that help preserve and flavor the crab meat. This fermentation process gives Burong Talangka its distinctive tangy and salty flavor.

While pickled and salted products also undergo preservation processes, Burong Talangka specifically relies on fermentation to achieve its characteristic taste and texture. Therefore, the correct answer is fermented product.

• Pickling vs. Fermentation: Pickling typically involves immersing food in an acidic solution (like vinegar) to preserve it, which is different from the natural fermentation process that occurs in Burong Talangka. While pickling can also involve brine (saltwater), it does not involve the same microbial activity that defines fermentation.
• Salted Product: While salt is a key ingredient in Burong Talangka, the product is not merely salted; the primary preservation and flavor development come from fermentation, not just the salting process.', '["Pickled product","Salted product","Fermented product","All of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T13:18:21.509Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:18:21.509Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:18:21.509Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756216408777-14', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Ropiness refers particularly to spoilage of bread characterized by:', 'formation of viscous, sticky material like slime', 'Ropiness refers particularly to spoilage of bread characterized by the formation of a viscous, sticky material like slime. This condition occurs due to microbial activity, typically from certain bacteria, Bacillus subtilis, that produce polysaccharides or exopolysaccharides that give the bread a slimy or rope-like texture. It is considered a form of spoilage that renders the bread unappealing and potentially unsafe to consume.

• Retrogradation: This is the process where starch molecules, particularly amylose and amylopectin, re-associate and crystallize after gelatinization, leading to the firming of bread over time. It’s one of the main causes of bread staling, making the bread crumb harder and less palatable.
• Staling: This refers to the overall process of bread becoming stale, which includes retrogradation, moisture loss, and changes in texture. Staling makes bread crumb dry, crumbly, and less flavorful.
• Drying: This occurs as bread loses moisture over time, contributing to the staling process. The bread becomes harder and less soft, affecting its texture and palatability.', '["formation of viscous, sticky material like slime","drying","staling","retrogradation"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T13:54:50.392Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:54:50.392Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:54:50.392Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756216286500-13', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'The following are equipment used in sensory evaluation of food, EXCEPT:', 'none of the above', '• Viscosimeter: Measures the viscosity or thickness of liquids, which can be relevant in sensory evaluation, especially for texture assessment.
• Refractometer: Measures the refractive index of liquids, which is useful for assessing sugar content (Brix) in beverages and fruits, influencing taste perception.
• Salometer: Measures the salinity or salt concentration in a solution, which can affect taste perception in salty foods.

Based on these descriptions, all three instruments (viscosimeter, refractometer, and salometer) are potentially relevant in sensory evaluation depending on the specific attributes being assessed.

Therefore, the correct answer is none of the above because all of the listed instruments can be used in sensory evaluation of food, depending on the specific needs of the evaluation.', '["viscosimeter","refractometer","salometer","none of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:10:36.762Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:10:36.762Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:10:36.762Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756216236252-12', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'A device used in plumbing systems to intercept grease and solids before they enter wastewater disposal systems.', 'grease trap', '• Exhaust: Refers to the system that removes air, heat, and odors from a space, often connected to the hood in commercial kitchens.
• Hood: The main device positioned over cooking equipment to capture and remove heat, smoke, steam, and grease vapors.
• Salamander: A type of broiler typically used in commercial kitchens to apply intense heat from above for browning or finishing dishes.', '["exhaust","hood","grease trap","salamander"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T13:56:32.536Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:56:32.536Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:56:32.536Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756216198670-11', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Refers to the system that removes air, heat, and odors from a space.', 'exhaust', '', '["exhaust","hood","grease trap","salamander"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:10:42.751Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:10:42.751Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:10:42.751Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756216136023-10', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'A device for collecting heat, smoke, steam, and grease vapors.', 'hood', 'A hood is the main device positioned over cooking equipment to capture and remove heat, smoke, steam, and grease vapors.

• Exhaust: Refers to the system that removes air, heat, and odors from a space, often connected to the hood in commercial kitchens.
• Grease trap: A device used in plumbing systems to intercept grease and solids before they enter wastewater disposal systems.
• Salamander: A type of broiler typically used in commercial kitchens to apply intense heat from above for browning or finishing dishes.', '["exhaust","hood","grease trap","salamander"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T13:59:11.507Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:59:11.507Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:59:11.507Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756216049327-9', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Which of the following is not one of the interlocking and interrelated roles of managers?', 'Organizational', 'Henry Mintzberg, a management theorist, categorized managerial roles into three main categories:

• Interpersonal roles: Roles that involve interactions with other people, including figurehead, leader, and liaison roles.
• Informational roles: Roles that involve receiving, collecting, and disseminating information, including monitor, disseminator, and spokesperson roles.
• Decisional roles: Roles that involve making decisions to solve problems or take advantage of opportunities, including entrepreneur, disturbance handler, resource allocator, and negotiator roles.

“Organizational” does not fit into any of these categories directly as described by Mintzberg. Therefore, Organizational is not one of the interlocking and interrelated roles of managers according to this framework.', '["Informational","Interpersonal","Organizational","Decisional"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:17:36.728Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:17:36.728Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:17:36.728Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756215988680-8', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Level in which the stock on hand is depleted before additional orders are place.', 'Reorder point', 'Reorder point refers to the inventory level at which a new order should be placed to replenish stock before it runs out.

• Par stock: The quantity of an item that should be kept in stock to meet immediate needs.
• Maximum level: The highest level of inventory that should be maintained to avoid excessive holding costs.', '["Par stock","Reorder point","Maximum level","Both a and b"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T13:39:58.433Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:39:58.433Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:39:58.433Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756215919467-7', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'When moisture removal is achieved by utilizing a chamber where heat and humidity are controlled, the process is known as:', 'dehydration', 'Dehydration involves removing moisture from food products using controlled conditions of temperature and humidity. This process helps to preserve the food by inhibiting the growth of microorganisms that require moisture to thrive.

• Freeze-drying is a different preservation method that involves freezing the food and then subjecting it to a vacuum to remove ice crystals directly as vapor (sublimation). 
• Sun-drying involves drying food products using the heat of the sun, while candying involves preserving fruit or peel by coating it with sugar syrup.

Therefore, the correct term for controlled moisture removal in a chamber is dehydration.', '["freeze-drying","dehydration","sun-drying","candying"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:15:52.316Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:15:52.316Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:15:52.316Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756215862553-6', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'A potential carcinogen on charcoal-broiled meat is', 'benzopyrene', 'The potential carcinogen formed on charcoal-broiled meat is benzopyrene. Benzopyrene is a type of polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbon (PAH) that forms when meat, especially fatty meat, is cooked at high temperatures such as grilling or broiling over charcoal or open flame. PAHs like benzopyrene are known to be carcinogenic and can pose health risks when consumed in significant quantities over time.

• Aflatoxin is a different type of carcinogen produced by certain molds on food, particularly nuts and grains, under certain conditions.
• Nitrosamines can form in certain preserved or processed meats, but they are not specifically associated with charcoal-broiled meats. Therefore, the correct answer to the question is benzopyrene.', '["aflatoxin","nitrosamines","benzopyrene","none of the above"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:18:07.097Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:18:07.097Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:18:07.097Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756215809589-5', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'The emulsifying agent in egg yolk.', 'Lecithin', 'The emulsifying agent in egg yolk is lecithin. Lecithin is a phospholipid present in egg yolk that helps stabilize emulsions by reducing the surface tension between immiscible liquids, such as oil and water. It allows for the formation and maintenance of a stable emulsion, such as in mayonnaise or hollandaise sauce, where oil and water are combined into a smooth, creamy mixture.

• Ovomucin: This is a glycoprotein found in egg whites. It contributes to the gel-like consistency of egg whites and has properties that help stabilize foams. It also plays a role in the structural integrity of the egg white.
• Albumin: Albumin is a major protein found in egg whites (also known as egg albumen) and is responsible for the egg white’s ability to form foams and stabilize mixtures. It also helps in binding and thickening in various food preparations.
• Lysozyme: Lysozyme is an enzyme found in egg whites and other bodily fluids. It has antimicrobial properties and can break down bacterial cell walls, contributing to the preservation and safety of the egg.', '["Ovomucin","Albumin","Lysozyme","Lecithin"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T13:27:53.863Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:27:53.863Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:27:53.863Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756215761859-4', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'This technique involves coating food, usually meat or fish with a dry ingredient like flour, breadcrumbs, or cornmeal before cooking. It helps create a crispy exterior when the food is fried or baked.', 'Dredging', '', '["Reduction","Concasse","Deglazing","Dredging"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:08:09.000Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:08:09.000Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:08:09.000Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756215704259-3', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'This process involves adding liquid to a pan after sauteing or searing meat to loosen and dissolve the browned bits of food stuck to the bottom. The resulting mixture can be used as a base for sauces.', 'Deglazing', '• Dredging: This technique involves coating food, usually meat or fish, with a dry ingredient like flour, breadcrumbs, or cornmeal before cooking. Dredging helps create a crispy exterior when the food is fried or baked.
• Reduction: This involves simmering or boiling a liquid (such as stock, wine, or sauce) to evaporate water and concentrate the flavors. This process thickens the liquid and intensifies its taste, resulting in a richer sauce or liquid base for dishes.
• Concasse: This term refers to a method of preparing tomatoes by blanching, peeling, and chopping them into small pieces. The technique is often used to create a base for sauces or as a fresh ingredient in various dishes.', '["Reduction","Concasse","Deglazing","Dredging"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:15:36.967Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:15:36.967Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:15:36.967Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756215633383-2', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'This term refers to a method of preparing tomatoes by blanching, peeling, and chopping them into small pieces. The technique is often used to creast a base for sauces or as a fresh ingredient in various dishes.', 'Concasse', '', '["Reduction","Concasse","Deglazing","Dredging"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:13:13.359Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:13:13.359Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:13:13.359Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756215565734-1', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'It is a culinary term which means to allow the evaporation of a liquid for a more concentrated sauce.', 'Reduction', 'Reduction involves simmering or boiling a liquid (such as stock, wine, or sauce) to evaporate water and concentrate the flavors. This process thickens the liquid and intensifies its taste, resulting in a richer sauce or liquid base for dishes.

• Concasse: This term refers to a method of preparing tomatoes by blanching, peeling, and chopping them into small pieces. The technique is often used to create a base for sauces or as a fresh ingredient in various dishes.
• Deglazing: This process involves adding liquid (like wine, broth, or vinegar) to a pan after sautéing or searing meat to loosen and dissolve the browned bits of food (Fond) stuck to the bottom. The resulting mixture can be used as a base for sauces.

*Fond, the browned bits left on the bottom of a pan after cooking, is not typically carcinogenic. It forms from the Maillard reaction, a process where proteins and sugars in food brown and develop complex flavors. However, it’s important to distinguish fond from burnt food. If food is burned to the point of charring, it can produce potentially harmful compounds, including some that are carcinogenic, like acrylamide and polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbons (PAHs). As long as the fond is browned and not charred, it is generally safe and adds flavor to dishes.

• Dredging: This technique involves coating food, usually meat or fish, with a dry ingredient like flour, breadcrumbs, or cornmeal before cooking. Dredging helps create a crispy exterior when the food is fried or baked.', '["Reduction","Concasse","Deglazing","Dredging"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:17:07.090Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:17:07.090Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:17:07.090Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756221141873-85', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'In cooking fibrous fruits like langka or beans in sugar syrup, tough product is obtained if:', 'sugar is added too early', 'Adding sugar too early in the cooking process can toughen fibrous fruits because it can cause the cell walls of the fruit to harden before they have a chance to soften sufficiently. This can lead to a chewy or tough texture instead of the desired tender consistency.

• Adding sugar too late might result in a less integrated flavor or less effective syrup concentration but generally doesn’t cause toughness. The texture issues are more related to when the sugar is added relative to the cooking time.
• Brown sugar can add a different flavor and color due to the presence of molasses, but it doesn’t usually make the product tougher. The toughness is more influenced by the timing of sugar addition.
• Stirring the syrup while cooking is generally done to ensure even cooking and to prevent burning.', '["sugar is added too early","sugar is added too late","brown sugar is used","the syrup is stirred while cooking"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T13:00:51.372Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:00:51.372Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:00:51.372Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756221051544-84', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Sliminess and color changes are signs of spoilage due to:', 'bacterial growth', 'Bacterial growth on food can lead to changes in texture (such as sliminess) and color (such as discoloration or darkening). These changes occur as bacteria break down proteins and fats in the food, producing substances that alter its appearance and texture.

• Mold growth: Typically results in visible fuzzy or powdery patches on food, which can be various colors like green, blue, or white. Molds can cause spoilage but are less commonly associated with sliminess compared to bacteria.
• Yeast growth: Can lead to spoilage, especially in sugary or acidic foods, causing fermentation and off-flavors. Yeasts are less likely to cause sliminess but can contribute to changes in texture and appearance.
• Oxidative changes: Chemical reactions involving oxygen that can lead to rancidity, discoloration, and off-flavors, particularly in fats and oils. These changes are not typically associated with sliminess but with color changes.', '["bacterial growth","mold growth","yeast growth","oxidative changes"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:12:17.797Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:12:17.797Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:12:17.797Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756215465308-0', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'A type of dispersion consisting of two immiscible liquids.', 'emulsion', 'A type of dispersion consisting of two immiscible liquids is called an emulsion. In an emulsion, one liquid is dispersed in the form of small droplets throughout another liquid. Common examples include oil-in-water (O/W) and water-in-oil (W/O) emulsions, where the two liquids do not mix completely but are stabilized with the help of emulsifiers to prevent separation.

• Gel: a semi-solid system where a network of polymer chains forms a three-dimensional structure, trapping a liquid within it. Examples include gelatin desserts and certain types of cheese.
• Foam: a collection of gas bubbles dispersed in a liquid or solid. Examples include whipped cream (air in cream) and mousse.
• Suspension: mixture in which solid particles are dispersed in a liquid but not dissolved. The particles in a suspension are typically larger and can settle over time. Examples include salad dressings and some types of sauces.', '["gel","emulsion","foam","suspension"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T13:31:43.422Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:31:43.422Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:31:43.422Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756265644860-86', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'It assumes that employees are self-motivated, enjoy work, and seek responsibility. This theory suggests that workers are motivated by intrinsic factors and can be creative and productive if given the right environment.', 'Theory Y', '', '["Theory X","Scientific Approach","Human Relation Approach","Theory Y"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T13:52:18.893Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:52:18.893Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:52:18.893Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756218144830-45', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'An appetizer made of fried or toasted bread spread with anchovies or other small savory foods is called:', 'Canape', 'Canapés are small pieces of bread or pastry topped with savory garnishes, often served as appetizers.

• Capelletti: Small, stuffed pasta shapes similar to tortellini. They are typically filled with meat or cheese and served in broth or with a sauce.
• Cassata: Traditional Italian dessert made with sponge cake, ricotta cheese, candied fruit, and a layer of marzipan. It is often associated with Sicily.
• Cannelloni: Large pasta tubes that are typically stuffed with a filling such as ricotta cheese and spinach or ground meat. They are then covered in sauce and baked.', '["Capelleti","Cassata","Canape","Cannelloni"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:07:58.715Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:07:58.715Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:07:58.715Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756218247558-46', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Small, stuffed pasta shapes similar to tortellini. They are typically filled with meat or cheese and served in broth or with a sauce.', 'Cappelletti', '• Canapés: Small pieces of bread or pastry topped with savory garnishes, often served as appetizers.
• Cassata: Traditional Italian dessert made with sponge cake, ricotta cheese, candied fruit, and a layer of marzipan. It is often associated with Sicily.
• Cannelloni: Large pasta tubes that are typically stuffed with a filling such as ricotta cheese and spinach or ground meat. They are then covered in sauce and baked.', '["Cappelletti","Cassata","Canape","Cannelloni"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:16:19.296Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:16:19.296Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:16:19.296Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756218324788-47', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'A traditional Italian dessert made with sponge cake, ricotta cheese, candied fruit, and a layer of marzipan. It is often associated with Sicily.', 'Cassata', '• Canapés: Small pieces of bread or pastry topped with savory garnishes, often served as appetizers.
• Capelletti: Capelletti are small, stuffed pasta shapes similar to tortellini. They are typically filled with meat or cheese and served in broth or with a sauce.
• Cannelloni: Cannelloni are large pasta tubes that are typically stuffed with a filling such as ricotta cheese and spinach or ground meat. They are then covered in sauce and baked.', '["Capelleti","Cassata","Canape","Cannelloni"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:17:02.008Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:17:02.008Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:17:02.008Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756218364417-48', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Large pasta tubes are typically stuffed with a filling such as ricotta cheese and spinach or ground meat. They are then covered in sauce and baked.', 'Cannelloni', '', '["Capelleti","Cassata","Canape","Cannelloni"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T14:00:36.615Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:00:36.615Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T14:00:36.615Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756218416451-49', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Vitamin C, Vitamin E, BHT, and BHT and sulfites are all:', 'antioxidants', 'Antioxidants are substances that inhibit oxidation processes, which can lead to the deterioration of food products. They help prevent or slow down the oxidation of fats and oils, thus extending the shelf life of foods. Examples include vitamin C (ascorbic acid), vitamin E (tocopherol), BHA (butylated hydroxyanisole), BHT (butylated hydroxytoluene), and sulfites.

• Flavor enhancers: These substances are added to food to enhance or modify its taste and flavor.
• Antimicrobial agents: These are substances that inhibit or kill microorganisms, helping to preserve food by preventing microbial spoilage or contamination.
• Incidental food additives: These are substances that may be present in food as a result of manufacturing, processing, packaging, or storing, but are not intentionally added.', '["flavor enhancers","antioxidants","antimicrobial agents","incidental food additives"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T13:05:54.898Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:05:54.898Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:05:54.898Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756218466880-50', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'An example of aseptic packaging:', 'tetra pack drinking boxes', 'Aseptic packaging refers to a method of packaging food and beverages in a sterile environment to maintain freshness without the need for refrigeration or additives. Tetra Pak is a well-known brand that produces aseptic packaging solutions, such as drinking boxes for juices, milk, and other beverages. These packages are designed to keep the contents safe from contamination and maintain their quality over an extended period without the need for preservatives or refrigeration until opened.

• Paper bag: Generally used for dry goods and not aseptically packaged.
• Milk carton: While milk cartons can be sealed aseptically, Tetra Pak specifically refers to the brand of aseptic packaging.
• Plastic bread bag: Used for packaging bread and typically not aseptic.', '["tetra pack drinking boxes","paper bag","milk carton","plastic bread bag"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T13:04:21.898Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:04:21.898Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:04:21.898Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756218549445-51', 'anki-deck-1783609369423-1790433139853-3jf91', 'Of the pork cuts, the most tender is:', 'loin', 'The loin is known for being the most tender cut of pork. It comes from the area along the back of the pig and includes cuts such as pork chops and pork tenderloin. This area of the pig does less work, resulting in more tender meat.', '["pork chop","loin","shank","pigue"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-15T13:59:29.113Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:59:29.113Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.891Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-14T13:59:29.113Z"'::jsonb)
