('anki-card-1758530767393-51', 'anki-deck-1783609212880-1790433142620-mxyd7', 'Food cost of Seafood Platter is P 145.00. When sold at P P450, what is the food cost percentage?*', '32.2%', '', '["30.5 %","35%","32.2%","36.5 %"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.930Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758530024246-4', 'anki-deck-1783609212880-1790433142620-mxyd7', 'Which statement is not true about popularity index?*', 'It indicates the need to increase portion size of items served', '', '["It tells us how popular or acceptable a particular entrée is, at a particular period.","It guides us in projecting future sales for a particular entrée.","It signifies a trend in menu selection if the results are recurring.","It indicates the need to increase portion size of items served"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.930Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758530085875-7', 'anki-deck-1783609212880-1790433142620-mxyd7', 'To prepare 50 portions of a standard recipe for 12 portions, how do I compute for scaling factor? *', 'Divide desired yield by the original yield', '', '["Divide desired yield by the original yield","Multiply desired yield by original yield.","Divide original yield by desired yield","Multiply original yield by desired yield"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.930Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758530323999-22', 'anki-deck-1783609212880-1790433142620-mxyd7', 'Which practice helps control labor cost?*', 'Setting productivity standards', '', '["Setting productivity standards","Taking physical inventories","Setting standard portion sizes","Using standard recipes"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.930Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758530341247-23', 'anki-deck-1783609212880-1790433142620-mxyd7', 'Standard portion sizes helps managers control food _________.*', 'quantity', '', '["quality","quantity","inventory records","issuing"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.930Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758530365596-24', 'anki-deck-1783609212880-1790433142620-mxyd7', 'A restaurant served 87 guests and made P 18, 705 sales. Average check per guest was______.*', 'P 215', 'In foodservice management and financial accounting, the average check (also termed cover average) measures the mean spending per customer. The standard mathematical formula is: Average Check = Total Sales Revenue / Total Number of Guests (Covers). Substituting the problem''s values: P 18,705 / 87 guests = P 215. This financial control metric allows managers to evaluate menu pricing efficiency, sales performance, and guest spending patterns.', '["P 250","P 215","P 205","P 217"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-30T08:57:11.842Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:57:11.842Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.930Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:57:11.842Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758530378596-25', 'anki-deck-1783609212880-1790433142620-mxyd7', 'To make a profit, total restaurant expenses must be less than _____ percent of its sales.*', '100%', '', '["50%","75%","90%","100%"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.930Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758530397279-26', 'anki-deck-1783609212880-1790433142620-mxyd7', 'If 43.5% of restaurant sales is needed to cover its variable costs, the remaining 56.5% is available to meet fixed costs and provide profits . The 56.5 % figure is called*', 'contribution margin', '', '["contribution rate","contribution margin","break-even point","variable rate"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.930Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758530410295-27', 'anki-deck-1783609212880-1790433142620-mxyd7', 'Standard purchase specifications describes what kind of standard?*', 'Quality', '', '["Quality","Quantity","Cost","Procedures"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.930Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758530429927-28', 'anki-deck-1783609212880-1790433142620-mxyd7', 'A restaurant had 3 cases tomatoes (12 cans/case) at start of the month and used up 1 1/2 cases. How many cans must be purchased this month to bring the inventory back to the same starting level?*', '18', '', '["12","18","24","36"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.930Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758530451310-29', 'anki-deck-1783609212880-1790433142620-mxyd7', 'The normal quantity of a stored item required in a given operating period plus a safety factor for possible delay in delivery and for unexpected requirements, is called_______.*', 'par stock', '', '["reorder point","balance on hand","par stock","perpetual inventory"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.930Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758530466091-30', 'anki-deck-1783609212880-1790433142620-mxyd7', 'Centralized purchasing is most appropriate for which type of operation?*', 'Chain restaurant', '', '["School cafeteria","Food stall","Coffee shop","Chain restaurant"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.930Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758530562304-37', 'anki-deck-1783609212880-1790433142620-mxyd7', 'First-in-first- out (FIFO) is a method of*', 'rotating stock', '', '["receiving deliveries","ordering food","rotating stock","maintaining storeroom security"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.930Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758530575118-38', 'anki-deck-1783609212880-1790433142620-mxyd7', 'Which of the following documents is used when issuing inventory supplies?*', 'Requisition', '', '["Purchase order","Purchase specifications","Requisition","invoice"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.930Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758530597370-39', 'anki-deck-1783609212880-1790433142620-mxyd7', 'If the portion size for Saba in Syrup is one piece whole banana, the portion is quantified by*', 'count', '', '["size","weight","count","invoice"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.930Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758530728345-48', 'anki-deck-1783609212880-1790433142620-mxyd7', 'To compute for cost of food sold, add purchases to opening inventory, and subtract ____.*', 'closing inventory', '', '["closing inventory","stores","directs","requisitions"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.930Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
