('anki-card-1756879459292-24', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Why are duck eggs generally preferred over chicken eggs for salt curing, such as in the preparation of salted eggs?', 'Because duck eggs have a higher fat content in the yolk, resulting in a richer texture and flavor after curing.', '', '["Because duck eggs have a thicker shell that absorbs salt faster.","Because duck eggs have a higher fat content in the yolk, resulting in a richer texture and flavor after curing.","Because duck eggs are smaller and cure more evenly in brine solutions.","Because duck eggs contain less water, allowing the salt to concentrate better in the yolk."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756879475459-25', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Why does overheating eggs beyond 70°C typically result in a tough and rubbery texture?', 'Because the egg proteins coagulate excessively, squeezing out water and forming a tight network.', '', '["Because the yolk fats evaporate, leaving behind only dense proteins.","Because the egg proteins coagulate excessively, squeezing out water and forming a tight network.","Because the sugar in the egg caramelizes, hardening the mixture.","Because the egg white becomes diluted at high temperatures, making it less flexible."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756879992684-49', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Which of the following functional properties of starch is most responsible for the firming of custards and pie fillings after cooling?', 'Retrogradation', '', '["Viscosity","Gelatinization","Retrogradation","Gel formation"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756879492275-26', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'In baked goods such as cakes and custards, how do eggs function as structural and textural agents?', 'Eggs coagulate during heating, helping form structure and a tender, fluffy texture.', '', '["Eggs contribute moisture only and do not affect texture or structure.","Eggs prevent browning, keeping the product pale and soft.","Eggs break down starches, making the product denser and chewier.","Eggs coagulate during heating, helping form structure and a tender, fluffy texture."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756879516657-27', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Why are eggs considered excellent emulsifying agents in food preparation such as in mayonnaise or cake batters?', 'Because the whole egg forms foams that naturally keep mixtures stable.', '', '["Because egg whites contain proteins that prevent oil and water from separating.","Because egg yolks contain lecithin, which stabilizes emulsions by binding fat and water.","Because eggs are high in fat, which dissolves both oil and water easily.","Because the whole egg forms foams that naturally keep mixtures stable."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756879541906-28', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Why do eggs whip better at room temperature compared to when they are taken directly from the refrigerator?', 'Because the proteins in room temperature eggs unfold more easily, allowing better foam structure.', '', '["Because room temperature eggs contain more air, which helps in foam formation.","Because the proteins in room temperature eggs unfold more easily, allowing better foam structure.","Because refrigeration adds water to the eggs, diluting the proteins needed for foaming.","Because warm eggs are heavier and create more stable peaks when beaten."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756879560938-29', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'What is the effect of adding an acid, such as cream of tartar or lemon juice, early in the whipping of egg whites?', 'It delays foaming but produces a more stable foam by strengthening protein structure.', '', '["It delays foaming but produces a more stable foam by strengthening protein structure.","It immediately increases foam volume but causes the foam to collapse quickly.","It prevents the egg whites from incorporating air, making whipping ineffective.","It reacts with egg white sugars to form a stiff, dry foam."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756879575903-30', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Why do eggs demonstrate excellent binding capacity in recipes such as meatballs, croquettes, or batters?', 'Because egg proteins coagulate when heated, holding ingredients in a firm structure.', '', '["Because egg yolks are high in fat, which glues ingredients together.","Because egg whites contain starch that thickens and binds ingredients.","Because eggs contain sugar that caramelizes and locks ingredients in place.","Because egg proteins coagulate when heated, holding ingredients in a firm structure."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756879593020-31', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Why does evaporated milk whip better when chilled?', 'Fat solidifies, increasing viscosity', '', '["Water evaporates faster","Fat solidifies, increasing viscosity","Protein denaturation occurs","Sugar crystallizes"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756879617985-32', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'What is the main difference between yogurt and buttermilk?', 'Yogurt uses whole or skim milk; buttermilk uses skim milk', '', '["Yogurt is fermented; buttermilk is not","Buttermilk has more sugar","Yogurt uses whole or skim milk; buttermilk uses skim milk","Yogurt contains more water"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756880723734-88', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Why does deep-frying cook food faster than baking at the same temperature (e.g., 180°C or 350°F)?', 'Oil has a higher heat transfer coefficient than air', '', '["Oil conducts heat more slowly than air","Oil radiates heat more intensely than air","Oil has a higher heat transfer coefficient than air","Air circulates more efficiently than oil"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756880691187-86', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'A recipe calls for 2 liters of broth. You only have a standard US measuring cup on hand. Approximately how many full cups will you need to measure out 2 liters of broth?', '9 cups', '', '["6 cups","8 cups","9 cups","12 cups"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756880677868-85', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Which seasoning would be most appropriate to reduce bitterness in a vegetable stir-fry without masking the natural flavors?', 'Sugar', '', '["Soy sauce","Vinegar","Sugar","Salt"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756880665120-84', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'What is the primary reason clarified butter (drawn butter) is preferred for high-heat cooking like sautéing or frying?', 'It has a higher smoke point due to removed milk solids', '', '["It is less expensive than regular butter","It contains more saturated fat","It has a higher smoke point due to removed milk solids","It is thicker and coats foods better"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756880633339-82', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Why is blanching used before freezing vegetables like broccoli or green beans?', 'To inactivate enzymes that cause spoilage', '', '["To inactivate enzymes that cause spoilage","To cook them halfway before final use","To improve their color by increasing chlorophyll","To reduce their carbohydrate content during long-term storage."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756880617905-81', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'What is the primary functional reason for basting during roasting?', 'It adds moisture and prevents surface drying', '', '["It prevents microbial growth on the surface","It caramelizes sugars for deeper browning","It adds moisture and prevents surface drying","It enhances the speed of protein coagulation"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756880602889-80', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Why is an acid rinse effective in preventing browning of peeled fruits and vegetables?', 'It lowers pH, slowing down enzymatic activity', '', '["It removes surface moisture that causes browning","It inhibits oxygen penetration by tightening cell walls","It lowers pH, slowing down enzymatic activity","It denatures surface proteins preventing browning"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756880582224-79', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Why is salt often used first in marinating meat, even when acidic ingredients like vinegar or citrus juice are also present?', 'It helps seasonings penetrate by breaking down the protein structure', '', '["It enhances sweetness","It tenderizes proteins chemically","It draws moisture out to dehydrate meat","It helps seasonings penetrate by breaking down the protein structure"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756880567459-78', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'You are preparing a dry rub for grilling meat. Which of the following ingredient combinations contributes best to flavor penetration and surface browning?', 'Garlic powder, onion powder, brown sugar', '', '["Garlic powder, onion powder, brown sugar","Salt, black pepper, lemon juice, vinegar","Soy sauce, sesame oil, ginger, honey","Salt, black pepper, lemon juice, olive oil"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
