('anki-card-1756880523378-75', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'What is the classification of tanglad (lemongrass) and siling labuyo (bird’s eye chili)?', 'Tanglad is an herb, and siling labuyo is a spice because of the plant parts used', '', '["Both are herbs because they are from plants and used for flavor","Tanglad is a spice, and siling labuyo is an herb because it is spicy","Tanglad is an herb, and siling labuyo is a spice because of the plant parts used","Both are spices because they are often used in stews and traditional recipes"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756880505744-74', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'A recipe calls for 1 tablespoon of coarse salt, but you only have fine salt. What principle should guide your adjustment?', 'Use less fine salt because it is denser and packs more per spoonful', '', '["Use the same amount, as salt type doesn’t affect salinity","Use more fine salt to match flavor intensity","Use less fine salt because it is denser and packs more per spoonful","Replace it with soy sauce for similar saltiness"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756880481663-73', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Why should a teapot be scalded before brewing tea?', 'To warm the pot and ensure optimal extraction of flavor compounds', '', '["To sterilize the pot for food safety.","To prevent caffeine from reacting with metal.","To warm the pot and ensure optimal extraction of flavor compounds","To dissolve tannins and reduce bitterness."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756880706602-87', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'You are preparing a recipe that requires 1.5 pounds of flour, but your kitchen scale only measures in grams. Approximately how many grams of flour should you use?', '680 grams', '', '["500 grams","680 grams","750 grams","900 grams"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756880464695-72', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'What is the main principle in preparing both tea and coffee?', 'To extract the maximum amount of flavoring substances and minimal bitter tannins.', '', '["To dissolve all components including oils and tannins for full-bodied taste.","To extract the maximum amount of flavoring substances and minimal bitter tannins.","To always use boiling water for a stronger taste.","To add milk and sugar for balanced flavor."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756880447981-71', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Why is cocoa often mixed with sugar before adding to liquids during preparation?', 'To prevent cocoa from forming lumps when mixed with liquid.', '', '["To enhance the sweetness and chocolate flavor.","To prevent cocoa from forming lumps when mixed with liquid.","To reduce the bitterness of cocoa during boiling.","To allow the sugar to caramelize and thicken the drink."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756880388916-70', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'A roaster aims to create a balanced coffee blend that offers rich aroma, moderate acidity, and a slightly stronger caffeine kick without overpowering bitterness. Which blend composition is most appropriate?', '70% Arabica, 30% Robusta', '', '["100% Arabica","70% Arabica, 30% Robusta","50% Arabica, 50% Liberica","100% Robusta"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756880372749-69', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Both coffee and tea are regarded as stimulating beverages. Which of the following best explains the physiological basis for this classification?', 'They contain caffeine, a central nervous system stimulant that enhances alertness and reduces fatigue', '', '["Both contain tannins, which directly stimulate brain activity.","They are brewed from roasted seeds and leaves, which increase metabolism regardless of content.","Their natural sugars provide an immediate energy boost that stimulates the body.","They contain caffeine, a central nervous system stimulant that enhances alertness and reduces fatigue"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756880358035-68', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Why is agitation important during the freezing of ice cream?', 'It incorporates air and promotes the formation of small ice crystals', '', '["It prevents sugar from concentrating","It equalizes salt and ice ratios in the mixture","It incorporates air and promotes the formation of small ice crystals","It raises the temperature inside the freezing can"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756880340084-67', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Which of the following best explains why agar-agar can gel with raw pineapple, while gelatin cannot?', 'Agar-agar is a carbohydrate and is not affected by proteolytic enzymes like bromelin.', '', '["Agar-agar is a protein that resists enzymatic breakdown.","Agar-agar forms gels at higher temperatures than gelatin.","Agar-agar is a carbohydrate and is not affected by proteolytic enzymes like bromelin.","Agar-agar forms clearer gels, making it more stable with pineapple."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756880322637-66', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Which of the following best explains why cold water is essential when preparing pastry dough?', 'It helps keep fat solid, promoting flakiness', '', '["It evaporates quickly, helping in leavening","It activates gluten formation for better structure","It helps keep fat solid, promoting flakiness","It adds moisture for a chewy texture"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756880271439-65', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Which of the following statements best explains why foam cakes are baked in ungreased pans and inverted during cooling?', 'Foam cakes need to cling to the sides of the pan during rising, and inverting prevents collapse while cooling', '', '["Ungreased pans allow even heat distribution and inverting keeps the crust soft.","Greasing the pan adds moisture, and inverting traps steam.","Ungreased pans create a crusty exterior, and inverting enhances flavor.","Foam cakes need to cling to the sides of the pan during rising, and inverting prevents collapse while cooling"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756880255556-64', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Which of the following best describes the correct mixing sequence for preparing a chiffon cake?', 'Beat egg whites with sugar; mix egg yolks, oil, and liquid with dry ingredients; fold in the beaten egg whites.', '', '["Beat egg whites with sugar; mix egg yolks, oil, and liquid with dry ingredients; fold in the beaten egg whites.","Beat egg yolks with sugar; add oil and liquid; beat egg whites separately and mix everything at once.","Mix all dry ingredients; add whole eggs and oil; beat until smooth.","Beat egg whites and yolks together with sugar; add oil and liquid, then stir in dry ingredients."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756880238341-63', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Which mixing method for shortened cakes is best for achieving a tender crumb with fine texture and good volume?', 'Conventional Method – because it incorporates air through creaming and alternates dry and liquid ingredients', '', '["Muffin Method – because it limits gluten development through minimal mixing","One-Bowl Method – because it uses all-purpose flour and mixes all ingredients quickly","Conventional Method – because it incorporates air through creaming and alternates dry and liquid ingredients","Sponge Method – because it separates eggs and beats whites to a foam before folding"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756880221891-62', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Why is the folding method essential in making sponge and angel food cakes?', 'Folding helps retain the air incorporated in beaten egg foams, maintaining cake volume.', '', '["Folding helps retain the air incorporated in beaten egg foams, maintaining cake volume.","Folding reduces fat clumping in the batter.","Folding incorporates more liquid into the batter to improve structure.","Folding dissolves sugar evenly throughout the batter."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756880205109-61', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'In foam cakes like angel or chiffon cake, why is cream of tartar commonly added to beaten egg whites?', 'To stabilize the foam structure during whipping', '', '["To sweeten the batter","To stabilize the foam structure during whipping","To enhance gluten development","To prevent coagulation of egg proteins"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756880190126-60', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Which of the following best explains the purpose of punching down dough after its initial fermentation in bread making?', 'To expel carbon dioxide, redistribute yeast, and develop gluten elasticity', '', '["To kill excess yeast and prevent over-fermentation","To increase the dough’s volume through added air","To enhance crust browning and accelerate proofing","To expel carbon dioxide, redistribute yeast, and develop gluten elasticity"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756880170726-59', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Which of the following best explains why fat is referred to as a "shortening" in flour mixtures?', 'It interrupts gluten formation by coating flour particles.', '', '["It shortens the baking time of products.","It prevents sugar from dissolving quickly.","It enhances the hydration of starch.","It interrupts gluten formation by coating flour particles."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756880155093-58', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Which of the following combinations would most likely result in a dense and poorly risen cake, assuming all other factors are constant?', 'Bread flour, baking soda, no acidic ingredient', '', '["Bread flour, baking soda, no acidic ingredient","Cake flour, baking soda, lemon juice","All-purpose flour, baking powder, milk","All-purpose flour, baking powder, vinegar"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756880137612-57', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'In which scenario will yeast activity be compromised, affecting the leavening process of bread?', 'Using active dry yeast at 42°C', '', '["Using active dry yeast at 42°C","Using compressed yeast stored at 5°C","Using quick-rising yeast at room temperature","Using active dry yeast in water at 25°C"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756880120277-56', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Which of the following combinations would most likely delay gluten development in a flour mixture?', 'All-purpose flour, sugar, fat, and lemon juice', '', '["Bread flour, water, and yeast","Cake flour, water, and salt","All-purpose flour, sugar, fat, and lemon juice","High-protein flour and vigorous kneading"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756880103597-55', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'A cook preparing popovers follows the correct flour-liquid ratio but ends up with flat and soggy results. Which of the following is the most likely factor affecting the product quality?', 'Incorrect oven temperature or improper placement in the oven', '', '["Use of soft wheat flour instead of hard flour","Use of the pastry method instead of the straight dough method","Incorrect oven temperature or improper placement in the oven","Use of stainless steel pans instead of glass pans"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756880083064-54', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'A baker notices that her muffins have developed large tunnels and a tough texture. Which factor most likely caused this issue?', 'Overmixing the batter using the muffin method', '', '["Using soft wheat flour instead of hard wheat flour","Undermixing the batter during preparation","Overmixing the batter using the muffin method","Using cake flour instead of all-purpose flour"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756880067830-53', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Which of the following situations will most likely result in a firmer gel during starch gelatinization?', 'Using milk and eggs with minimal stirring', '', '["Adding sugar and acid before heating","Cooking with direct heat and stirring continuously","Using milk and eggs with minimal stirring","Using low starch concentration and high agitation"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756880033217-51', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Why does continuous stirring during the cooking of starch mixtures lead to a pasty consistency?', 'It breaks down starch granules, releasing more amylose', '', '["It enhances retrogradation","It causes over-gelatinization","It breaks down starch granules, releasing more amylose","It prevents starch swelling"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756880008751-50', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Which of the following best explains why waxy starches are preferred in products requiring freeze-thaw stability (e.g., frozen pie fillings)?', 'They swell less during gelatinization', '', '["They contain high amylose content","They are resistant to syneresis due to high amylopectin","They swell less during gelatinization","They retrograde faster"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756880757350-89', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'In which cooking method does radiation play the dominant role in transferring heat directly to the surface of the food?', 'Broiling', '', '["Simmering","Broiling","Steaming","Braising"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756879971453-48', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Brown rice is considered more nutritious than white rice primarily because:', 'It is milled with only the hull removed, retaining the bran and germ.', '', '["It is a processed cereal.","It contains added nutrients.","It is milled with only the hull removed, retaining the bran and germ.","It is highly milled and polished for easy digestion."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756879956687-47', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Which of the following will result in a fluffy and separate-grained texture when cooking rice?', 'Starting with hot water and using the correct rice-to-water ratio', '', '["Using more water and starting with cold water","Soaking the rice and using hard water","Starting with hot water and using the correct rice-to-water ratio","Stirring rice frequently during cooking"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756879940519-46', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'A student wanted to cook champorado with a thick consistency. She used a 2:1 water-to-rice ratio and added milk and sugar at the beginning of cooking. The final product turned out thick but slightly undercooked. What is the most likely reason for the undercooked texture?', 'Sugar and milk were added too early, delaying gelatinization.', '', '["She used too much water for champorado.","Sugar and milk were added too early, delaying gelatinization.","The rice was over-agitated during cooking.","She should have used cold water instead of hot water."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756879923687-45', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Which of the following rice types is most suitable for sticky desserts such as suman or biko?', 'Waxy rice (malagkit), because it has virtually no amylose and becomes sticky when cooked.', '', '["IR 8, because it has high amylose content and remains separate when cooked.","Milagrosa, because it has intermediate amylose content and a soft texture.","Waxy rice (malagkit), because it has virtually no amylose and becomes sticky when cooked.","Basmati, because it is aromatic and elongates on cooking."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756879906740-44', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'A chef prepares two batches of beef stew—one simmered for 2 hours, and another simmered for only 20 minutes. Based on the effect of cooking duration on flavor, which statement best explains the difference in flavor between the two?', 'The long-cooked stew has deeper flavor because prolonged heat breaks down fat and protein into flavorful compounds.', '', '["The short-cooked stew develops more umami due to faster protein coagulation.","The long-cooked stew has deeper flavor because prolonged heat breaks down fat and protein into flavorful compounds.","The short-cooked stew retains more natural meat flavor due to minimal protein denaturation.","The long-cooked stew loses flavor because the volatile aroma compounds evaporate completely."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756879853874-43', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'The correct classification of a bird that has been slaughtered, bled, defeathered, with head and feet removed is:', 'Dressed', '', '["Whole or Galantina","Dressed","Ready-to-cook","Live"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756879834926-42', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Why are lard, butter, margarine, and suet called shortening?', 'It coats flour particles, limiting gluten formation and "shortening" gluten strands.', '', '["It melts quickly at high temperatures, shortening the cooking time.","It increases the shelf life of baked products.","It coats flour particles, limiting gluten formation and \"shortening\" gluten strands.","It causes baked goods to rise faster by shortening proofing time."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756879817891-41', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Why is butter typically soft at room temperature compared to beef tallow?', 'It is composed of mostly unsaturated fatty acids.', '', '["It contains smaller fat crystals.","It has undergone winterization.","It is composed of mostly unsaturated fatty acids.","It has a high smoke point."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb)
