('anki-card-1756879008500-0', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Why is steaming preferred over boiling for cooking green vegetables when the goal is to maximize nutrient retention?', 'Steaming prevents loss of water-soluble vitamins into the cooking liquid.', '', '["Steaming maintains a higher cooking temperature.","Boiling enhances the flavor through leaching.","Steaming prevents loss of water-soluble vitamins into the cooking liquid.","Boiling preserves more enzymes needed for digestion"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756879033895-1', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'A food technologist is designing a process to minimize enzymatic browning in freshly sliced apples while enhancing flavor and color during baking. Which of the following best explains why applying heat serves this dual purpose?', 'Heat inactivates enzymes responsible for enzymatic browning and initiates Maillard browning, contributing to color and flavor.', '', '["Heat promotes Maillard browning and accelerates the activity of polyphenol oxidase, increasing overall browning.","Heat inactivates enzymes responsible for enzymatic browning and initiates Maillard browning, contributing to color and flavor.","Enzymatic browning occurs at high temperatures, while Maillard browning is prevented by heat due to sugar caramelization.","Heating encourages enzymatic browning through protein denaturation and prevents the Maillard reaction by breaking down amino acids."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
