('anki-card-1756879054795-2', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Which of the following best explains why kneading is essential for proper gluten development in yeast-leavened dough?', 'Kneading aligns gluten strands, forming an elastic network that traps gas.', '', '["Kneading warms the dough, accelerating yeast fermentation.","Kneading introduces more flour, which strengthens the dough.","Kneading aligns gluten strands, forming an elastic network that traps gas.","Kneading dissolves gluten proteins to form a smoother texture."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756879076047-3', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Which of the following best explains why a starch-thickened sauce becomes watery when subjected to excessive heat for a prolonged period?', 'Excessive heat disrupts starch micelles, leading to a breakdown of the gel structure and resulting in a watery consistency.', '', '["Gelatinization causes starch granules to swell and burst, increasing the viscosity of the mixture.","Dextrinization enhances the thickening power of starch by breaking it into smaller chains.","Excessive heat disrupts starch micelles, leading to a breakdown of the gel structure and resulting in a watery consistency.","Higher temperatures always increase the thickening ability of starch due to continuous gelatinization."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756879096026-4', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Why should acidic ingredients like tomato juice or molasses be added only after beans have become tender during cooking?', 'Acids toughen cellulose, delaying softening and prolonging cooking time', '', '["Acids increase the rate of gelatinization, softening beans too quickly","Acids neutralize the beans’ natural flavor and aroma","Acids toughen cellulose, delaying softening and prolonging cooking time","Acids remove pigments that affect color and texture of beans"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756879115026-5', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Why is open kettle cooking recommended when preparing strong-flavored vegetables such as cabbage or radish?', 'It allows sulfur compounds to escape, reducing strong odors and flavors', '', '["It prevents oxidation of nutrients by limiting air exposure","It allows sulfur compounds to escape, reducing strong odors and flavors","It retains more chlorophyll for greener appearance","It speeds up cooking by increasing pressure inside the pot"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756879132791-6', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Why does cooking beans in hard water take longer compared to soft water?', 'Calcium and magnesium ions in hard water form insoluble salts with pectin, slowing the softening.', '', '["The minerals in hard water enhance bean flavor but reduce the temperature.","Calcium and magnesium ions in hard water form insoluble salts with pectin, slowing the softening.","Hard water contains fewer electrolytes needed for heat transfer.","Beans absorb less water in hard water due to its higher boiling point"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756879152691-7', 'anki-deck-1783609411469-1790433139866-aqx4l', 'Why is it advisable to add acidic ingredients (like vinegar or calamansi) at the end of cooking green vegetables such as kangkong in dishes like sinigang?', 'Acids promote the formation of pheophytin, causing a dull or olive green color if added early.', '', '["Acids enhance the texture of vegetables by making them firmer.","Acids speed up the cooking process by increasing the temperature.","Acids preserve chlorophyll, maintaining the bright green color of vegetables.","Acids promote the formation of pheophytin, causing a dull or olive green color if added early."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.986Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
