('anki-card-1758787860990-82', 'anki-deck-1783610488281-1790433142627-pf2m5', 'The approximate value for the thermic effect of a 2,500-kcal diet is: *', '250 kcal', '', '["25 kcal","250 kcal","400 kcal","500 kcal"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, 'The Thermic Effect of Food (TEF)—also known as specific dynamic action (SDA)—is the amount of energy expenditure your body uses to digest, absorb, transport, and store nutrients from a meal. For a standard mixed diet, TEF is universally estimated to be approximately 10% of the total energy intake.', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-29T16:04:31.259Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T16:04:31.259Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:29.989Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T16:04:31.259Z"'::jsonb),
