Sentence B. Bacteria causes holes in swiss cheese.', 'Sentence B is correct', 'Primarily, Rennet or acids: Milk is turned into solid curds and liquid whey using rennet (an enzyme) or acids like vinegar or lemon juice, rather than bacteria alone.

Lactic acid bacteria: Starter cultures of bacteria are added to milk to consume lactose and produce lactic acid, which helps with acidification and flavor. This acid environment prepares the milk, but coagulation itself relies on rennet or direct acidifiers

Certain cultures also produce gases that create the characteristic holes in Swiss-type cheeses.

The holes in Swiss cheese are created by carbon dioxide gas released during fermentation by the bacterium Propionibacterium freudenreichii.', '["Sentence A is correct","Sentence B is correct","Both sentences are correct","Both sentences are incorrect"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:49:41.176Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:49:41.176Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:49:41.176Z"'::jsonb),
