('anki-card-1755153278002-36', 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Sentence A. Pasteurized milk can be stored at room temperature.
Sentence B. In pasteurization, pathogenic microorganisms are destroyed.', 'Sentence B is correct', 'Sentence A is incorrect because pasteurized milk still requires refrigeration. 

Sentence B is correct because pasteurization is designed to destroy pathogenic microorganisms and reduce spoilage organisms, although it does not sterilize the product.

Pasteurization – the process of heating food to a certain temperature and holding it at that temperature until most of the possible pathogens present in food are destroyed or killed. Used for products that are heat-sensitive like milk and fruit juices.

Sterilization – the process by which food is rendered completely free of microorganisms, which could be injurious to the health of man. Use temperatures higher than that in pasteurization. A “commercially sterile” product is not completely free of microorganisms but has killed all but the more resistant bacterial (thermophilic) spores and conditions in the container are not conducive for the growth of the bacterial spores.', '["Sentence A is correct","Sentence B is correct","Both sentences are correct","Both sentences are incorrect"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T12:57:41.409Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T12:57:41.409Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T12:57:41.625Z"'::jsonb),
