• Sentence A is incorrect: Polished rice (white rice) actually cooks much faster than unpolished rice (brown or red rice). Polished rice usually takes about 15 to 20 minutes to cook, whereas unpolished rice takes 40 to 45 minutes. This is because unpolished rice retains its tough, fibrous outer bran layer, which slows down water absorption and requires a longer time to soften.
• Sentence B is incorrect: Since the premise of Sentence A is completely backward, the explanation in Sentence B is also fundamentally incorrect. While milling and polishing do increase the percentage of starch by weight (by stripping away the fiber-rich bran and nutrient-dense germ), it makes the grain cook faster, not longer, because the water can instantly penetrate the exposed starch.', '["Sentence A is correct","Sentence B is correct","Both sentences are correct","Both sentences are incorrect"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:50:42.813Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:50:42.813Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:50:42.813Z"'::jsonb),
