Sentence B. Temporary emulsions are separated by heat.', 'Sentence A is correct', 'Sentence A is correct because vinaigrette is a temporary emulsion of oil and vinegar that separates on standing. 

Sentence B is incorrect because temporary emulsions separate primarily because the phases are immiscible and the emulsion is unstable, not simply because of heat.', '["Sentence A is correct","Sentence B is correct","Both sentences are correct","Both sentences are incorrect"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:22:53.292Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:22:53.292Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:22:53.292Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1755155315058-94', 'anki-deck-1755151710403-1790432463944-n11t8', 'Best temperature for drying.', '140-145ºF', 'In food dehydration, 140°F or 60°C is widely recognized as the optimum standard temperature. If the temperature is too high, the outside of the food cooks and hardens (“case hardening”), which traps moisture inside and leads to molding. 

This temperature range is also high enough to safely drive out moisture quickly before spoilage micro-organisms can replicate, but low enough to avoid cooking the food. 

Consider also:
• Air Flow
• Time
• Nature of food', '["100-115ºF","120-125ºF","130-135ºF","140-145ºF"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-23T16:45:16.051Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:45:16.051Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.039Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-22T16:45:16.051Z"'::jsonb),
