('anki-card-1754292489190-106', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'What is stated in the 7th Nutritional Guidelines for Filipinos', 'Use iodized salt to prevent Iodine Deficiency Disorders', 'Nutritional Guideline for Filipinos (NGF) Rule #7 specifically recommends: "Use iodized salt to prevent Iodine Deficiency Disorders (IDD)." Iodized salt is mandated under RA 8172 (ASIN Law) to eliminate goiter, cretinism, and mental impairment.', '["Consume milk, milk product, and other calcium-rich foods, such as small fish and shellfish, every day for healthy bones and teeth","Use iodized salt to prevent Iodine Deficiency Disorders","Eat more vegetables and fruits every day to get essential vitamins, minerals, and fiber for regulation of body processes.","Limit intake of salty, fried, fatty, and sugar-rich foods to prevent cardiovascular disease"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T15:33:11.772Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:33:11.772Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:33:11.974Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754299830914-195', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'This refers to the presence of adequate, quality, and safe food that satisfies the dietary need of individual, supplied through either domestic production or imports', 'Availability', 'Availability - physical presence of food

• Accessibility - ability to get or afford the resources (e.g., food, services, markets).
• Nutrition security - consistent access, affordability, and utilization of diverse, safe, and nutritious food to ensure a healthy life.
• Economic security - stable income, resources, and access to work that guarantees a basic standard of living and protects against shocks.', '["Availability","Accessibility","Nutrition security","Economic security"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T12:54:26.886Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T12:54:26.886Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T12:54:26.886Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754299671340-193', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'All of the following are possible blocks to food consumption except:', 'poor road conditions', 'In community nutrition, barriers to food security are classified according to specific stages of the Food Pathway:
• Food Distribution Block: Poor road conditions serve as a barrier during the transport and logistics stage. It prevents food from reaching marketplaces efficiently, affecting availability and accessibility rather than the choices made at the household table.
• Food Consumption Blocks: Religious laws (e.g., halal/kosher), personal food preferences, and a lack of knowledge on nutrition are all localized or individual factors that directly obstruct or alter how families choose to consume available food.', '["food preference","religion","knowledge on nutrition","poor road conditions"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T07:58:25.050Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T07:58:25.050Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T07:58:25.366Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754298054063-166', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Schilling test is used to assess the status of this vitamin?', 'Vit B12', 'The Schilling test is a classic diagnostic procedure specifically designed to assess the body''s ability to absorb vitamin B12, including distinguishing whether malabsorption is due to intrinsic factor deficiency (pernicious anemia) or another cause.', '["Vit B12","Vit B6","Vit B2","Vit B1"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T15:32:09.489Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:32:09.489Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:32:09.692Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754292095672-102', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'The Nutriskwela Community Radio Network partners named their stations with words starting with this letter.', 'K', 'The correct answer is the letter K, reflecting the “ka-“ branding convention used across Nutriskwela community radio stations established by the NNC.', '["C","K","N","M"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T08:21:02.256Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:21:02.256Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:21:02.256Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754294321520-126', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'In preparing for program planning and management, the first step is:', 'Identifications/mobilization of LNC or planning core group', 'Establishing the group responsible for leading the planning process is the necessary first step before any assessment, goal-setting, or plan preparation can occur. 

Assessment or diagnostic analysis, setting goals and objectives, and preparing the plan of operation are all important subsequent steps, but they require an organized planning group to already be in place to carry them out.', '["Assessment or Diagnostic Analysis","Setting of goals and objectives","Identifications/mobilization of LNC or planning core group","Preparation of plan of operation"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T13:42:57.936Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T13:42:57.936Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T13:42:58.141Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754298754614-178', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'What is the biochemical criterion included in the WHO classification scheme for xerophthalmia?', 'Plasma Vitamin A level', 'Plasma vitamin A level is the standard biochemical marker used alongside clinical/ocular signs (like night blindness, Bitot''s spots, corneal xerosis) in the WHO classification of xerophthalmia severity.

• Skinfold thickness – measures body fat
• Sensitivity test for Vitamin A deficiency - vague, non-standard term rather than a recognized biochemical criterion
• Urinary Vitamin A concentration - not the standard biochemical measure used for vitamin A status, since vitamin A is fat-soluble and stored/circulated differently than water-soluble vitamins excreted in urine.', '["Skinfold thickness","Sensitivity test for Vitamin A deficiency","Plasma Vitamin A level","Urinary Vitamin A concentration"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T15:28:22.412Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:28:22.412Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:28:22.615Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754298675651-177', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Breastmilk can be used for biochemical assessment of ?', 'Vit A', 'In public health and community nutrition assessments, breast milk retinol concentration is a well-established, non-invasive biomarker used to evaluate the Vitamin A status of both lactating mothers and their breastfed infants.

• Breast milk retinol levels are highly sensitive to maternal Vitamin A intake and liver reserves.
• The World Health Organization (WHO) recognizes breast milk testing as a valuable epidemiological tool. A high prevalence of low breast milk retinol concentrations (e.g., < 1.05 µmol/L or < 30 µg/dL) in a community indicates a subclinical Vitamin A deficiency problem requiring public health interventions like maternal postpartum supplementation or food fortification.

• Vitamin K & Vitamin D: Human breast milk is inherently and universally low in both Vitamin K and Vitamin D, regardless of maternal nutritional status. Because their baseline levels in milk are naturally close to zero, breast milk is not used as a reliable biochemical index to assess systemic status for these vitamins.
• Vitamin E: While present in breast milk (especially colostrum), serum alpha-tocopherol blood tests remain the primary clinical diagnostic tool for Vitamin E, rather than breast milk analysis.', '["Vit K","Vit E","Vit D","Vit A"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T08:33:26.418Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:33:26.418Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:33:26.606Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754298630654-176', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Which of the followng is NOT a substrate used to assess zinc status?', 'Nails', 'Nails are not a standard, validated substrate used in clinical or population-level zinc status assessment. 

Hair, saliva, and blood/plasma are all recognized substrates that have been used, with varying degrees of reliability, to assess zinc status in research and clinical settings.', '["Hair","Saliva","Blood","Nails"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T08:19:52.013Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:19:52.013Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:19:52.013Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754298586803-175', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Which of the following is a functional test used to assess Vitamin A?', 'Dark adaptation test', 'In nutritional assessment, diagnostic tools are broadly split into biochemical (static) tests and functional tests:

A functional test measures the actual biological or physiological consequence of a nutrient deficiency on body function. Vitamin A is vital for the formation of rhodopsin (visual purple) in the rod cells of the retina, which allows eyes to see in dim light. The dark adaptation test evaluates the functional impairment of night vision caused by early-stage Vitamin A deficiency.

	• Test for serum albumin: A biochemical test primarily used as a general indicator of visceral protein status or systemic inflammation rather than a vitamin check.
	• Immunological test: Assesses immune system components (like T-cell counts or antibody levels). While Vitamin A impacts immunity, it is not a direct diagnostic test for it.
	• Test for urinary creatinine: Used alongside height measurements to calculate the creatinine-height index (CHI), which estimates skeletal muscle mass or evaluates kidney function.', '["Immunological test","Test for serum albumin","Dark adaptation test","Test for urinary creatinine"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T15:33:42.398Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:33:42.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:33:42.598Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754298998121-182', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'A deficiency in ___ can be seen in the nails', 'Selenium', 'Selenium, whose deficiency can manifest with changes visible in the nails (among other signs), consistent with selenium''s role in numerous enzymatic and antioxidant functions. 

• Iodine deficiency instead manifests primarily as goiter and thyroid-related signs. 
• Thiamin deficiency manifests as beri-beri-related neurological/cardiovascular signs. 
• Copper deficiency, while it can affect hair (as in Menkes disease), is not primarily associated with nail changes in the same way selenium is.', '["Iodine","Selenium","Thiamin","Copper"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-25T08:53:39.418Z","interval":27,"easeFactor":2.1,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:53:39.418Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:53:39.603Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754298537274-174', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'It is a condition when Vit B3 is deficient', 'Pellagra', 'Pellagra is a niacin deficiency, classically presenting with the "three Ds": dermatitis, diarrhea, and dementia (and if untreated, a fourth D - death).

• Ariboflavinosis – riboflavin deficiency
• Beri-beri – thiamin deficiency
• Tiqui-tiqui - extract to cure beri-beri', '["Pellagra","Ariboflavinosis","Beri-beri","Tiqui-Tiqui"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T09:43:51.596Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:43:51.596Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:43:51.596Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754298484727-173', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'An essential trace element for both humans and animals.', 'Molybdenum', 'Molybdenum is a recognized essential trace element required by both humans and animals for enzymatic cofactor functions (such as in xanthine oxidase). 

Bromine, lithium, and vanadium are elements that have been studied for potential biological roles but are not established as essential trace elements with confirmed dietary requirement status in the same way molybdenum is officially recognized.', '["Bromine","Lithium","Vanadium","Molybdenum"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T07:41:32.820Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T07:41:32.820Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T07:41:32.820Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754298433363-172', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Diagnostic test to determine the sufficiency of post nutriture to permit cells, tissues, organ systems or the host to optimally perform nutrient dependent biologic function.', 'Functional test', 'Functional test is the measure of actual physiological/biological functions.

• Biochemical test - laboratory test
• Clinical test - physical test
• Static test - single-point-in-time biochemical measurement', '["Functional test","Biochemical test","Clinical test","Static test"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T15:33:21.085Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:33:21.085Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:33:21.282Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754298331816-171', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Sonia has a fasting blood sugar level of 118 mg/dl. According to the assessment criteria of WHO, this value can be classified as  ____', 'impaired', 'According to the World Health Organization (WHO) and standard medical assessment guidelines, intermediate states of glucose regulation are formally categorized using the term "impaired".
• Impaired Fasting Glucose (IFG): Defined as a fasting blood sugar level between 100 mg/dL and 125 mg/dL (or 6.1 mmol/L to 6.9 mmol/L based on specific WHO thresholds). Since Sonia''s value is 118 mg/dl, it falls precisely within this category.
• Impaired Glucose Tolerance (IGT): Refers to blood sugar levels that are elevated during a 2-hour postprandial or oral glucose tolerance test (140–199 mg/dL).
In a clinical or exam context, these clinical categories represent "prediabetes," flagging that the individual''s glucose metabolism is altered but has not yet met the diagnostic cutoff for a diabetes mellitus classification (≥126 mg/dL).

Normal Levels
	• Fasting Blood Sugar: Less than 100 mg/dL (< 5.6 mmol/L)
	• 2-Hour Oral Glucose Tolerance Test: Less than 140 mg/dL (< 7.8 mmol/L)
	• HbA1c: Less than 5.7% (< 39 mmol/mol)

 Impaired Levels (Prediabetes)
	• Fasting Blood Sugar: 100 to 125 mg/dL (5.6 to 6.9 mmol/L) — called Impaired Fasting Glucose (IFG)
	• 2-Hour Oral Glucose Tolerance Test: 140 to 199 mg/dL (7.8 to 11.0 mmol/L) — called Impaired Glucose Tolerance (IGT)
	• HbA1c: 5.7% to 6.4% (39 to 46 mmol/mol)

 Diabetes Mellitus
	• Fasting Blood Sugar: 126 mg/dL or higher (≥ 7.0 mmol/L)
	• 2-Hour Oral Glucose Tolerance Test: 200 mg/dL or higher (≥ 11.1 mmol/L)
	• HbA1c: 6.5% or higher (≥ 48 mmol/mol)
	• Random Blood Sugar: 200 mg/dL or higher when accompanied by severe symptoms like extreme thirst or frequent urination', '["desirable","impaired","borderline","high"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T08:02:27.780Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:02:27.780Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:02:27.780Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754298261902-170', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'The method used to analyze protein content of foods in the FCT:', 'Kjeldahl', 'Kjeldahl method is the standard, classic laboratory technique for determining protein content by measuring total nitrogen and applying a conversion factor, widely used in food composition analysis.

• Soxhlet - fat/lipid extraction and analysis
• Roes-Gottlieb - specific method for fat analysis in dairy products
• Carr-Price - colorimetric method historically used for vitamin A analysis', '["Soxhlet","Rose-Gottlieb","Kjeldahl","Carr-Price"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T08:29:21.309Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:29:21.309Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:29:21.633Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754298209918-169', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Laxatives can affect nutrient absorption through ___', 'altering motility', 'Laxatives work primarily by speeding up gastrointestinal transit time, which reduces the contact time between food/nutrients and the absorptive intestinal surface, thereby impairing nutrient absorption.', '["binding to nutrients","altering motility","irritating the GIT","interfering with taste"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T08:33:43.539Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:33:43.539Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:33:43.731Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754298156308-168', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Which among these food items is a good source of preformed Vitamin A?', 'Egg yolk', 'Egg yolk contains preformed vitamin A (retinol) directly, as animal-source foods provide vitamin A in its ready-to-use, preformed (retinol) state. 

Grains, peanuts, and corn oil are all plant-based foods that, if they contain any vitamin A activity at all, would provide it as provitamin A carotenoids (like beta-carotene) rather than preformed vitamin A, which the body must convert before use.', '["Egg yolk","Grains","Peanuts","Corn oil"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T15:33:32.238Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:33:32.238Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:33:32.435Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754298111810-167', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'A condition when folate and Vitamin B12 are deficient', 'Megaloblastic anemia', 'Megaloblastic anemia - RBCs are large and immature due to impaired DNA synthesis; large (macrocytic) RBCs; caused by folate or vitamin B12 deficiency.

• Microcytic anemia - RBCs are abnormally small.
• Pernicious anemia - megaloblastic anemia caused specifically by lack of intrinsic factor (for B12 absorption).
• Hypochromic anemia - RBCs are pale due to insufficient hemoglobin.', '["Megaloblastic anemia","Microcytic anemia","Pernicious anemia","Hypochromic anemia"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T08:22:51.607Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:22:51.607Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:22:51.796Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754298010483-165', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'A condition characterized by vertical fissuring in the lips:', 'Cheilosis', 'Cheilosis is the vertical cracking/fissuring at the lips, sometimes extending to angular fissures at the mouth corners (angular stomatitis).

• Fluorosis - affects tooth enamel (mottling) from excess fluoride
• Glossitis - inflammation of the tongue
• Dermatitis - general skin inflammation', '["Fluorosis","Glossitis","Cheilosis","Dermatitis"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T07:40:59.718Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T07:40:59.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T07:40:59.718Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754297971150-164', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'A condition characterized as having sand paper feel of the skin:', 'Follicular hyperkeratosis', 'In clinical nutrition and dermatology, follicular hyperkeratosis (also known as phrynoderma or "toad skin") is classic textbook-defined by a rough, sandpaper-like texture on the skin.

This condition occurs when the body overproduces keratin (a structural protein), which forms hard, scaly plugs that block the openings of hair follicles. This creates tiny, elevated, rough bumps typically found on the back of the upper arms, thighs, and buttocks.

In a board exam context, follicular hyperkeratosis is highly pathognomonic for Vitamin A deficiency or a chronic lack of essential fatty acids (like Omega-3).

• Pellagrous dermatitis - symmetric, dark, scaling rash on sun-exposed skin (the "casal''s necklace").
• Petechiae - tiny, non-blanching red or purple dots on the skin due to bleeding under the skin.
• Xerosis - generalized, abnormal dryness of the skin (or mucous membranes).', '["Pellagrous dermatitis","Follicular hyperkeratosis","Petechiae","Xerosis"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T08:37:33.886Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:37:33.886Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:37:34.073Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754297916202-163', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Keshan disease is a deficiency in?', 'Selenium', 'The correct answer is selenium, a trace mineral deficiency specifically linked to Keshan disease, an endemic cardiomyopathy first identified in selenium-poor regions of China.

Keshan disease is an endemic, potentially fatal form of dilated cardiomyopathy (weakening and enlargement of the heart muscle).

 It is directly linked to severe dietary selenium deficiency, typically occurring in rural regions where the soil lacks selenium, leaving local agricultural crops deplete of the mineral. It was first documented in Keshan County, China.', '["Selenium","Chromium","Zinc","Folate"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T10:56:46.965Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:56:46.965Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:56:46.965Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754297871940-162', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Using the WHO standard, what is the classification of goiter if the thyroid gland is enlarged and easily visible from a distance?', 'Grade 2', 'In 1994, the WHO, UNICEF, and the International Council for Control of Iodine Deficiency Disorders simplified the scale down to the standard 3-tier system:

• Grade 0: No goiter (neither palpable nor visible).
• Grade 1: A mass that is palpable but not visible when the neck is in a normal position.
• Grade 2: A swelling that is clearly visible when the neck is in a normal position and is consistent with an enlarged thyroid upon palpation.', '["Grade 0","Grade 1","Grade 2","Grade 3"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T15:32:06.621Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:32:06.621Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:32:06.823Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754297799490-161', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'The plasma retinol level of Flora is 25 µg/dL. How do you interpret this value?', 'Flora has an acceptable plasma retinol level', 'In public health and clinical nutrition, the World Health Organization (WHO) and the National Institutes of Health (NIH) establish specific reference thresholds for circulating plasma or serum retinol to evaluate Vitamin A status:

• Deficient / Severe Deficiency: Less than 10 µg/dL (< 0.35 µmol/L).
• Low / Subclinical Deficiency: 10 to 20 µg/dL (0.35 to 0.70 µmol/L).
• Acceptable / Adequate: More than 20 µg/dL (≥ 0.70 µmol/L).

Flora''s level is 25 µg/dL, which places her comfortably above the 20 µg/dL cutoff, classifying her Vitamin A status as acceptable or adequate.', '["Flora has a deficient plasma retinol level","Flora has a low plasma retinol level","Flora has an acceptable plasma retinol level","Flora has high plasma retinal level"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T15:34:55.869Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:34:55.869Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:34:56.070Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754297710612-160', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Moderate IDD in the population is indicated by median UIE level of:', '20-49 µg/L', 'The severity of Iodine Deficiency Disorders (IDD) in a population is classified based on the Median Urinary Iodine Excretion (UIE) or Concentration (UIC) levels:
• Severe Iodine Deficiency: Median UIE of <20 µg/L
• Moderate Iodine Deficiency: Median UIE of 20–49 µg/L
• Mild Iodine Deficiency: Median UIE of 50–99 µg/L
• Adequate Iodine Nutrition: Median UIE of 100–199 µg/L (Target public health range for school-age children)', '["20-49 µg/L","<20 µg/L","50-99 µg/L",">100 µg/L"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T15:31:26.812Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:31:26.812Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:31:27.012Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754297652397-159', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Multiple replicates of 24-hour food recall is used to measure nutrient intake to meet ___ level of study objectives', '2nd', 'Second-level study objectives (often referred to as secondary or specific objectives) break down primary research goal into actionable, measurable steps. First-level (primary) objective states WHAT you want to achieve overall, second-level objectives explain HOW you will achieve it by focusing on specific variables, steps, or populations.', '["1st","2nd","3rd","4th"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T15:27:10.015Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:27:10.015Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:27:10.214Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754297606534-158', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'It is a condition when thiamin is deficient', 'Beri-beri', 'Beri-beri is a classic, well-established clinical deficiency disease resulting from inadequate thiamine (vitamin B1) intake, presenting with neurological (dry beri-beri) or cardiovascular (wet beri-beri) manifestations. 

• Pellagra - niacin (vitamin B3) deficiency 
• Ariboflavinosis - riboflavin (vitamin B2) deficiency 
• Tiqui-tiqui is actually a traditional Filipino rice bran extract historically used as a treatment/cure for beri-beri', '["Pellagra","Ariboflavinosis","Beri-beri","Tiqui-tiqui"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T10:50:53.657Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:50:53.657Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:50:53.657Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754297385077-156', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Which of the following is a dietary assessment method which uses specific food item list to record intakes over a given period?', 'Food frequency', 'Food frequency questionnaire (FFQ), which is defined precisely by its use of a structured, predetermined list of food items that respondents report consuming over a specified recall period (e.g., past month or year). 

• The 24-hour food recall instead captures all foods consumed in the preceding 24 hours without being restricted to a predetermined food list. 
• Diet records involve prospectively recording all foods eaten in real time, also without a fixed food item list. 
• Food weighing involves precisely weighing all food consumed.', '["24-hour food recall","Food frequency","Diet record","Food weighing"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T13:55:27.488Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T13:55:27.488Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T13:55:27.682Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754297296463-155', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Which of the following methods can be used to estimate height?', 'Arm span', 'When a patient cannot stand straight due to physical disabilities, bedridden status, or severe skeletal deformities (such as kyphosis or scoliosis), indirect anthropometric measurements are used to estimate stature:

 There is a strong biological correlation between an individual''s arm span and their actual height. In a healthy adult, the distance from the tip of the middle finger of one hand to the tip of the middle finger of the other hand (when arms are extended fully at a 90-degree angle from the torso) roughly equals their max height.

Other common clinical measurements used in height-estimation equations include knee height and demispan (half of the arm span).

• Skinfold thickness - fat deposits
• MUAC - muscle mass
• Chest circumference - chest size', '["Arm span","Skinfold thickness","MUAC","Chest circumference"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T11:23:50.928Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T11:23:50.928Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T11:23:51.105Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754297244199-154', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'A measure of years in perfect health lost:', 'DALY', 'DALY - Disability-Adjusted Life Year (Burden of Disease): Measures the total healthy life years lost (YLL + YLD).

• YLL - Years of Life Lost (Mortality): Measures the number of years lost due to premature death.
• YLD - Years Lived with Disability (Morbidity): Measures the number of years lived in less than full health due to illness or injury.
• QALY - Quality-Adjusted Life Year (Health Economics): Measures the value of a year of life adjusted by its quality or utility.', '["YLL","YLD","QALY","DALY"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T08:39:31.398Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:39:31.398Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:39:31.589Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754297204152-153', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'It describes the adequacy with which any measurement or index reflects the nutritional parameter of interest:', 'Validity', 'Validity - measuring what you intended to measure (truthfulness)

• Accuracy - how close a measurement is to the true or accepted value (correctness)
• Specificity - a test''s ability to correctly identify negative cases (truly non-diseased or non-affected).
• Precision - how close repeated measurements are to each other (consistency/reproducibility)', '["Validity","Accuracy","Specificity","Precision"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T13:27:04.975Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T13:27:04.975Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T13:27:04.975Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754297142507-152', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'A good survey sample is one in which:', 'the subjects are heterogenous', 'In most social, health, and market research, the goal is to have a representative sample that reflects the heterogeneity (diversity) of the larger population.', '["the entire population to be studied is included","all the characteristics of the population are represented proportionately","the subject are willing volunteers","the subjects are heterogenous"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T15:35:29.932Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:35:29.932Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:35:30.130Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754297053708-151', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'It refers to the epidemiological approach which explains the occurence, nature, and extent of a disease:', 'Man-Agent-Environment Triad', 'Man-Agent-Environment triad - epidemiological model; analyzing disease causation via host, pathogen, and surroundings.

• Triple A approach - cycle for planning: assessment, analysis, action
• UNICEF framework - three-level causes of malnutrition: basic, underlying, and immediate (food/health).
• Undernutrition infection cycle - vicious spiral where poor nutrition weakens immunity, increasing infection risk, which worsens nutrition.', '["Triple A approach","Man-Agent-Environment Triad","UNICEF framework","Undernutrition infection cycle"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T08:47:05.807Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:47:05.807Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:47:06.113Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754296966446-150', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'A researcher wants to conduct a study wherein men with coronary artery disease and a comparable group of men without coronary artery disease were asked about their prior use of aspirin. This is an example of which type of study?', 'Case control', 'This scenario perfectly illustrates the design of a case-control study based on two defining factors:

• Selection by Outcome (Disease Status): The researcher selects participants based on whether they already have the condition of interest. The "cases" are the men with coronary artery disease, and the "controls" are the comparable group of men without the disease.
• Retrospective Assessment: The researcher then looks backward in time ("asked about their prior use of aspirin") to compare how frequently each group was exposed to the factor being studied.

• Ecological study - Comparing the average per capita salt intake across ten different countries to the average national hypertension rate in those same countries.
• Randomized clinical trial - Dividing 500 patients with a specific disease into two groups: one receiving a new drug and one receiving a placebo (or standard treatment), and then following both groups for a year to see which group has a better outcome.
• Case series - A doctor publishing a report detailing the clinical presentation, diagnosis, treatment, and outcomes for three unusual patients presenting with the same rare cluster of symptoms at their clinic over a six-month period.', '["Case control","Ecological study","Randomized clinial trial","Case series"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T14:55:11.634Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T14:55:11.634Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T14:55:11.634Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754297544770-157', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Which of the following describes nutrition surveillance?', 'Keeping watch over nutrition in order to make decisions that will lead to improvement in nutrition in population', 'This responds to the main goal of nutrition surveillance is to continuously monitor a population''s nutritional status so leaders can make informed decisions and policies that improve health and fix nutrition problems.', '["Keeping watch over nutrition in order to make decisions that will lead to improvement in nutrition in population","Provides information about dietary intake patterns, specific foods consumed and estimated nutrient intake","Mortality and morbidity data to identify groups at high risk and indicate the extent of risk of the community","All of the above"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T15:32:19.169Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:32:19.169Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:32:19.372Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754296874551-149', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'A decision-making process of identifying potential nutrition problems and needs of a specific population group, analyzing possible ways of preventing and controlling malnutrition, allocating resources based on needs and expectations, and taking deliberate action to address nutritional problems, including those related to monitoring and evaluation.', 'Nutrition Program Management', 'Nutrition Program Management is executing, supervising, and coordinating all activities to achieve program goals.

• Nutrition Program Planning - designing the specific program: defining objectives, strategies, resources, and implementation steps.
• Nutrition Intervention - specific action designed to directly improve nutritional status (e.g., supplementation, education).
• Food and Nutrition Planning - macro-level process to set national/regional policies and strategies for food supply and consumption.', '["Nutrition Program Management","Nutrition Program Planning","Nutrition Intervention","Food and Nutrition Planning"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T08:37:36.627Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:37:36.627Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:37:36.627Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754296717625-148', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'A BNS is trained volunteer community worker with the following qualifications EXCEPT:', 'At least high school graduate', 'At least high school graduate - the law states ‘elementary’ or ‘primary school’ (see PD 1569)', '["Bonadife resident of the barangay","At least high school graduate","Willingness to serve, part-time or full-time","More than 18 years old, but younger than 60 years old"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T07:52:15.829Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T07:52:15.829Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T07:52:15.829Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754296620729-147', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'In 1976, Letter of Instruction 441 directed the Department of Local Government and Community Development (now called DILG) to establish ____ in every region, province, city, municipality to implement nutrition action plans.', 'Functional nutrition committees', 'Functional nutrition committees, which LOI 441 specifically mandated be established at every administrative level to implement nutrition action plans, laying early institutional groundwork for what would later become the Local Nutrition Committees.', '["Functional nutrition councils","Functional nutrition committees","Functional nutrition coordinating system","Functional nutrition management system"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T10:23:58.281Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:23:58.281Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:23:58.281Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754296410604-146', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Interventions that address the immediate causes of malnutrition.', 'Nutrition-Specific Interventions', 'Nutrition-specific interventions address the immediate, direct causes of malnutrition at the individual level (e.g., micronutrient supplementation, breastfeeding promotion, treatment of acute malnutrition).

• Nutrition-sensitive interventions instead address the underlying causes of malnutrition, such as food security, health services access, and caregiving practices, operating at a different causal level. 
• "Nutrition and Development Interventions" and "Nutrition-in-Development Interventions" are not standard, recognized terms in this classification framework.', '["Nutrition-Sensitive Interventions","Nutrition and Development Interventions","Nutrition-in-Development Interventions","Nutrition-Specific Interventions"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T15:32:34.637Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:32:34.637Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:32:34.836Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754296241345-144', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'In planning for a supplementary feeding, the following are key decision points, EXCEPT:', 'What technology of production will be promoted?', '“What technology of production will be promoted?” refers to a food production intervention.', '["Type of commodity to be used to include for formulationss like Nutripak","What technology of production will be promoted?","Center-based vs home-based","Mechanism for community mobilization and particpation of parents"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T08:51:02.320Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:51:02.320Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:51:02.320Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754296131638-143', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'In planning for a food for work intervention, the following key decision points must be considered, EXCEPT:', 'Will the assistance be in cash or kind?', 'By definition, food-for-work is already established as a food (in-kind) assistance modality, so this cash-versus-kind question does not apply as a decision point within a program already defined as food-based.', '["What food commodities will be used?","What volume of food will be given for each unit of work?","Will the assistance be in cash or kind?","What complementary services will be provided?"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T09:54:17.765Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:54:17.765Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:54:17.765Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754296007893-142', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'The LNAP is best prepared on the first semester of an election year to ensure that the nutrition agenda is integrated in the Executive Legislative Agenda which becomes the bases for local development plan and in-turn the annual investment plan. This is essential for:', 'Local Budgeting', 'Local budgeting because timely integration of the nutrition agenda into the Executive Legislative Agenda ensures that nutrition programs are properly reflected and funded in the subsequent Annual Investment Plan and local budget allocations. 

While local planning, implementation, and monitoring/evaluation are all eventually affected by this timing, the question mentioning ELA and AIP points most directly to securing adequate budgeting for nutrition programs.', '["Local Planning","Local Budgeting","Local Implementation","Local Monitoring and evaluation"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T10:08:57.545Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:08:57.545Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:08:57.545Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754295703656-139', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'In the Monitoring and Evaluation of Local Level Plan Implementation (MELLPI) of the National Nutrition Council, which one refers to the highest award given to an LGU?', 'Nutrition Honor Award', 'The National Nutrition Council (NNC) utilizes the MELLPI framework to monitor Local Government Units (LGUs) and recognize them with progressive awards for outstanding performance in implementing the Philippine Plan of Action for Nutrition (PPAN):

• Nutrition Honor Award (NHA): This is the highest and most prestigious accolade given to an LGU. It is conferred only to LGUs that have maintained excellent nutrition program implementation for six (6) consecutive years, coming with a standard ₱1,000,000 cash prize and trophy.
• Consistent Regional Outstanding Winner in Nutrition (CROWN) Award: Given to an LGU that has been a regional winner for three (3) consecutive years. After achieving the CROWN, an LGU must successfully clear 1st and 2nd Year CROWN Maintenance Evaluations before it can qualify for the final Nutrition Honor Award.
• Green Banner Seal of Compliance: The initial tier of recognition awarded at the regional level to municipalities, cities, or provinces that excel in their annual nutrition performance benchmarks.', '["Green Banner Award","Consistent Regional Outstanding Winner in Nutrition","Nutrition Honor Award","National Outstanding Nutrition Award"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T12:47:03.246Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T12:47:03.246Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T12:47:03.246Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754295580230-138', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Field visits, meeting, record keeping, reporting, plan implementation reviews and special studies are known approaches for:', 'Monitoring and Evaluation', 'The correct answer is monitoring and evaluation combined, since this specific list of activities (field visits, meetings, record keeping, reporting, implementation reviews, special studies) spans both the ongoing, process-tracking functions of monitoring and the more in-depth, periodic assessment functions of evaluation.

• Monitoring alone or evaluation alone would not fully encompass this comprehensive list of approaches, since some (like routine field visits and record keeping) are more monitoring-oriented while others (like special studies) are more evaluation-oriented. 
• "Monitoring or evaluation" incorrectly implies these are separate, alternative approaches and not combined, integrated set of activities.', '["Monitoring","Evaluation","Monitoring and Evaluation","Monitoring or Evaluation"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T07:55:39.496Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T07:55:39.496Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T07:55:39.496Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754295498266-137', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Adoption of Local Nutrition Action Plan by the LGU requires:', 'All of the above', 'Formal LNAP adoption by a local government unit requires multiple coordinated steps together: acceptance, approval, and endorsement by the local chief executive to the Sanggunian; sponsorship by a member of the local legislative body; and a resolution filed for adoption and funding.', '["Acceptance, approval and endorsement of LCE to Sangguniang Bayan/Panlalawigan","Sponsorship by a member of the local legislative body","Resolution filed for adoption and funding of the LNAP","All of the above"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T10:03:48.820Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:03:48.820Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:03:48.820Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754295389422-136', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'In process evaluation, the following questions will be addressed, EXCEPT:', 'What will be the result of this project?', 'The question "what will be the result of this project?" belongs to result evaluation, which focuses on outcomes and impact, not process evaluation, which focuses on implementation quality and efficiency.', '["Are we doing our job well?","What can we be improved upon in the project?","Are we spending resources properly?","What will be the result of this project?"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T14:55:54.648Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T14:55:54.648Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T14:55:54.842Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754295288077-135', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'It shows how inputs or resources invested in the project are transformed through a series of sequential processes into outputs; helpful in monitoring ongoing projects or activities.', 'Process evaluation', 'Process evaluation - assessing how the program was implemented and managed (efficiency, quality).

• Ex-ante evaluation - assessing potential before program starts (feasibility, relevance).
• Ex-post evaluation - assessing actual results/impact after program ends (overall success).
• Result evaluation - assessing what the program achieved (outcomes, effects, and impact).', '["Ex-ante evaluation","Ex-post evaluation","Process evaluation","Result evaluation"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T13:24:34.247Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T13:24:34.247Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T13:24:34.247Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754295192634-134', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'It refers to the changes in the condition of the target population which generally reflect the primary objectives of the project or program, e.g. percent improvement in the prevalence of stunting in the municipality.', 'Impact indicator', 'Impact indicator - measures long-term, ultimate changes in well-being or the environment (e.g., reduced mortality rates, national poverty reduction)

• Input indicator - measures resources put into a program (e.g., funds spent, staff hired)
• Output indicator - measures direct, tangible results of program activities (e.g., training sessions held, meals served)
• Outcome indicator - measures changes in behavior, knowledge, or condition achieved by the target group (e.g., improved hygiene practices, increased enrollment)', '["Input indicator","Output indicator","Outcome indicator","Impact indicator"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T08:37:21.574Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:37:21.574Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:37:21.766Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754295080469-133', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Information which is used to measure changes which occur during course of program it allows one to monitor the progress of the program or it is a measure of progress towards meeting a program''s objectives', 'Indicators', 'Indicators are specific, measurable values that show the status or progress toward a desired result or goal.

• Data - raw, unorganized facts and figures
• Records - stored, organized sets of data about a specific entity
• Criteria - standards or principles used to judge, classify, or make a decision (e.g., age, income level).', '["Data","Records","Criteria","Indicators"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T09:45:08.653Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:45:08.653Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:45:08.841Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754294999358-132', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'It is the regular and periodical follow-up of the implementation of planned activities and progress to determine whether steps in the strategy are followed and whether program objectives by phase or activity are attained as planned.', 'Monitoring', 'Monitoring is tracking progress and resource use against plans, usually ongoing and internal.

• Systematic Assessment of Progress (SAP) - structured, periodic check to see if short-term goals are being met and whether the project logic remains sound
• Evaluation - determining relevance, effectiveness, impact, and efficiency of the project, often periodic or end-of-cycle
• Sustainability - ensuring benefits continue after the program''s funding or external support ends', '["Monitoring","Systematic Assessment of Progress","Evaluation","Sustainability"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T10:52:22.872Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:52:22.872Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:52:22.872Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754294871679-131', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Depends on decision-making structures at the community level to allocate program goods or services effectively according to the criteria as defined in the program objectives.', 'Community-based', 'Community-based uses local knowledge and consensus (e.g., councils) to select beneficiaries.

• Administrative - uses official records and pre-determined criteria (e.g., income data, public registries).
• Self-targeting - uses program design (e.g., low-quality food, hard labor requirement) to make the benefit unattractive', '["Administrative","Community-based","Self-targeting","Market-based"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T12:55:51.323Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T12:55:51.323Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T12:55:51.502Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754294765749-130', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'A method of delivering goods and/or services to a selected group of individuals or households rather than to every individual or household in the population.', 'Targeting', 'Targeting is defined as directing program benefits to a specifically selected subgroup rather than universally to the entire population. 

• Prioritizing of beneficiaries is a related but broader concept describing the ranking of need, not the delivery mechanism. 
• Sampling refers to a research/survey selection method, not a program service delivery approach. 
• Identification and selection of clients is part of the targeting process but does not capture the full definition of the delivery method as precisely as "targeting" does.', '["Prioritizing of beneficiaries","Sampling","Identification and selection of clients","Targeting"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T13:52:15.731Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T13:52:15.731Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T13:52:15.923Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754294224925-125', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Focal persons for nutrition at the local levels are:', 'BNS, CNAO, MNAO, PNAO', 'Regional nutrition focal points/officers serve national/sub-national levels.

• BNS, CNAO, MNAO, PNAO, RNAO - national level
• BNS, CNAO, MNAO, PNAO, RNPC - national level
• BNS, CNPC, MNPC, PNPC, RNPC - national level', '["BNS, CNAO, MNAO, PNAO, RNAO","BNS, CNAO, MNAO, PNAO, RNPC","BNS, CPNC, MNPC, PNPC, RNPC","BNS, CNAO, MNAO, PNAO"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T09:24:00.428Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:24:00.428Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:24:00.428Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754294137080-124', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Local nutrition action plans (LNAP) serves as the mechanism to achieve nutrition goals at the city/municipal/provincial level. It should be harmonized in the local development system and plans, EXCEPT:', 'Environmental Impact Assessment', 'Environmental Impact Assessment is a project-specific environmental review process, not one of the standard local development planning documents that the Local Nutrition Action Plan (LNAP) is meant to be harmonized with. 

The Comprehensive Land Use Plan, Executive Legislative Agenda, and Comprehensive Development Plan are all standard local government planning documents that the LNAP should align with to ensure nutrition is mainstreamed into broader development planning and budgeting processes.', '["Comprehensive Land Use Plan","Environmental Impact Assessment","Executive Legislative Agenda","Comprehensive Development Plan"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T08:20:34.639Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:20:34.639Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:20:34.962Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754293882457-123', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Local nutrition committees are chaired by the following local chief executives, EXCEPT:', 'Congressmen', 'Congressmen are national legislative officials, not local chief executives, and therefore do not chair Local Nutrition Committees. 

Barangay Captains, Mayors, and Governors are all local chief executives who chair LNCs at their respective barangay, city/municipal, and provincial levels.', '["Barangay Captains","Mayors","Governors","Congressmen"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T10:19:00.812Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:19:00.812Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:19:00.812Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754293803929-122', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Mechanism for planning, implementing, monitoring, evaluating, and coordinating the local plans of action for nutrition at the province, city/municipality, and barangay levels.', 'Local Nutrition Committees', 'Local Nutrition Committees (LNCs) serve as multi-function coordinating role across all local government levels in the Philippines, chaired by the respective local chief executive, and the basic functional unit of the nutrition program implementation and management.

See more here: https://nnc.gov.ph/mindanao-region/lnc-the-basic-functional-unit-of-the-nutrition-program/', '["Local Nutrition Committees","Local Nutrition Action Officers","Local Development Coordinators","Local Development Planning Team"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T15:29:34.922Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:29:34.922Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:29:35.140Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754293672217-121', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'The following are characteristics of nutrition-oriented development planning EXCEPT:', 'Malnutrition is merely a problem of food consumption and availability', 'Nutrition-oriented development planning explicitly recognizes malnutrition as a complex, multi-causal problem, not one reducible to just food consumption/availability alone. 

Nutrition being included as an objective integrated into development planning, diagnostic analysis used to identify causes, and nutrition actions applied across local/national and sectoral plans are all genuine, defining characteristics of this planning approach.', '["Malnutrition is merely a problem of food consumption and availability","Nutrition is included as an objective and integrated into development planning","Diagnostic analysis is used in identifying cause of malnutrition","Nutrition actions are applied in local and national levels; and in sectoral development plans"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T09:02:35.289Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:02:35.289Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:02:35.605Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754295800386-140', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Views malnutrition as a disease which has to be cured by therapeutic approaches', 'Public Health', '• Social Welfare - malnutrition as deprivation of social safety net
• Agriculture - malnutrition due to limited food production
• Education - malnutrition is due to poor nutrition knowledge and skills', '["Social Welfare","Public Health","Agriculture","Education"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T08:24:36.581Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:24:36.581Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:24:36.581Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754294432383-127', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Re-planning is a necessary step in nutrition program planning and management. In doing so, the following are revisited:', 'All of the above', 'Re-planning revisits the nutrition situation, the goals and objectives, and the strategies for targeting and implementing interventions together. Re-planning is triggered by monitoring and evaluation findings that suggest the current approach needs adjustment, and effective re-planning requires reassessing the full planning cycle.', '["Nutrition situation","Goals and objectives","Strategies in targeting for and implementation of nutrition interventions","All of the above"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T12:53:08.968Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T12:53:08.968Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T12:53:08.968Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754293495908-120', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Characterized mainly by a program already prepared by a group external to a community or environment. It may also mean top-down approach which is characterized mainly by the formulation of a plan at a higher level (e.g. national level), for implementation at a lower level (e.g. municipality or barangay).', 'Pre-Determined planning', 'Pre-determined planning is defined as a top-down approach where plans are formulated at a higher level (e.g., national) for implementation at a lower level (e.g., barangay), without the community''s initial input into design. 

• Self-determined planning instead involves the community itself formulating its own plan. 
• Joint planning involves collaboration between external and community stakeholders together. 
• Strategic planning refers to a broader planning methodology focused on long-term goal-setting.', '["Self-Determined planning","Pre-Determined planning","Joint planning","Strategic planning"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T07:48:55.869Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T07:48:55.869Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T07:48:55.869Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754293357865-119', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Which CMAM component treats children with SAM with poor appetite or medical complications?', 'Inpatient care', 'Inpatient care, which is specifically designated within the Community-based Management of Acute Malnutrition (CMAM) framework for children with severe acute malnutrition (SAM) who present with poor appetite (failed appetite test) or medical complications requiring more intensive, facility-based treatment. 

• Outpatient care is instead used for SAM children who pass the appetite test and have no medical complications, allowing home-based management with ready-to-use therapeutic food.
• Home care and community care are not standard, formally defined CMAM components matching this specific clinical criterion.', '["Inpatient care","Outpatient care","Home care","Community care"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T10:58:35.422Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:58:35.422Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:58:35.607Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754293288222-118', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'What is/are the priority foods source/s during the early emergency period?', 'Water and Calories', 'Water and calories are the two most immediately life-sustaining priorities in the very early phase of an emergency response. 

• Water alone is insufficient because caloric/energy needs are also urgently critical for survival. 
• Adding protein and further adding fat reflect priorities that become important slightly later, as the emergency response matures beyond the immediate survival phase into more complete dietary support.', '["Water","Water and Calories","Water, Calories, and Protein","Water, Calores, Protein, and Fat"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T10:01:23.598Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:01:23.598Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:01:23.598Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754293198155-117', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Which is a livelihood assistance program?', 'Lingap sa mahirap', 'Lingap sa Mahirap: A historical, comprehensive poverty alleviation fund introduced during the Estrada administration targeting the 100 poorest families in every province and city to deliver integrated social welfare packages.

• Tindahan Natin Program (TNP): This is a national government initiative implemented by the Department of Social Welfare and Development (DSWD). It serves as a livelihood assistance and job generation project alongside working as a targeted food price subsidy. It provides micro-financing and starter capital for low-income individuals, barangay councils, or community groups to set up small grocery stores (tindahan) that sell low-priced, quality food items like NFA rice and noodles.
• Ginintuang Masaganang Ani: An overarching agricultural modernization program run by the Department of Agriculture (DA) focused on boosting crop productivity, farm technology, and national food sufficiency.
• Sustansya para sa Masa: A multi-sectoral national movement launched to combat malnutrition through public food fortification strategies, such as adding Vitamin A to localized products.', '["Ginintuang masaganang ani","Lingap sa mahirap","Sustansya para sa masa","Tindahan natin"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T09:38:39.302Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:38:39.302Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:38:39.302Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1754293131141-116', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', '____ is an information-sharing type of activity that provides nutrition information to 10-12 participating mothers who are seated in a circular position', 'Pabasa sa nutrisyon', 'Pabasa sa Nutrisyon (PSN) is an information-sharing nutrition education initiative developed by the Nutrition Center of the Philippines (NCP). It is traditionally formatted as a community course where small groups of around 10 to 12 target mothers or caregivers sit in a circular arrangement to comfortably read, learn from standard nutritional guidelines, and share personal child-rearing experiences.

• Nutribus - 1980’s Nutrition Education using a bus.
• TCP - Teacher Child Parent Approach - The Teacher-Child-Parent approach to nutrition is a collaborative strategy where teachers, parents, and other community members work together to promote and improve children''s nutrition through consistent education and support
• Kumare - (Kalusugan para Umunlad si Mare) is a maternal health program designed to improve the delivery of much-needed iron supplements to pregnant women. This approach increases the number of prenatal visits, the number of iron tablets consumed, and improved hemoglobin levels. The intervention is anchored on training and re-orientation of health workers by giving them more responsibility for the mothers in their catchment area.', '["Nutribus","Pabasa sa nutrisyon","TCP","Kumare"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T09:17:05.810Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:17:05.810Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.310Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:17:06.133Z"'::jsonb)
