She established hospital dietetics standards in the Philippines and was the first Chief Dietitian of Philippine General Hospital in 1952. Moreover, she was one of the first nutrition majors (BSHE) to graduate from UP alongside Magdalena Lerma.', '', '["Irma Florentin or Preciosa Irma Pineda-Florentin\n\nShe established hospital dietetics standards in the Philippines and was the first Chief Dietitian of Philippine General Hospital in 1952. Moreover, she was one of the first nutrition majors (BSHE) to graduate from UP alongside Magdalena Lerma.","60% - Service oriented (1.67)\n50% - Government, hospital, schools (2.0)\n40% - Fast foods, cafeteria (2.5)\n33% - Profit-oriented (3)\n25% - Hotels, restaurant (4)\n29% - Catering functions (5)","Victor Hugo\n<img alt=\"Victor Hugo - Wikipedia\" src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" width=\"162\">","Accommodator caterers"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-18T20:00:00.000Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.491Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788431618901-6', 'anki-deck-1788431213230-1790433145985-sfnk4', 'Sirkele is a regional iteration of which popular local dish?', 'Dinuguan


Serkele is a hearty, soupy Filipino blood-based stew made with beef innards instead of pork. It originated in Baliwag, Bulacan.

Aling Luring (Leonila Castro-Trinidad) created the recipe in 1972 at her local snack shop. The name comes from the word "circle," describing how the sliced innards curl up while boiling.

<img alt="sirkele – Tita S Travels" src="data:image/jpeg;base64," width="220">', '', '["Sisig","Dinuguan","Bopis","Kilawin"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 4, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-08T20:00:00.000Z","interval":22,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.503Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
