('anki-card-1788431555320-5', 'anki-deck-1788431213230-1790433145985-sfnk4', 'Etag is a smoked meat traditionally made and used in cooking in _____.', 'CAR', 'Etag is a smoked meat traditionally made and used in cooking in the Cordillera region of the Philippines. It is usually made from slabs of pork (like belly or neck).<img alt="Etag – Pinoy Reads" src="data:image/jpeg;base64," width="200">The meat is cured heavily with salt and then air-dried or smoked over a wood fire for weeks or months. Locals often prefer wood from the alnus tree to give the meat a pleasant, aromatic smoke flavor.', '["CAR","Region II","Region I","Region III"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-12-16T07:06:54.286Z","interval":53,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T07:06:54.286Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.503Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T07:06:54.286Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788431664461-7', 'anki-deck-1788431213230-1790433145985-sfnk4', 'The meal concept known as “Banchan” is from which international cuisine', 'Korean', '<img alt="Banchan – Curious Foodies" src="data:image/jpeg;base64," width="200">Banchan are small Korean side dishes served in the middle of the table to share alongside cooked rice and soup.', '["Korean","Vietnamese","Japanese","Chinese"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'medium', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-12-06T07:07:20.316Z","interval":43,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T07:07:20.316Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.503Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T07:07:20.316Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788431685651-8', 'anki-deck-1788431213230-1790433145985-sfnk4', 'Which situation BEST illustrates the concept of time-temperature abuse in food safety?', 'Leaving potentially hazardous food in the temperature danger zone for an extended period', '', '["Storing raw chicken on the bottom shelf of the refrigerator","Using a separate chopping board for vegetables","Leaving potentially hazardous food in the temperature danger zone for an extended period","Washing a cutting board with hot water and soap after use"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'medium', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-12-06T07:06:16.519Z","interval":43,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T07:06:16.519Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.503Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T07:06:16.519Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788431809370-9', 'anki-deck-1788431213230-1790433145985-sfnk4', '<img alt="Manchego - Futura Foods" src="data:image/jpeg;base64," width="200">Manchego is a variant of hard cheese that originated from this European country.', 'Spain
Manchego cheese is made in the La Mancha region of Spain from the milk of Manchega sheep.


🇮🇹 Italy: Famous for Parmigiano-Reggiano (the "King of Cheeses") and Pecorino Romano, which is a sharp, salty hard cheese made from sheep''s milk, similar to Manchego.








🇫🇷 France: Famous for Comté and Beaufort, which are rich, nutty hard cheeses made from cow''s milk in the Alpine regions.




🇵🇹 Portugal: Famous for Queijo da Serra da Estrela and Queijo de Azeitão.', '', '["Italy","France","Spain","Portugal"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'medium', 3, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-06T20:00:00.000Z","interval":20,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.503Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788431412824-0', 'anki-deck-1788431213230-1790433145985-sfnk4', 'Which ingredient refers to the “K” in the abbreviated dish KBL?', 'Kadios', 'KBL in Ilonggo stands for Kadyos, Baboy, Langka, a famous traditional soup or stew from the Western Visayas region of the Philippines.<img alt="KBL (Kadyos, Baboy, at Langka) Recipe" src="data:image/jpeg;base64," width="200">', '["Kadios","Kamote","Kamias","Kalamay"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-12-16T07:06:05.123Z","interval":53,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T07:06:05.123Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.503Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T07:06:05.123Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788431434345-1', 'anki-deck-1788431213230-1790433145985-sfnk4', 'Which of the following BEST describes the primary goal of meal management?', 'Using resources effectively and efficiently to create meals', '', '["Preparing meals using the most expensive ingredients available","Using resources effectively and efficiently to create meals","Increasing the number of dishes served in every meal","Reducing preparation time regardless of nutritional quality"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'medium', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-12-11T07:07:38.438Z","interval":48,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T07:07:38.438Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.503Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T07:07:38.438Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1788431450436-2', 'anki-deck-1788431213230-1790433145985-sfnk4', 'A cook wants to minimize nutrient loss when preparing vegetables. Which practice is MOST consistent with the recommendations in the material?', 'Cook vegetables with as little water as possible', '', '["Soak thinly sliced vegetables in water before cooking","Cut vegetables into very small pieces","Cook vegetables with as little water as possible","Discard the cooking water immediately after boiling"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'medium', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-12-03T07:07:29.758Z","interval":40,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T07:07:29.758Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.503Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T07:07:29.758Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757210672852-214', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'What is the main difference between a cohort study and a case-control study in nutrition research?', 'A cohort study follows a group over time, while a case-control study looks back at past exposure', 'A cohort study follows a group forward over time (from exposure toward outcome), while a case-control study looks backward from an already-occurred outcome to past exposures.', '["A cohort study follows a group over time, while a case-control study looks back at past exposure","A cohort study involves intervention, while a case-control study does not","A cohort study is more expensive than a case-control study","A cohort study uses randomization, while a case-control study does not"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T12:50:46.996Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T12:50:46.996Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.510Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T12:50:46.996Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757210531659-213', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Which of the following is an example of a secondary data source in nutrition research?', 'Data collected from a nutrition surveillance system', 'Primary (newly collected)
Secondary (previously collected, reused)

• A newly conducted survey – primary
• Published research articles – secondary in a broader sense
• Results from a clinical trial – primary
• Data collected from a nutrition surveillance system – secondary from previously collected surveillance data with an ongoing, general monitoring purpose and later reused/reanalyzed by researchers', '["A newly conducted survey","Published research articles","Results from a clinical trial","Data collected from a nutrition surveillance system"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T07:54:36.202Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T07:54:36.202Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.510Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T07:54:36.202Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757210360551-211', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'The 2022 Expanded National Nutrition Survey (ENNS) was designed with a special purpose. What was this purpose?', 'To compare nutrition and health indicators before and during the pandemic', 'The correct answer is to compare nutrition and health indicators before and during the pandemic, reflecting the ENNS''s specific timing and design to capture the COVID-19 pandemic''s impact on the nutritional status of Filipinos.', '["To compare nutrition and health indicators before and during the pandemic","To assess the impact of climate change on food security","To evaluate the effectiveness of the national immunization program","To monitor the implementation of local government unit projects"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T15:05:55.363Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:05:55.363Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.510Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:05:55.363Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757209267185-201', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Which of the following is NOT a common method used to assess dietary intake in nutrition research?', 'Randomized controlled trial (RCT)', 'RCT is a study design not a dietary assessment method.', '["Diet record","24-hour recall","Food frequency questionnaire (FFQ)","Randomized controlled trial (RCT)"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T10:53:27.287Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:53:27.287Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.510Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:53:27.287Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757209369847-202', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'In nutrition research, what is the primary reason for using random sampling techniques?', 'To ensure every member of the population has an equal chance of selection', 'The correct answer is that random sampling ensures every member of the population has an equal chance of selection, allowing findings from the sample to be validly generalized to the broader population. 

• Choice A (saving time/resources) may be a secondary practical benefit but is not the primary scientific rationale. 
• Choice C (researcher convenience) actually describes convenience sampling, a non-random, less rigorous method. 
• Choice D (targeting specific dietary habits) describes purposive, non-random sampling, which serves a different research purpose.', '["To save time and resources","To ensure every member of the population has an equal chance of selection","To make the study more convenient for the researcher","To specifically target individuals with certain dietary habits"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 5, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-25T15:11:18.933Z","interval":27,"easeFactor":2.1,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T15:11:18.933Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.510Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T15:11:19.133Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757210243156-210', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'The survey highlighted a significant burden of malnutrition in the Philippines. Which of the following is NOT considered a form of malnutrition in the survey''s findings?', 'Diabetes', 'Diabetes - one of the NCDs; not a form of malnutrition', '["Stunting","Wasting","Obesity","Diabetes"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T07:56:00.161Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T07:56:00.161Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.510Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T07:56:00.470Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757210160377-209', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'What is the primary purpose of the Philippines National Nutrition Survey (2021-2023)?', 'To determine the nutritional status of Filipinos and identify areas of concern', 'To determine the nutritional status of Filipinos and identify areas of concern is the defining, core purpose of any national nutrition survey.', '["To assess the prevalence of infectious disease","To determine the nutritional status of Filipinos and identify areas of concern","To evaluate the effectiveness of the national health insurance program","To monitor the implementation of environmental protection policies"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T12:51:31.718Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T12:51:31.718Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.510Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T12:51:31.718Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757210032283-208', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'What is a key characteristic of a well-functioning nutrition surveillance system?', 'It provides information that is relevant, timely, and accessible for decision-making', 'A well-functioning system provides information that is relevant, timely, and accessible for decision-making, since data that arrives too late or is not actionable fails the core purpose of surveillance.

• It relies solely on data from clinical settings – incorrect; effective systems draw on multiple data sources, not clinical data alone.
• It focuses on individual nutritional assessments rather than population-level trends - incorrect; surveillance is specifically oriented toward population-level trends not individual assessments.
• It has a limited scope and only tracks a few indicators – incorrect; comprehensive systems typically track a broad and appropriately scoped set of indicators, not just a limited few.', '["It relies solely on data from clinical setting","It provides information that is relevant, timely, and accessible for decision-making","It focuses on individual nutritional assessments rather than population-level trends","It has a limited scope and only tracks a few indicators"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T08:14:42.767Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:14:42.767Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.510Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:14:42.767Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757209912506-207', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Which of the following best describes the role of a nutrition surveillance system in public health emergencies?', 'It can be used as an early warning system for food crises', 'Nutrition surveillance systems can be used as an early warning system for food crises, allowing timely detection of deteriorating food security or nutritional status before a full-blown crisis occurs.

• Choice A is incorrect because surveillance is valuable during both stable and emergency periods, not just stable ones. 
• Choice C is incorrect because surveillance is, highly useful for assessing disaster impact through rapid nutritional assessments. 
• Choice D is too narrow, since surveillance in emergencies focuses on acute malnutrition trends as well, not just chronic malnutrition..', '["It is relevant during stable periods","It can be used as an early warning system for food crises","It is not useful for assessing the impact of disasters","It focuses on tracking chronic malnutrition"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T08:18:32.116Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:18:32.116Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.510Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T08:18:32.116Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757209770611-206', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Which of the following is NOT typically a component of a nutrition surveillance system?', 'Assessing the availability of processed foods in supermarkets', 'The correct answer is assessing the availability of processed foods in supermarkets, because this is too narrow and specific to be a standard, defining component of surveillance systems.', '["Monitoring food consumption","Tracking changes in body weight and height (Anthropometry)","Assessing the availability of processed foods in supermarkets","Evaluating the effectiveness of nutrition education programs"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T08:23:44.062Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:23:44.062Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.510Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:23:44.253Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757210450697-212', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'What is the primary purpose of nutritional monitoring within a surveillance system?', 'To track changes in nutritional status over time within a population', 'To track changes in nutritional status over time within a population is the defining purpose of the "monitoring" function within a broader surveillance system.', '["To diagnose individual cases of malnutrition","To track changes in nutritional status over time within a population","To determine the optimal dietary intake for individuals","To provide immediate nutritional interventions"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T09:11:40.531Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:11:40.531Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.510Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:11:40.531Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757209675200-205', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Which of the following is the primary goal of a nutrition surveillance system?', 'To inform public health policies and interventions related to nutrition', 'The correct answer is to inform public health policies and interventions related to nutrition, which is the defining purpose of surveillance: continuous data collection specifically intended to guide decision-making.

• To diagnose individual nutritional deficiencies - surveillance systems track population trends, not individual diagnoses
• To monitor trends in food prices - only one possible component, not the overall goal
• To assess the nutritional status of individuals in a clinical setting - surveillance is population-based, not conducted in individual clinical settings.', '["To diagnose individual nutritional deficiencies","To monitor trends in food prices","To inform public health policies and interventions related to nutrition","To assess the nutritional status of individuals in a clinical setting"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T10:25:12.129Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:25:12.129Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.510Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:25:12.312Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757209572904-204', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Which of the following is NOT a typical component of a nutrition survey?', 'Randomized controlled trial design', 'Randomized controlled trial DESIGN is where researchers manipulate an independent variable (the intervention) and randomly assign participants to an intervention group or a control group, hence it is not a typical component of a nutrition survey.', '["Anthropometric measurements (height, weight, etc.)","Biochemical tests (blood or urine analysis)","Detailed clinical examination","Randomized controlled trial design"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T09:14:17.585Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:14:17.585Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.510Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:14:17.909Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757209179242-200', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'What is the main advantage of using randomized controlled trial (RCT) in nutrition research?', 'It enables researchers to control for confounding variables', 'The correct answer is: randomization allows researchers to control for confounding variables, both known and unknown.

• Choice A is incorrect because RCTs are typically better suited for shorter-term interventions, not long-term dietary pattern studies, which favor cohort designs.
• Choice C is false because RCTs are generally more expensive and time-consuming than observational designs. 
• Choice D overstates the claim; RCTs are the gold standard for causal inference but are not the "only way" to study nutrient-health relationships, since other designs also contribute evidence. The RCT''s defining strength is its ability to minimize both measured and unmeasured confounding through random allocation.', '["It allows for the study of long-term dietary patterns","It enables researchers to control for confounding variables","It is less expensive and time-consuming than other study designs","It is the only way to study the effects of specific nutrients on health"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T15:32:45.063Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:32:45.063Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.510Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:32:45.262Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757209484591-203', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'What is the primary purpose of nutrition survey in research?', 'To determine the prevelance of specific nutrient deficiencies in a population', 'The best answer is to determine the prevalence of specific nutrient deficiencies in a population, which is the classic, defining purpose of a population-based nutrition survey such as the National Nutrition Survey.

Choices A, C, and D describe purposes that a survey-type methodology could theoretically serve, but they are more specialized or unrelated to the core mission of nutrition surveys. Nutrition surveys generate the prevalence data that inform national policy and program planning.', '["To assess the effectiveness of a new weight loss drug","To determine the prevelance of specific nutrient deficiencies in a population","To compare the nutritional content of different brands of cereal","To evaluate the impact of a marketing campaign on consumer food choices"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T13:25:08.084Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T13:25:08.084Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.510Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T13:25:08.265Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757213173520-223', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'A public health nutritionist is developing a new community-based infant feeding program. Which of the following quality assurance (QA) procedures is most critical for ensuring the program''s long term effectiveness and sustainability, beyond a single evaluation cycle?', 'Establishing a continuous improvement (CQI) process that involves regular feedback loops from stakeholders and data-driven adjustments to program activities', 'The correct answer is establishing a continuous quality improvement (CQI) process involving regular feedback loops from stakeholders and data-driven adjustments to program activities, because CQI is specifically designed as an ongoing, cyclical process that sustains program quality and effectiveness well beyond any single evaluation point. 

• A one-time pre-post knowledge test captures only a single snapshot of educational outcomes, not ongoing sustainability. 
• A randomized controlled trial is a rigorous but typically one-time comparative research design, not an ongoing quality assurance mechanism. 
• An annual peer review provides periodic, but not truly continuous, quality checking and lacks the responsive feedback-loop mechanism central to CQI.', '["Conducting a pre-post knowledge test for all program participants to measure educational outcomes","Implementing a randomized trial to compare the new program''s outcomes against a standard intervention","Establishing a continuous improvement (CQI) process that involves regular feedback loops from stakeholders and data-driven adjustments to program activities","Performing an annual peer review of all materials and educational handouts to ensure scientific accuracy"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T10:02:54.044Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:02:54.044Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.510Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T10:02:54.044Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757212045271-219', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'In a rural community, a nutritionist identifies a high prevalence of iron-deficiency anemia among women of childbearing age. The community has a strong agricultural tradition and relies heavily on local produce of whole grains and legumes, but the soil lacks bioavailable iron. A pilot program introduces a new iron-fortified flour, but a year later, the anemia rates have not significantly improved. Applying the principles of community nutrition, what is the most plausible reason for the program''s failure?', 'The intervention failed to account for potential food-food interactions, as the community''s diet is high in phytates, which inhibit iron absorption.', 'The correct answer is that the intervention failed to account for food-food interactions, since the community''s diet is high in phytates (found abundantly in whole grains and legumes), which are well-known potent inhibitors of non-heme iron absorption, potentially neutralizing much of the benefit of the iron fortification.', '["The intervention failed to account for potential food-food interactions, as the community''s diet is high in phytates, which inhibit iron absorption.","The program did not employ a randomized controlled trial, making it impossible to accurately measure its impact on the target population.","The nutritionist did not adequately engage local political leaders, resulting in a lack of policy support for the program''s long-term sustainability.","The intervention was not tailored to the individual health needs of each participant, failing to address unique comorbidities that might interfere with iron absorption."]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T15:35:22.145Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:35:22.145Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.510Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:35:22.348Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757212954514-222', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'A public health nutritionist is invited to participate in a hospital-based team that manages the care of patients recently discharged from a cardia unit. The team includes a cardiologist, a registered nurse, a physical therapist, and a social worker. What term best described this type of collaborative effort, and what is its main objective?', 'Term: Interdisciplinary Team. Objective: To provide a holistic, integrated care plan by having team members work together and communicate about shared patient goals.', 'The correct answer is that this is an Interdisciplinary Team, whose objective is to provide a holistic, integrated care plan by having team members work together and communicate about shared patient goals, integrating their different disciplinary approaches into a coherent, unified methodology.', '["Term: Multidisciplinary Team. Objective: To provide comprehensive, coordinated care by having different professionals work independently on different aspects of the patient''s recovery.","Term: Interdisciplinary Team. Objective: To provide a holistic, integrated care plan by having team members work together and communicate about shared patient goals.","Term: Ad Hoc Team. Objective: To address a specific, short-term patient need, such as a single consultation, before the patient''s discharge.","Term: Transdisciplinary Team. Objective: To cross-train team members so they can perform tasks outside of their primary professional roles to increase efficiency."]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T15:29:16.906Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:29:16.906Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.510Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:29:17.105Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757212619610-221', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'A community health center provides comprehensive services including primary care, dental care, and a public health nutritionist. A patient with recently diagnosed pre-diabetes is referred by their primary care physician to the nutritionist for a consultation. In the scenario, what type of healthcare delivery model does this best represent, and what is the primary benefit for the patient?', 'Model: Integrated Healthcare System. Benefit: Coordinated care and communication between the physician and nutritionist are streamlined.', 'The correct answer is that this represents an Integrated Healthcare System, whose primary benefit is coordinated care and streamlined communication between the physician and nutritionist within the same facility/system. 

• Fee-for-service describes a payment model emphasizing provider choice, unrelated to the coordinated, in-house referral pathway described. 
• Specialized healthcare system would emphasize focused expert care in one narrow area, not the coordinated, multi-service nature of the scenario. 
• Direct primary care describes a flat-fee payment model for physician access, unrelated to the multidisciplinary, coordinated referral pattern described.', '["Model: Fee-for-Service. Benefit: The patient has a wide choice of providers.","Model: Integrated Healthcare System. Benefit: Coordinated care and communication between the physician and nutritionist are streamlined.","Model: Specialized Healthcare System. Benefit: The patient receives highly focused care from an expert in one specific area.","Model: Direct Primary Care. Benefit: The patient pays a flat monthly fee for unlimited access to the physician."]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T15:30:26.767Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:30:26.767Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.510Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:30:26.962Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757212310492-220', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'Which group of laws is related to each other:
I. RA 10862 - PD 2862 - RA 6760
II. EO 51 - RA 7600 - A.O. No. 2007-0026
III. EO 94 - EO 128 - EO 352
IV. PD 491 - EO 234 - A.O. 88 - EO 472
V. A.O. No. 2019-0033 - A.O. No. 2016-0020
VI. RA 8976 - RA 8172 - Department Memorandum No. 2012-0113
VII. A.O. #2015-0055 - A.O. #2010-00015 - A.O. #2009-0025 -  A.O. #2007-0045 - A.O. #2005-0014', 'All of the above', 'I. RA 10862 – PD 2862 – RA 6760 - RND laws
II. EO 51 (1987) - RA 7600 (1992) - A.O. No. 2007-0026 - Breastfeeding laws
III. EO 94 (1947) - EO 128 (1987) - EO 352 (1996) - FNRI
IV. PD 491 – EO 234 (1987) – AO 88 (1988) - EO 472 (1996) - NNC
V. A.O. No. 2019-0033 - A.O. No. 2016-0020 - NCP
VI. RA 8976 – RA 8172 - Department Memorandum No. 2012-0113 - Fortification
VII. AO # 2015-0055 - AO # 2010-00015 - AO # 2009-0025 - AO # 2007-0045 – AO # 2005-0014 - Maternal and Child Health', '["I, III, VII","II, IV, VI","All of the above","None of the above"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T07:50:47.843Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T07:50:47.843Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.510Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T07:50:47.843Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757211670090-218', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'A public health nutritionist is evaluating a long-standing food assistance program for pregnant women. The program has high participation rates, but a recent health survey shows that participants'' fruit and vegetable intake remains well below recommended levels. Which of the following principles of community nutrition is most likely being neglected, and what is the most appropriate next step?', 'Principle Neglected: Cultural competency. Next Step: Conduct focus groups with participants to understand their food preferences and dietary habits, and adjust the food packages accordingly.', 'The correct answer is that the principle neglected is cultural competency, and the appropriate next step is conducting focus groups to understand participants'' food preferences and dietary habits and adjusting food packages accordingly. 

High participation with persistently poor dietary outcomes suggests the food assistance being provided may not align with what participants actually want or will consistently consume, pointing to a cultural/preference mismatch rather than a participation or awareness problem.', '["Principle Neglected: Cultural competency. Next Step: Conduct focus groups with participants to understand their food preferences and dietary habits, and adjust the food packages accordingly.","Principle Neglected: Outcome-based evaluation. Next Step: Implement a more rigorous evaluation protocol to measure changes in health indicators like blood pressure and BMI.","Principle Neglected: Community empowerment. Next Step: Train participants to become peer-educators and advocates for healthy eating within their own social networks.","Principle Neglected: The ecological perspective. Next Step: Broaden the program to include a walking club and cooking demonstrations to address multiple factors influencing food choices."]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-11-01T08:33:18.632Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:33:18.632Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.510Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-29T08:33:18.811Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757211242642-217', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'According to the Philippine Nutrition and Dietetics Act of 2016 (RA 10862), which of the following is a specific function that a public health nutritionist-dietitian is mandated to perform in collaboration with other professionals?', 'Conducting nutrition program planning, implementation, and evaluation at a community or institutional level', 'The correct answer is conducting nutrition program planning, implementation, and evaluation at a community or institutional level, which falls within the legally mandated scope of practice for public health nutritionist-dietitians under the Philippine Nutrition and Dietetics Act of 2016 (RA 10862).', '["Prescribing specific drug medications for nutritional deficiencies","Leading a multidisciplinary team in a surgical ward","Conducting nutrition program planning, implementation, and evaluation at a community or institutional level","Owning and operating a food manufacturing company that produces fortified products"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T14:50:45.628Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T14:50:45.628Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.510Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T14:50:45.628Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757211070736-216', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'A community nutritionist is tasked with designing an intervention to reduce childhood obesity in a low-income urban neighborhood. A preliminary needs assessment revealed that the primary barriers are limited access to affordable, fresh produce and a lack of safe, accessible recreational spaces. According to the socio-ecological model and the principles of community nutrition, which of the following interventions would be most effective and sustainable?', 'Advocating for a city policy that provides incentives for mobile vendores to sell fresh produce in the neighborhood, while also collaborating with the parks and recreation department to improve a local playground', 'Advocating for a city policy incentivizing mobile produce vendors while also improving a local playground addresses multiple levels of the socio-ecological model (SEM) simultaneously: policy/environmental level (vendor incentives) and physical/community environment level (playground improvement), matching both identified barriers (limited produce access and lack of safe recreational space). 

• A nutrition education class alone addresses only the individual/interpersonal level, ignoring the structural access barriers identified in the assessment. 
• Partnering with a grocery store addresses food access but does not address the recreational space barrier. 
• A school-based program addresses only the school setting and misses the broader community-level access and environment barriers identified. 

The SEM framework explains how multiple levels of influence: from individual factors to broad social structures interact to determine a health outcome, such as malnutrition.', '["Implementing a weekly nutrition education for parents at a local community center.","Partnering with a local grocery store to create a \"healthy eating\" ailse and offering discount coupons for fruits and vegetables","Advocating for a city policy that provides incentives for mobile vendores to sell fresh produce in the neighborhood, while also collaborating with the parks and recreation department to improve a local playground","Developing a school-based program that offers free healthy snacks and incorporates a daily physical activity period"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T15:28:51.206Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:28:51.206Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.510Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T15:28:51.414Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1757210772996-215', 'anki-deck-1783608953857-1790433145942-e1oub', 'A key aspect of designing a nutrition surveillance system is to determine:', 'The specific population group to be monitored', 'The specific population group to be monitored is correct because defining the target population is a foundational design decision that shapes every other aspect of a surveillance system, including what indicators to collect and how. 

• The exact number of individuals to include is more of a sampling/statistical detail; 
• The optimal time of day for data collection and ideal food sample storage temperature are narrow, operational/logistical details.', '["The specific population group to be monitored","The exact number of individuals to be included in the study","The optimal time of day for data collection","The ideal temperature for storing food samples"]'::jsonb, '["General Dietetics"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-25T09:50:13.780Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:50:13.780Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.510Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-24T09:50:13.780Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756009053604-204', 'anki-deck-1783609287590-1790433139864-1mswi', 'To avoid discoloration of raw, cut-up fruits, immerse in:', 'Citrus
Ascorbic, citric, tartaric
Syrup (add sugar)', '', '["___ juice","Solutions of ___, ___, or ___ acids","___"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'medium', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","interval":11,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":4}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.583Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756013724749-222', 'anki-deck-1783609287590-1790433139864-1mswi', 'Least exercised muscles', 'Tender cuts', '', '["Tender cuts","Less tender cuts","Tough cuts","Retail cuts"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'medium', 3, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-27T20:00:00.000Z","interval":15,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":5}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.583Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756013553223-218', 'anki-deck-1783609287590-1790433139864-1mswi', 'Changes in meats after slaughter (post mortem):', '7-7.2 to 5.5', '', '["Immediately after death - muscle is pliant, soft, gel-like, extensive, and sticky; best to cook at this stage","Decrease in pH from __ to __ due to the formation of lactic acid anaerobically from glycogen."]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-14T20:00:00.000Z","interval":2,"easeFactor":2.35,"repetitions":7}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.583Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756013690316-221', 'anki-deck-1783609287590-1790433139864-1mswi', 'Example of this is "steak"', 'Retail cuts', '', '["Hind quarter","Forequarter","Retail cuts","Tough cuts"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'medium', 3, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-27T20:00:00.000Z","interval":15,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":3}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:32:30.583Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb)
