('anki-card-1756875742064-68', 'anki-deck-1783609405436-1790433139823-mldgr', 'The Labor Code of the Philippines is embodied in', 'PD 442
The Labor Code of the Philippines was enacted on May 1, 1974, through Presidential Decree No. 442. It serves as the primary law governing employment practices, labor relations, worker protection, and welfare across the country.


❌ PD 440: Tariff and Customs Code Amendment of 1974




❌ PD 540: Post Office Stamps Repeal of 1974



