<img alt="Nicolas Appert | Biography & Facts | Britannica" src="data:image/jpeg;base64," width="156">

❌ Delmonico: Refers to the Delmonico brothers, who established Delmonico''s in New York City, widely considered the first fine-dining restaurant in the United States.
❌ Louis Pasteur: A French chemist who later discovered why Appert''s method worked by proving that bacteria cause food spoilage, leading to the process of "pasteurization."
❌ Marie Antoine Carême: A legendary French chef known as the "King of Chefs and the Chef of Kings," famous for codifying the grand/high cuisine and creating the system of French mother sauces.', '', '["Nicolas Appert\n<img alt=\"Nicolas Appert | Biography & Facts | Britannica\" src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" width=\"156\">\n\n❌ Delmonico: Refers to the Delmonico brothers, who established Delmonico''s in New York City, widely considered the first fine-dining restaurant in the United States.\n❌ Louis Pasteur: A French chemist who later discovered why Appert''s method worked by proving that bacteria cause food spoilage, leading to the process of \"pasteurization.\"\n❌ Marie Antoine Carême: A legendary French chef known as the \"King of Chefs and the Chef of Kings,\" famous for codifying the grand/high cuisine and creating the system of French mother sauces.","invoice","It gives information on rules and regulations related to the job","to determine job satisfaction level of employees"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:35:40.426Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
