('anki-card-1756875844191-73', 'anki-deck-1783609405436-1790433139823-mldgr', 'As per Labor Code, the normal daily hours of work for any employee is', '8 hours', '', '["9 hours","8 hours","10 hours","12 hours"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:35:40.426Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756875877908-74', 'anki-deck-1783609405436-1790433139823-mldgr', '“Hours worked” as defined by the Labor Code, refers to', 'duty hours + short rest periods', '', '["duty hours + short rest periods","duty hours - short rest periods","duty hours + short rest periods + 1hr lunch break","duty hours + short rest periods - 1hr lunch break"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:35:40.426Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756875897688-75', 'anki-deck-1783609405436-1790433139823-mldgr', 'As per Labor Code, our overtime (OT) practice is  wrong if we  ____________', 'offset OT by going under time on another day', '', '["give at least 25% of regular wage as OT pay","offset OT by going under time on another day","ask employees to work OT in an emergency","give 40% of pay for OT work rendered"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:35:40.426Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756875914688-76', 'anki-deck-1783609405436-1790433139823-mldgr', 'As per Labor Code, which statement related to holidays is incorrect?', 'Companies w/ 5 or less employees are exempted from giving regular pay during regular holidays', '', '["Companies w/ 5 or less employees are exempted from giving regular pay during regular holidays","Compensation for employees working on holidays should be twice his regular rate","Employer determines employees’ schedule & weekly rest day","Religion should be considered in determining rest day"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:35:40.426Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1756875930222-77', 'anki-deck-1783609405436-1790433139823-mldgr', 'The following are functions of human resource management except ________', 'Developing standards for food and beverage', '', '["Recruiting potential employees","Screening applicants","Attracting potential job seekers to apply","Developing standards for food and beverage"]'::jsonb, '["Food Service Systems"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 1, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":0}'::jsonb, NULL, '"2026-09-26T14:35:40.426Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:32:12.431Z"'::jsonb),
('card-mnt-2', 'deck-clinical-mnt', 'What is the maximum osmolarity cutoff for Peripheral Parenteral Nutrition (PPN) infusion to avoid phlebitis?', '900 mOsm/L', 'Peripheral veins can tolerate solutions up to ~900 mOsm/L. Solutions exceeding 900 mOsm/L are hypertonic and must be infused via Central Parenteral Nutrition (CPN / TPN) through a large central vein (e.g., subclavian/jugular) where high blood flow rapidly dilutes the solution.', '["900 mOsm/L","500 mOsm/L","1500 mOsm/L","300 mOsm/L"]'::jsonb, '["Parenteral","Osmolarity","ICU"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-12T08:58:51.077Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-09T08:58:51.077Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:47:19.752Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-09T08:58:51.170Z"'::jsonb),
('card-mnt-4', 'deck-clinical-mnt', 'Which specific storage protein (prolamin) in wheat triggers the autoimmune enteropathy in Celiac Disease?', 'Gliadin', 'Celiac disease is triggered by the ingestion of gluten prolamins: Gliadin in wheat, Secalin in rye, and Hordein in barley. These induce immune-mediated small intestinal mucosal inflammation and villous atrophy.', '["Gliadin","Glutenin","Casein","Zein"]'::jsonb, '["GI","Celiac","Gluten"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-12T08:58:54.785Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-09T08:58:54.785Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:47:19.752Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-09T08:58:54.878Z"'::jsonb),
('card-mnt-1', 'deck-clinical-mnt', 'What is the recommended protein intake for a non-dialysis Chronic Kidney Disease (CKD) patient in Stage 4 (GFR 15–29 mL/min)?', '0.6 to 0.8 g/kg body weight/day', 'For CKD Stages 3–5 (non-dialysis), protein is restricted to 0.6–0.8 g/kg/day to slow renal disease progression and decrease uremic toxin accumulation. Once on hemodialysis, protein requirement increases to 1.2–1.4 g/kg/day due to dialysate losses.', '["0.6 to 0.8 g/kg body weight/day","1.2 to 1.4 g/kg body weight/day","1.5 to 2.0 g/kg body weight/day","0.3 to 0.5 g/kg body weight/day"]'::jsonb, '["CKD","Renal","Protein"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'medium', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-12T08:58:46.647Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-09T08:58:46.647Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:47:19.752Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-09T08:58:46.741Z"'::jsonb),
('card-mnt-3', 'deck-clinical-mnt', 'What is the classic dietary fat to combined carbohydrate + protein ratio used in the Ketogenic Diet for refractory pediatric epilepsy?', '4:1 (or 3:1) ratio', 'The classic ketogenic diet uses a 4:1 ratio of fat (in grams) to combined carbohydrate and protein (in grams), providing ~90% of calories from fat to induce and sustain ketosis, providing ketone bodies (beta-hydroxybutyrate) as the primary cerebral fuel.', '["4:1 (or 3:1) ratio","1:1 ratio","2:1 ratio","5:2 ratio"]'::jsonb, '["Pediatric","Epilepsy","Ketogenic"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'medium', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-12T08:58:43.667Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-09T08:58:43.667Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:47:19.752Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-09T08:58:43.767Z"'::jsonb),
('card-mnt-5', 'deck-clinical-mnt', 'What sodium limit is recommended in the strict DASH (Dietary Approaches to Stop Hypertension) diet trial?', '1,500 mg/day (Lower limit) or 2,300 mg/day (Standard)', 'The standard DASH diet limits sodium to 2,300 mg/day, while the lower-sodium DASH plan caps sodium at 1,500 mg/day. It emphasizes potassium, calcium, magnesium, fiber, and lean proteins.', '["1,500 mg/day (Lower limit) or 2,300 mg/day (Standard)","500 mg/day","3,500 mg/day","1,000 mg/day max"]'::jsonb, '["Cardiovascular","Hypertension","DASH"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'easy', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-12T08:58:48.948Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-09T08:58:48.948Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-26T14:47:19.752Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-09T08:58:49.031Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758693637557-193', 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'Refer to the case below: A 35-year-old diabetic teacher went to the Nutrition Clinic for counseling. She is 5’4” tall andweighs 86 kg. She enrolled in a gymnasium and tried taking special slimming teas but she onlyexperienced hypoglycemia. She never lost a pound, instead gained weight. Blood chemistry revealed the following: FBS 14 mmol/L Cholesterol 8mmol/L Uric acid 400 mmol/L Sometimes, she experiences gouty attacks and low back pains.
What would be the best protein requirement? *', '55 g', '1. Calculate the Desirable Body Weight (DBW):
	• Convert height to centimeters: 5 feet 4 inches = 64 inches.
	• 64 inches x 2.54 cm/inch = 162.56 cm
	• Use Tannhauser’s Method (the standard method utilized in Philippine board exams):
		• DBW (kg) = (Height in cm - 100) - 10%
		• Base weight = 162.56 - 100 = 62.56 kg
		• Deduct 10%: 62.56 - 6.25 = 56.31 kg
	• Rounding off the DBW gives approximately 55 kg.

2. Determine the Protein Requirement:
	• For an adult with diabetes and normal renal function, the standard nutritional care plan uses a baseline allowance of 1.0 gram of protein per kilogram of DBW per day.
	• Total Protein Required = 55 kg DBW x 1.0 g/kg = 55 grams

Because her blood work reveals elevated uric acid (400 mmol/L) and she experiences gouty attacks, keeping the protein requirement at a controlled, standard adult level of 1.0 g/kg (rather than high-protein or upper-range clinical levels) helps manage purine intake while protecting kidney health.', '["55 g","50 g","65 g","60 g"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, 'For a female who is 5''4" (162.5 cm), the estimated DBW using standard clinical formulas (like Tannhauser''s method) is approximately 55 to 56 kg. The baseline recommendation for a patient with controlled/early-stage conditions is 1.0 gram of protein per kilogram of DBW per day. The patient has an elevated uric acid level of 400 µmol/L and suffers from acute gouty attacks. Keeping protein at a conservative, adequate baseline of 55 g (roughly 15% of her target therapeutic energy requirement) prevents excessive purine load from animal proteins while providing enough essential amino acids to protect muscle mass during weight loss. ', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-29T16:24:31.803Z","interval":1,"easeFactor":2.3,"repetitions":1}'::jsonb, '"2026-10-28T16:24:31.803Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T11:40:39.332Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-10-28T16:24:31.978Z"'::jsonb),
('anki-card-1758690294177-28', 'anki-deck-1758689429896-1790185671252', 'An amino acid that can form a special covalent bond called a disulfide bond: *', 'cysteine', '', '["cysteine","tyrosine","lysine","methionine"]'::jsonb, '["Nutritional Biochemistry"]'::jsonb, NULL, 'hard', 2, '', '{"dueDate":"2026-10-01T10:44:24.824Z","interval":3,"easeFactor":2.5,"repetitions":2}'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T10:44:24.824Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T11:40:39.332Z"'::jsonb, '"2026-09-28T10:44:24.824Z"'::jsonb),
