('mc:also known as vitamin h.:::biotin', 'also known as vitamin h.', 'Biotin', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Vitamin H is another name for biotin, which is also known as vitamin B7. The \"H\" comes from the German words \"Haar und Haut,\" which mean hair and skin. It helps maintain healthy hair, skin, and nails.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Biotin\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Vitamin H is another name for biotin, which is also known as vitamin B7. The \"H\" comes from the German words \"Haar und Haut,\" which mean hair and skin. It helps maintain healthy hair, skin, and nails.\n\nBiotin is also known as Vitamin B7, Coenzyme R, Bios I, and anti-egg white injury factor.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Riboflavin, Anti-vitamins, Carnitine"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:german global online food delivery marketplace that allows customers to directly order meals online or via mobile.:::foodpanda', 'german global online food delivery marketplace that allows customers to directly order meals online or via mobile.', 'Foodpanda', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Foodpanda is an online food and grocery delivery platform brand owned by Delivery Hero, which is headquartered in Berlin, Germany and operates with 20 brands in about 50 countries across four continents. The Foodpanda brand, currently used in Asia, Bulgaria and Romania, was acquired by Delivery Hero in December 2016.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Foodpanda\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Foodpanda is an online food and grocery delivery platform brand owned by Delivery Hero, which is headquartered in Berlin, Germany and operates with 20 brands in about 50 countries across four continents. The Foodpanda brand, currently used in Asia, Bulgaria and Romania, was acquired by Delivery Hero in December 2016.\n\n• Honestbee was an online grocery and food delivery service based in Singapore.\n• Munchpunch is a food discovery and restaurant directory website based in the Philippines.\n• AmazonFresh is a grocery delivery service owned by the American tech giant Amazon.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Honestbee, Munchpunch"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:german global online food delivery marketplace that allows customers to directly order meals online or via mobile.:::', 'german global online food delivery marketplace that allows customers to directly order meals online or via mobile.', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Foodpanda is an online food and grocery delivery platform brand owned by Delivery Hero, which is headquartered in Berlin, Germany and operates with 20 brands in about 50 countries across four continents. The Foodpanda brand, currently used in Asia, Bulgaria and Romania, was acquired by Delivery Hero in December 2016.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Foodpanda\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Foodpanda is an online food and grocery delivery platform brand owned by Delivery Hero, which is headquartered in Berlin, Germany and operates with 20 brands in about 50 countries across four continents. The Foodpanda brand, currently used in Asia, Bulgaria and Romania, was acquired by Delivery Hero in December 2016.\n\n• Honestbee was an online grocery and food delivery service based in Singapore.\n• Munchpunch is a food discovery and restaurant directory website based in the Philippines.\n• AmazonFresh is a grocery delivery service owned by the American tech giant Amazon.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Honestbee, Munchpunch"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:decision-making guides that are written to ensure that all actions taken by organization members are consistent with the organization''s strategy and objectives.:::policies', 'decision-making guides that are written to ensure that all actions taken by organization members are consistent with the organization''s strategy and objectives.', 'Policies', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"In organizational management and foodservice planning, policies function as comprehensive, high-level decision-making guides. Rather than telling employees exactly what to do step-by-step, they establish a reliable boundaries framework. This ensures that every independent decision or action made by staff members stays completely aligned with the company’s broad strategy, vision, and core objectives.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Policies\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"In organizational management and foodservice planning, policies function as comprehensive, high-level decision-making guides. Rather than telling employees exactly what to do step-by-step, they establish a reliable boundaries framework. This ensures that every independent decision or action made by staff members stays completely aligned with the company’s broad strategy, vision, and core objectives.\n\n• Rules: These are strict, specific, and inflexible directives that dictate exactly what must or must not be done in a given situation (e.g., \"No smoking in the kitchen\"). They leave zero room for individual decision-making or managerial discretion.\n• Operating plans: These are short-term, detailed tactical blueprints that outline specific tasks, timelines, schedules, and budgets to execute operations over a precise period (such as weekly or monthly outputs).\n• Standing plans: This is a broad, overarching category of plans designed to be used repeatedly for recurring organizational activities. Standing plans include policies, procedures, and rules collectively, making it too broad of a classification to serve as the definition for a targeted decision-making guide.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Rules, Standing plans, Operating plans"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:decision-making guides that are written to ensure that all actions taken by organization members are consistent with the organization''s strategy and objectives.:::', 'decision-making guides that are written to ensure that all actions taken by organization members are consistent with the organization''s strategy and objectives.', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"In organizational management and foodservice planning, policies function as comprehensive, high-level decision-making guides. Rather than telling employees exactly what to do step-by-step, they establish a reliable boundaries framework. This ensures that every independent decision or action made by staff members stays completely aligned with the company’s broad strategy, vision, and core objectives.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Policies\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"In organizational management and foodservice planning, policies function as comprehensive, high-level decision-making guides. Rather than telling employees exactly what to do step-by-step, they establish a reliable boundaries framework. This ensures that every independent decision or action made by staff members stays completely aligned with the company’s broad strategy, vision, and core objectives.\n\n• Rules: These are strict, specific, and inflexible directives that dictate exactly what must or must not be done in a given situation (e.g., \"No smoking in the kitchen\"). They leave zero room for individual decision-making or managerial discretion.\n• Operating plans: These are short-term, detailed tactical blueprints that outline specific tasks, timelines, schedules, and budgets to execute operations over a precise period (such as weekly or monthly outputs).\n• Standing plans: This is a broad, overarching category of plans designed to be used repeatedly for recurring organizational activities. Standing plans include policies, procedures, and rules collectively, making it too broad of a classification to serve as the definition for a targeted decision-making guide.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Rules, Standing plans, Operating plans"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:limiting amino acid in rice::::lysine', 'limiting amino acid in rice:', 'Lysine', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Lysine, the main limiting essential amino acid in cereals, restricts the absorption and utilization of other amino acids and proteins, which leads to nutrient deficiency.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Lysine\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Lysine, the main limiting essential amino acid in cereals, restricts the absorption and utilization of other amino acids and proteins, which leads to nutrient deficiency.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Tryptophan, Methionine, Tyrosine"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:also known as vitamin h.:::', 'also known as vitamin h.', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Vitamin H is another name for biotin, which is also known as vitamin B7. The \"H\" comes from the German words \"Haar und Haut,\" which mean hair and skin. It helps maintain healthy hair, skin, and nails.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Biotin\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Vitamin H is another name for biotin, which is also known as vitamin B7. The \"H\" comes from the German words \"Haar und Haut,\" which mean hair and skin. It helps maintain healthy hair, skin, and nails.\n\nBiotin is also known as Vitamin B7, Coenzyme R, Bios I, and anti-egg white injury factor.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Riboflavin, Anti-vitamins, Carnitine"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:a function of management that involves developing in broad outline the activities required to accomplish the objectives of the organization and the most effective ways of doing so. it is a continuous process and requires that management be diligent in conducting periodic reviews of all plans to ensure that they are still appropriate as conditions change.:::planning', 'a function of management that involves developing in broad outline the activities required to accomplish the objectives of the organization and the most effective ways of doing so. it is a continuous process and requires that management be diligent in conducting periodic reviews of all plans to ensure that they are still appropriate as conditions change.', 'Planning', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"In management theory, planning is universally recognized as the foundational function that involves determining the organization''s goals and charting out a broad outline of activities and strategies to achieve them.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Planning\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"In management theory, planning is universally recognized as the foundational function that involves determining the organization''s goals and charting out a broad outline of activities and strategies to achieve them.\n\nBecause business and environmental conditions constantly shift, planning cannot be a one-time task. It requires an ongoing, continuous process where managers regularly review, adjust, and adapt their roadmaps to ensure the organization stays on track.\n\n• Marketing: The function focused on identifying, anticipating, and satisfying customer needs through product design, pricing, promotion, and distribution.\n• Finance: The function responsible for managing the organization''s monetary resources, budgeting, and capital allocations.\n• Operations: The function that deals with the daily execution, transformation of inputs into outputs, and physical manufacturing or service delivery processes.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Marketing, Finance, Operations"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:a function of management that involves developing in broad outline the activities required to accomplish the objectives of the organization and the most effective ways of doing so. it is a continuous process and requires that management be diligent in conducting periodic reviews of all plans to ensure that they are still appropriate as conditions change.:::', 'a function of management that involves developing in broad outline the activities required to accomplish the objectives of the organization and the most effective ways of doing so. it is a continuous process and requires that management be diligent in conducting periodic reviews of all plans to ensure that they are still appropriate as conditions change.', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"In management theory, planning is universally recognized as the foundational function that involves determining the organization''s goals and charting out a broad outline of activities and strategies to achieve them.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Planning\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"In management theory, planning is universally recognized as the foundational function that involves determining the organization''s goals and charting out a broad outline of activities and strategies to achieve them.\n\nBecause business and environmental conditions constantly shift, planning cannot be a one-time task. It requires an ongoing, continuous process where managers regularly review, adjust, and adapt their roadmaps to ensure the organization stays on track.\n\n• Marketing: The function focused on identifying, anticipating, and satisfying customer needs through product design, pricing, promotion, and distribution.\n• Finance: The function responsible for managing the organization''s monetary resources, budgeting, and capital allocations.\n• Operations: The function that deals with the daily execution, transformation of inputs into outputs, and physical manufacturing or service delivery processes.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Marketing, Finance, Operations"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:the main goal of staff orientation program::::communicate information and create response to the company and the job', 'the main goal of staff orientation program:', 'communicate information and create response to the company and the job', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Staff orientation is done to help recently hired staff in adjusting to their new employer. It gives staff members the fundamental organizational knowledge and serves as a venue for the employees to solicit responses about their new team, division, and job within the firm.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"communicate information and create response to the company and the job\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Staff orientation is done to help recently hired staff in adjusting to their new employer. It gives staff members the fundamental organizational knowledge and serves as a venue for the employees to solicit responses about their new team, division, and job within the firm.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: establish a system of discipline and rewards for the staff, establish training plan and method for evaluation progress, assess the reaction of other workers to the new worker"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:the main goal of staff orientation program::::', 'the main goal of staff orientation program:', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Staff orientation is done to help recently hired staff in adjusting to their new employer. It gives staff members the fundamental organizational knowledge and serves as a venue for the employees to solicit responses about their new team, division, and job within the firm.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"communicate information and create response to the company and the job\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Staff orientation is done to help recently hired staff in adjusting to their new employer. It gives staff members the fundamental organizational knowledge and serves as a venue for the employees to solicit responses about their new team, division, and job within the firm.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: establish a system of discipline and rewards for the staff, establish training plan and method for evaluation progress, assess the reaction of other workers to the new worker"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:chemical precursors of vitamins that are converted within the body to active vitamins.:::provitamins', 'chemical precursors of vitamins that are converted within the body to active vitamins.', 'Provitamins', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Provitamins are inactive substances that the body can convert into active vitamins through normal metabolic processes. A classic example is beta-carotene, which the human body converts into active Vitamin A in the intestinal wall.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Provitamins\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Provitamins are inactive substances that the body can convert into active vitamins through normal metabolic processes. A classic example is beta-carotene, which the human body converts into active Vitamin A in the intestinal wall.\n\n• Tetrahydrofolate is already an active, coenzyme form of Vitamin B9 (folate), rather than a precursor.\n• Anti-vitamins are chemical compounds that inhibit the absorption or metabolic actions of vitamins.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Anti-vitamins, Previtamins, Tertrahydrofolate"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:chemical precursors of vitamins that are converted within the body to active vitamins.:::', 'chemical precursors of vitamins that are converted within the body to active vitamins.', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Provitamins are inactive substances that the body can convert into active vitamins through normal metabolic processes. A classic example is beta-carotene, which the human body converts into active Vitamin A in the intestinal wall.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Provitamins\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Provitamins are inactive substances that the body can convert into active vitamins through normal metabolic processes. A classic example is beta-carotene, which the human body converts into active Vitamin A in the intestinal wall.\n\n• Tetrahydrofolate is already an active, coenzyme form of Vitamin B9 (folate), rather than a precursor.\n• Anti-vitamins are chemical compounds that inhibit the absorption or metabolic actions of vitamins.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Anti-vitamins, Previtamins, Tertrahydrofolate"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:the energy-releasing process by which large molecules are broken down to form smaller molecules is::::catabolism', 'the energy-releasing process by which large molecules are broken down to form smaller molecules is:', 'Catabolism', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Catabolism is the branch of metabolism specifically responsible for breaking down complex, large molecules (such as carbohydrates, proteins, and lipids) into smaller, simpler units. This degradation process releases energy, which cells capture and store primarily in the form of ATP.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Catabolism\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Catabolism is the branch of metabolism specifically responsible for breaking down complex, large molecules (such as carbohydrates, proteins, and lipids) into smaller, simpler units. This degradation process releases energy, which cells capture and store primarily in the form of ATP.\n\n• Anabolism is the exact opposite; it uses energy to build large molecules from smaller ones.\n• Metabolism is the overarching term that combines both catabolism and anabolism.\n• Glycolysis is a specific metabolic pathway that breaks down glucose, meaning it is an example of a catabolic process rather than the general definition.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Anabolism, Metabolism, Glycolysis"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:the energy-releasing process by which large molecules are broken down to form smaller molecules is::::', 'the energy-releasing process by which large molecules are broken down to form smaller molecules is:', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Catabolism is the branch of metabolism specifically responsible for breaking down complex, large molecules (such as carbohydrates, proteins, and lipids) into smaller, simpler units. This degradation process releases energy, which cells capture and store primarily in the form of ATP.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Catabolism\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Catabolism is the branch of metabolism specifically responsible for breaking down complex, large molecules (such as carbohydrates, proteins, and lipids) into smaller, simpler units. This degradation process releases energy, which cells capture and store primarily in the form of ATP.\n\n• Anabolism is the exact opposite; it uses energy to build large molecules from smaller ones.\n• Metabolism is the overarching term that combines both catabolism and anabolism.\n• Glycolysis is a specific metabolic pathway that breaks down glucose, meaning it is an example of a catabolic process rather than the general definition.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Anabolism, Metabolism, Glycolysis"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:which of the following is not considered a micromineral?:::', 'which of the following is not considered a micromineral?', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Chlorine is a macronutrient mineral present in amounts greater than 5g.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Chlorine\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Chlorine is a macronutrient mineral present in amounts greater than 5g.\n\nChlorine is classified as a macromineral (major mineral). Macrominerals are required by the body in large quantities (greater than 100 mg per day), alongside calcium, sodium, and potassium. Therefore, it is not a micromineral.\n\n• Copper, Zinc, and Iron: Both of these are classic examples of essential microminerals (trace minerals) required by the body in very small quantities.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Iron, Copper, Zinc"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:a 6-carbon vitamin compound closely related to the monosaccharide glucose.:::vit b6', 'a 6-carbon vitamin compound closely related to the monosaccharide glucose.', 'Vit B6', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Vitamin B6 (specifically its vitamer Pyridoxine) is a 6-carbon compound (chemical formula: C₈H₁₁NO₃) containing a pyridine ring with six ring carbons. It has key structural similarities and functional relationships with glucose metabolism (e.g., serving as an essential cofactor for glycogen phosphorylase to break down glycogen into glucose units).","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Vit B6\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Vitamin B6 (specifically its vitamer Pyridoxine) is a 6-carbon compound (chemical formula: C₈H₁₁NO₃) containing a pyridine ring with six ring carbons. It has key structural similarities and functional relationships with glucose metabolism (e.g., serving as an essential cofactor for glycogen phosphorylase to break down glycogen into glucose units).\n\n• Note on Vitamin C: While Vitamin C (Ascorbic acid) is the classic 6-carbon vitamin structurally derived directly from and most closely resembling the monosaccharide glucose (C₆H₈O₆), it is not listed among the given options. Among the choices provided, Vitamin B6 matches the 6-carbon molecular framework constraint.\n• Vitamin B12 is an extremely large, complex organometallic compound containing dozens of carbons and a cobalt core.\n• Vitamins D₂ and D₃ are large Secosteroid structural variants containing over 27 carbons.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Vit B12, Vit D2, Vit D3"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:a 6-carbon vitamin compound closely related to the monosaccharide glucose.:::', 'a 6-carbon vitamin compound closely related to the monosaccharide glucose.', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Vitamin B6 (specifically its vitamer Pyridoxine) is a 6-carbon compound (chemical formula: C₈H₁₁NO₃) containing a pyridine ring with six ring carbons. It has key structural similarities and functional relationships with glucose metabolism (e.g., serving as an essential cofactor for glycogen phosphorylase to break down glycogen into glucose units).","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Vit B6\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Vitamin B6 (specifically its vitamer Pyridoxine) is a 6-carbon compound (chemical formula: C₈H₁₁NO₃) containing a pyridine ring with six ring carbons. It has key structural similarities and functional relationships with glucose metabolism (e.g., serving as an essential cofactor for glycogen phosphorylase to break down glycogen into glucose units).\n\n• Note on Vitamin C: While Vitamin C (Ascorbic acid) is the classic 6-carbon vitamin structurally derived directly from and most closely resembling the monosaccharide glucose (C₆H₈O₆), it is not listed among the given options. Among the choices provided, Vitamin B6 matches the 6-carbon molecular framework constraint.\n• Vitamin B12 is an extremely large, complex organometallic compound containing dozens of carbons and a cobalt core.\n• Vitamins D₂ and D₃ are large Secosteroid structural variants containing over 27 carbons.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Vit B12, Vit D2, Vit D3"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb)
ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
