('mc:the following are antioxidant vitamin except::::vitamin k', 'the following are antioxidant vitamin except:', 'Vitamin K', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Vitamin K is primarily required for blood coagulation (clotting) and bone metabolism, but it does not serve as a major antioxidant.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Vitamin K\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Vitamin K is primarily required for blood coagulation (clotting) and bone metabolism, but it does not serve as a major antioxidant.\n\n• Vitamins A, C, and E (often remembered by the acronym ACE) are the primary nutrient antioxidants. They protect cells from damage by neutralizing free radicals.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Vitamin A, Vitamin C, Vitamin E"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
