('mc:a component of coenzyme a, a carrier of acetyl groups.:::pantothenic acid', 'a component of coenzyme a, a carrier of acetyl groups.', 'Pantothenic acid', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Pantothenate is vitamin B5 and is the key precursor for the biosynthesis of CoA, a universal and essential cofactor involved in a myriad of metabolic reactions, including the synthesis of phospholipids, the synthesis and degradation of fatty acids, and the operation of the TCA cycle.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Pantothenic acid\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Pantothenate is vitamin B5 and is the key precursor for the biosynthesis of CoA, a universal and essential cofactor involved in a myriad of metabolic reactions, including the synthesis of phospholipids, the synthesis and degradation of fatty acids, and the operation of the TCA cycle.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Biotin, Provitamin, Thiamin"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:a component of coenzyme a, a carrier of acetyl groups.:::', 'a component of coenzyme a, a carrier of acetyl groups.', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Pantothenate is vitamin B5 and is the key precursor for the biosynthesis of CoA, a universal and essential cofactor involved in a myriad of metabolic reactions, including the synthesis of phospholipids, the synthesis and degradation of fatty acids, and the operation of the TCA cycle.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Pantothenic acid\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Pantothenate is vitamin B5 and is the key precursor for the biosynthesis of CoA, a universal and essential cofactor involved in a myriad of metabolic reactions, including the synthesis of phospholipids, the synthesis and degradation of fatty acids, and the operation of the TCA cycle.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Biotin, Provitamin, Thiamin"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:it is known as anti-hemolytic vitamin.:::vitamin e', 'it is known as anti-hemolytic vitamin.', 'Vitamin E', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Vitamin E is historically recognized as the anti-hemolytic vitamin because it protects the cell membranes of red blood cells (erythrocytes) from oxidative damage caused by free radicals. Without adequate Vitamin E, the lipid bilayer undergoes lipid peroxidation, making the cells fragile and causing them to rupture easily (hemolytic anemia).","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Vitamin E\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Vitamin E is historically recognized as the anti-hemolytic vitamin because it protects the cell membranes of red blood cells (erythrocytes) from oxidative damage caused by free radicals. Without adequate Vitamin E, the lipid bilayer undergoes lipid peroxidation, making the cells fragile and causing them to rupture easily (hemolytic anemia).\n\n• Vitamin K is the anti-hemorrhagic vitamin (prevents bleeding/hemorrhage), which is a common point of confusion.\n• Folic acid deficiency leads to megaloblastic anemia, not hemolytic anemia.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Folic acid, Biotin, Vitamin K"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
