('mc:deficiency of this micronutrient is associated with anencephaly.:::folic acid', 'deficiency of this micronutrient is associated with anencephaly.', 'Folic acid', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Folate deficiency is highly associated with the risk of neural tube defects in growing fetus, malformation of the brain or lack of brain and skull (anencephaly) and spinal cord that result in disability or death.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Folic acid\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Folate deficiency is highly associated with the risk of neural tube defects in growing fetus, malformation of the brain or lack of brain and skull (anencephaly) and spinal cord that result in disability or death.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Cobalamin, Biotin, Provitamins"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
