('mc:it is a hormone secreted by the adrenal gland in response to low blood volume by keeping the sodium inside the body.:::aldosterone', 'it is a hormone secreted by the adrenal gland in response to low blood volume by keeping the sodium inside the body.', 'Aldosterone', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Aldosterone secreted by the adrenal gland retains sodium in the blood in response the low blood blood volume thus increasing blood pressure.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Aldosterone\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Aldosterone secreted by the adrenal gland retains sodium in the blood in response the low blood blood volume thus increasing blood pressure.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Vasopressin, Diuretics, Angiotensinogen"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
