('mc:component of nad and nadp.:::niacin', 'component of nad and nadp.', 'Niacin', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Niacin (Vitamin B3) forms the active nicotinamide portion of NAD (Nicotinamide Adenine Dinucleotide) and NADP (Nicotinamide Adenine Dinucleotide Phosphate). ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Niacin\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Niacin (Vitamin B3) forms the active nicotinamide portion of NAD (Nicotinamide Adenine Dinucleotide) and NADP (Nicotinamide Adenine Dinucleotide Phosphate). \n\nNiacin is derived from the function of its coenzymes: NAD and NADP in the hydrogen/electron transfer redox reactions in living cells.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Thiamin, Riboflavin, Biotin"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
