('mc:it is secreted by macrophages to active lymphocytes, suppress appetite and induce malaise and fever.:::monokines', 'it is secreted by macrophages to active lymphocytes, suppress appetite and induce malaise and fever.', 'Monokines', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Monokines are signaling proteins historically used to describe cytokines produced by monocytes and macrophages. Examples include interleukin-1 (IL-1) and tumor necrosis factor (TNF), which can promote immune-cell activation and produce systemic effects such as fever, anorexia, and malaise during inflammation.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Monokines\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Monokines are signaling proteins historically used to describe cytokines produced by monocytes and macrophages. Examples include interleukin-1 (IL-1) and tumor necrosis factor (TNF), which can promote immune-cell activation and produce systemic effects such as fever, anorexia, and malaise during inflammation.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Cytokines, Macrokines, Complements"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
