('mc:etag is a smoked meat traditionally made and used in cooking in .:::car', 'etag is a smoked meat traditionally made and used in cooking in .', 'CAR', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Etag is a smoked meat traditionally made and used in cooking in the Cordillera region of the Philippines. It is usually made from slabs of pork (like belly or neck).<img alt=\"Etag – Pinoy Reads\" src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" width=\"200\">The meat is cured heavily with salt and then air-dried or smoked over a wood fire for weeks or months. Locals often prefer wood from the alnus tree to give the meat a pleasant, aromatic smoke flavor.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"CAR\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Etag is a smoked meat traditionally made and used in cooking in the Cordillera region of the Philippines. It is usually made from slabs of pork (like belly or neck).<img alt=\"Etag – Pinoy Reads\" src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" width=\"200\">The meat is cured heavily with salt and then air-dried or smoked over a wood fire for weeks or months. Locals often prefer wood from the alnus tree to give the meat a pleasant, aromatic smoke flavor.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Region II, Region I, Region III"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
