-test scores as the primary objective."}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:all of the following are attributes of functional foods, except::::high calories', 'all of the following are attributes of functional foods, except:', 'High calories', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Functional foods are explicitly designed or naturally chosen to provide health benefits beyond basic nutrition (like raw caloric energy). They target specific physiological advantages (such as disease prevention) rather than loading the body with empty or high calories.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"High calories\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Functional foods are explicitly designed or naturally chosen to provide health benefits beyond basic nutrition (like raw caloric energy). They target specific physiological advantages (such as disease prevention) rather than loading the body with empty or high calories.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: High fiber, Low cholesterol, Reduced caffeine"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
