('mc:is a common feature in cancer patients.:::weight loss', 'is a common feature in cancer patients.', 'Weight loss', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Unintentional weight loss is one of the most prominent, universal, and classic hallmarks of cancer. It occurs in up to 60–80% of patients with advanced stages or specific tumor types (such as lung or upper gastrointestinal cancers). It is driven by cancer cachexia—a metabolic syndrome where tumor-induced inflammation breaks down muscle and fat tissue.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Weight loss\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Unintentional weight loss is one of the most prominent, universal, and classic hallmarks of cancer. It occurs in up to 60–80% of patients with advanced stages or specific tumor types (such as lung or upper gastrointestinal cancers). It is driven by cancer cachexia—a metabolic syndrome where tumor-induced inflammation breaks down muscle and fat tissue.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Taste/smell alteration, Dysphagia, Early satiety"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
