('mc:the philippines'' abundant use of rice is reflected on its wide selection of rice-based desserts. example of rice-based delicacies include the following except::::etag', 'the philippines'' abundant use of rice is reflected on its wide selection of rice-based desserts. example of rice-based delicacies include the following except:', 'Etag', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Etag is a type of preserved meat, specifically salted and smoked pork, not a rice-based dessert.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Etag\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Etag is a type of preserved meat, specifically salted and smoked pork, not a rice-based dessert.\n\n• Tibok-Tibok: A Filipino dessert made from carabao’s milk and rice flour, often flavored with latik (coconut caramel).\n• Kalamay: A sticky sweet delicacy made from glutinous rice, coconut milk, and sugar.\n• Puto Calasiao: A type of steamed rice cake that originates from Calasiao, Pangasinan, made from fermented rice batter.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Tibok-tibok, Kalamay, Puto Calasiao"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:the similarities in food culture between the southern philippines, malaysia, and indonesia are attributed to common religion. the similarity in food culture between the philippines and latin america is the history of colonization.:::both sentences are correct', 'the similarities in food culture between the southern philippines, malaysia, and indonesia are attributed to common religion. the similarity in food culture between the philippines and latin america is the history of colonization.', 'Both sentences are correct', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Sentence A is correct. The southern Philippines, Malaysia, and Indonesia share a significant Muslim population, and their food cultures reflect Islamic dietary laws, including the use of halal ingredients and specific cooking practices.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Both sentences are correct\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Sentence A is correct. The southern Philippines, Malaysia, and Indonesia share a significant Muslim population, and their food cultures reflect Islamic dietary laws, including the use of halal ingredients and specific cooking practices.\n\nSentence B is also correct. The Philippines was colonized by Spain for over 300 years, which influenced Filipino cuisine with techniques and dishes similar to those found in Latin America, which were also Spanish colonies. Examples include the use of ingredients like tomatoes, garlic, and onions, as well as dishes like adobo and empanadas.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Only the first sentence is correct, Only the second sentence is correct, Both sentences are incorrect"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
