('mc:in resource conservation, this term applies to the consideration of the design and manufacture of products and packaging with minimum toxic content and volume of material and its longevity.:::source reduction', 'in resource conservation, this term applies to the consideration of the design and manufacture of products and packaging with minimum toxic content and volume of material and its longevity.', 'source reduction', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Source reduction focuses on reducing the amount of waste generated at the source by designing products that use less material, are less toxic, and have longer lifespans. It aims to prevent waste before it is created.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"source reduction\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Source reduction focuses on reducing the amount of waste generated at the source by designing products that use less material, are less toxic, and have longer lifespans. It aims to prevent waste before it is created.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: waste segregation, recycling, land filling"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
