('mc:what statistical test will you use in the study particularly if the data is normally distributed? study: to determine the relation of wealth status (rich, middle class) and fruit intake (in grams) per day:::t-test', 'what statistical test will you use in the study particularly if the data is normally distributed? study: to determine the relation of wealth status (rich, middle class) and fruit intake (in grams) per day', 'T-test', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"T-test - parametric test used to compare the means of exactly two groups. Since there are only two wealth statuses to compare fruit intake then this is the correct answer.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"T-test\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"T-test - parametric test used to compare the means of exactly two groups. Since there are only two wealth statuses to compare fruit intake then this is the correct answer.\n\n• ANOVA - parametric test used to compare the means of three or more groups.\n• Chi-square test - used for categorical data\n• Mann-Whitney - is a non-parametric test","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: ANOVA, Chi-square test, Mann-Whitney"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
