('mc:it refers to a set of processes and conditions by which food is produced, processed, and stored, marketed and distributed, and prepared and consumed for proper nutrition and good.:::food and nutrition system', 'it refers to a set of processes and conditions by which food is produced, processed, and stored, marketed and distributed, and prepared and consumed for proper nutrition and good.', 'Food and Nutrition system', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"• Food Security - the state of having reliable access to sufficient, affordable, nutritious food.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Food and Nutrition system\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"• Food Security - the state of having reliable access to sufficient, affordable, nutritious food.\n• Food Path - the entire set of activities from farm to fork (production, processing, distribution, consumption, and waste).\n• Ecology of Food and Nutrition - the complex relationship between humans, food, and the natural, social, and cultural environment.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Food security, Food Path, Ecology of Food and Nutrition"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
