('mc:who was the first president of philippine association of nutrition?:::dr. francisco o. santos', 'who was the first president of philippine association of nutrition?', 'Dr. Francisco O. Santos', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Dr. Francisco O. Santos is a Filipino chemist and agricultural scientist, recognized as the \"Father of Human Nutrition\" in the Philippines.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Dr. Francisco O. Santos\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Dr. Francisco O. Santos is a Filipino chemist and agricultural scientist, recognized as the \"Father of Human Nutrition\" in the Philippines.\n\n• Dr. Jose Fabella - A Filipino physician and public health leader, known as the \"Father of Public Health\" in the Philippines. He served as the first Secretary of Health.\n• Dr. Juan Salcedo, Jr. - A prominent Filipino physician, researcher, and public health advocate; he led early efforts against Vitamin B1 deficiency and served as Secretary of Health and Chairman of the National Science Development Board.\n• Dr. Coronado R. Pascual - A Filipino nutritionist and physician who served as the Director of the Food and Nutrition Research Institute (FNRI) formerly NI and was a key figure in Philippine national nutrition planning.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Dr. Jose Fabella, Dr. Juan Salcedo Jr., Dr. Coronado R. Pascual"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
