('mc:a theory of aging where cells are inactivated or defective as a result of errors in dna replication.:::somatic mutation theory', 'a theory of aging where cells are inactivated or defective as a result of errors in dna replication.', 'Somatic mutation theory', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"• Genetic theory - Internal Clock/Programmed","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Somatic mutation theory\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"• Genetic theory - Internal Clock/Programmed\n• Wear-and-tear theory - External Damage/Breakdown\n• Cross-linkage theory - Molecular Rigidity/Stiffening","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Genetic theory, Wear-and-Tear theory, Cross-linkage theory"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:which behavior change theory/model is best to use if the community members are interested to be involved in the nutrition programs because they believe that they will benefit to the program?:::theory of planned behavior', 'which behavior change theory/model is best to use if the community members are interested to be involved in the nutrition programs because they believe that they will benefit to the program?', 'Theory of Planned Behavior', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"The correct answer is the Theory of Planned Behavior because the scenario describes both a personal attitude/belief about benefit (attitude toward the behavior) and social influence from friends (subjective norm), the two central constructs the theory uses to predict behavioral intention.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Theory of Planned Behavior\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"The correct answer is the Theory of Planned Behavior because the scenario describes both a personal attitude/belief about benefit (attitude toward the behavior) and social influence from friends (subjective norm), the two central constructs the theory uses to predict behavioral intention.\n\n• Precaution Adoption Process Model - Process of adopting a new precaution.\n• Health Belief Model - Beliefs about risk and effectiveness.\n• Theory of Planned Behavior - Intentions predict behavior.\n• Self-determination Theory - quality of motivation","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Precaution Adoption Process Model, Health Belief Model, Self-determined Theory"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
