('mc:in promotion of healthy lifestyle, which behavior change theory/model is best if the community members are eager to participate in zumba sessions because they are fond of dancing.:::self-determination theory', 'in promotion of healthy lifestyle, which behavior change theory/model is best if the community members are eager to participate in zumba sessions because they are fond of dancing.', 'Self-determination Theory', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Self-Determination Theory focuses heavily on the distinction between intrinsic motivation (doing an activity because it is inherently enjoyable, interesting, or fun) and extrinsic motivation (doing an activity for an external reward or out of fear).","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Self-determination Theory\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Self-Determination Theory focuses heavily on the distinction between intrinsic motivation (doing an activity because it is inherently enjoyable, interesting, or fun) and extrinsic motivation (doing an activity for an external reward or out of fear).\n• The Core Clue: The question stem states that community members are eager to participate because they \"are fond of dancing.\"\n• This means their drive is entirely autonomous and intrinsically motivated. SDT is the premier framework for leveraging and sustaining health behaviors that align with a person''s natural passions, autonomy, and intrinsic joy.\n\n• Precaution Adoption Process Model - Process of adopting a new precaution.\n• Health Belief Model - Beliefs about risk and effectiveness.\n• Theory of Planned Behavior - Intentions predict behavior.\n• Self-determination Theory - quality of motivation","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Precaution Adoption Process Model, Health Belief Model, Theory of Planned Behavior"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
