('mc:which of the following is an example of alliance building?:::convening the key persons that can contribute to the implementation of the program', 'which of the following is an example of alliance building?', 'Convening the key persons that can contribute to the implementation of the program', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"The best answer is convening key persons who can contribute to program implementation, because alliance building specifically involves bringing together influential stakeholders to form a working partnership around a shared goal. ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Convening the key persons that can contribute to the implementation of the program\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"The best answer is convening key persons who can contribute to program implementation, because alliance building specifically involves bringing together influential stakeholders to form a working partnership around a shared goal. \n\nWhile every item could be an answer, Letter D is the best because it includes the action and purpose.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Coordination to all stakeholders, Selecting interested stakeholders, Providing incentives to increase participation among stakeholders"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
