('mc:why are theories important in nutrition education?:::', 'why are theories important in nutrition education?', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"The best answer is that theories are used to shape nutrition education interventions and answer the \"why, what, and how\" of behavior change, providing the conceptual foundation for designing effective programs. ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"They are used to shape the nutrition education interventions and answer the \"Why, What, and How\"\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"The best answer is that theories are used to shape nutrition education interventions and answer the \"why, what, and how\" of behavior change, providing the conceptual foundation for designing effective programs. \n\n• The other choices each describe legitimate but narrower functions of theory (serving as the basis for behavior change, identifying target audiences, or identifying moderators of change), while the correct answer most comprehensively captures theory''s overall guiding role in shaping the full intervention design process.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: They are the bases and center of behavior change, They are useful in identifying target audience of nutrition education, They help nutrition educators identify and modify the specific set of moderators of behavior change"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:a multi-level tool for promoting and sustaining risk-reducing behavior change in individuals and communities by distributing tailored specific messages thru variety of channels:::behavior change communication', 'a multi-level tool for promoting and sustaining risk-reducing behavior change in individuals and communities by distributing tailored specific messages thru variety of channels', 'Behavior Change Communication', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"• Nutrition Education - narrower activity focused on knowledge/skill transfer","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Behavior Change Communication\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"• Nutrition Education - narrower activity focused on knowledge/skill transfer\n• Learning Strategies - specific pedagogical techniques\n• Health Promotion (D) - broader umbrella concept encompassing BCC as one of its strategic tools","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Nutrition Education, Learning Strategies, Health Promotion"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
