('mc:which country made the first specific commitment on the un decade of action on nutrition?:::brazil', 'which country made the first specific commitment on the un decade of action on nutrition?', 'Brazil', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"On May 22, 2017, Brazil became the first country to make SMART commitments as part of the United Nations (UN) Decade of Action on Nutrition 2016–2025. Ricardo Barros, Minister of Health of Brazil, made the announcement at the UN in Geneva, on the first day of the Seventieth World Health Assembly.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Brazil\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"On May 22, 2017, Brazil became the first country to make SMART commitments as part of the United Nations (UN) Decade of Action on Nutrition 2016–2025. Ricardo Barros, Minister of Health of Brazil, made the announcement at the UN in Geneva, on the first day of the Seventieth World Health Assembly.\n\nBrazil’s 3 commitments, to be achieved by 2019, are as follows:\n• Stop the growth in the adult obesity rate (which currently stands at 20.8%)\n• Reduce by at least 30% consumption of sugar-sweetened beverages among adults\n• Increase by at least 17.8% the proportion of adults who regularly eat fruit and vegetables\n\nBrazil outlined specific policy measures it will take to achieve these goals. These include fiscal measures (tax reductions, subsidies) to reduce the price of fresh foods, microcredit loans to family farmers, and cash transfers to poor families so that they can buy fresh produce.\n\nSee reference here: https://www.who.int/news/item/22-05-2017-brazil-first-country-to-make-specific-commitments-in-un-decade-of-action-on-nutrition","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Norway, France, Ecuador"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:which country made the first specific commitment on the un decade of action on nutrition?:::', 'which country made the first specific commitment on the un decade of action on nutrition?', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"On May 22, 2017, Brazil became the first country to make SMART commitments as part of the United Nations (UN) Decade of Action on Nutrition 2016–2025. Ricardo Barros, Minister of Health of Brazil, made the announcement at the UN in Geneva, on the first day of the Seventieth World Health Assembly.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Brazil\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"On May 22, 2017, Brazil became the first country to make SMART commitments as part of the United Nations (UN) Decade of Action on Nutrition 2016–2025. Ricardo Barros, Minister of Health of Brazil, made the announcement at the UN in Geneva, on the first day of the Seventieth World Health Assembly.\n\nBrazil’s 3 commitments, to be achieved by 2019, are as follows:\n• Stop the growth in the adult obesity rate (which currently stands at 20.8%)\n• Reduce by at least 30% consumption of sugar-sweetened beverages among adults\n• Increase by at least 17.8% the proportion of adults who regularly eat fruit and vegetables\n\nBrazil outlined specific policy measures it will take to achieve these goals. These include fiscal measures (tax reductions, subsidies) to reduce the price of fresh foods, microcredit loans to family farmers, and cash transfers to poor families so that they can buy fresh produce.\n\nSee reference here: https://www.who.int/news/item/22-05-2017-brazil-first-country-to-make-specific-commitments-in-un-decade-of-action-on-nutrition","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Norway, France, Ecuador"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb)
