('mc:is an information-sharing type of activity that provides nutrition information to 10-12 participating mothers who are seated in a circular position:::pabasa sa nutrisyon', 'is an information-sharing type of activity that provides nutrition information to 10-12 participating mothers who are seated in a circular position', 'Pabasa sa nutrisyon', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Pabasa sa Nutrisyon (PSN) is an information-sharing nutrition education initiative developed by the Nutrition Center of the Philippines (NCP). It is traditionally formatted as a community course where small groups of around 10 to 12 target mothers or caregivers sit in a circular arrangement to comfortably read, learn from standard nutritional guidelines, and share personal child-rearing experiences.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Pabasa sa nutrisyon\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Pabasa sa Nutrisyon (PSN) is an information-sharing nutrition education initiative developed by the Nutrition Center of the Philippines (NCP). It is traditionally formatted as a community course where small groups of around 10 to 12 target mothers or caregivers sit in a circular arrangement to comfortably read, learn from standard nutritional guidelines, and share personal child-rearing experiences.\n\n• Nutribus - 1980’s Nutrition Education using a bus.\n• TCP - Teacher Child Parent Approach - The Teacher-Child-Parent approach to nutrition is a collaborative strategy where teachers, parents, and other community members work together to promote and improve children''s nutrition through consistent education and support\n• Kumare - (Kalusugan para Umunlad si Mare) is a maternal health program designed to improve the delivery of much-needed iron supplements to pregnant women. This approach increases the number of prenatal visits, the number of iron tablets consumed, and improved hemoglobin levels. The intervention is anchored on training and re-orientation of health workers by giving them more responsibility for the mothers in their catchment area.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Nutribus, TCP, Kumare"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:is an information-sharing type of activity that provides nutrition information to 10-12 participating mothers who are seated in a circular position:::', 'is an information-sharing type of activity that provides nutrition information to 10-12 participating mothers who are seated in a circular position', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Pabasa sa Nutrisyon (PSN) is an information-sharing nutrition education initiative developed by the Nutrition Center of the Philippines (NCP). It is traditionally formatted as a community course where small groups of around 10 to 12 target mothers or caregivers sit in a circular arrangement to comfortably read, learn from standard nutritional guidelines, and share personal child-rearing experiences.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Pabasa sa nutrisyon\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Pabasa sa Nutrisyon (PSN) is an information-sharing nutrition education initiative developed by the Nutrition Center of the Philippines (NCP). It is traditionally formatted as a community course where small groups of around 10 to 12 target mothers or caregivers sit in a circular arrangement to comfortably read, learn from standard nutritional guidelines, and share personal child-rearing experiences.\n\n• Nutribus - 1980’s Nutrition Education using a bus.\n• TCP - Teacher Child Parent Approach - The Teacher-Child-Parent approach to nutrition is a collaborative strategy where teachers, parents, and other community members work together to promote and improve children''s nutrition through consistent education and support\n• Kumare - (Kalusugan para Umunlad si Mare) is a maternal health program designed to improve the delivery of much-needed iron supplements to pregnant women. This approach increases the number of prenatal visits, the number of iron tablets consumed, and improved hemoglobin levels. The intervention is anchored on training and re-orientation of health workers by giving them more responsibility for the mothers in their catchment area.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Nutribus, TCP, Kumare"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:which is a livelihood assistance program?:::lingap sa mahirap', 'which is a livelihood assistance program?', 'Lingap sa mahirap', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Lingap sa Mahirap: A historical, comprehensive poverty alleviation fund introduced during the Estrada administration targeting the 100 poorest families in every province and city to deliver integrated social welfare packages.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Lingap sa mahirap\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Lingap sa Mahirap: A historical, comprehensive poverty alleviation fund introduced during the Estrada administration targeting the 100 poorest families in every province and city to deliver integrated social welfare packages.\n\n• Tindahan Natin Program (TNP): This is a national government initiative implemented by the Department of Social Welfare and Development (DSWD). It serves as a livelihood assistance and job generation project alongside working as a targeted food price subsidy. It provides micro-financing and starter capital for low-income individuals, barangay councils, or community groups to set up small grocery stores (tindahan) that sell low-priced, quality food items like NFA rice and noodles.\n• Ginintuang Masaganang Ani: An overarching agricultural modernization program run by the Department of Agriculture (DA) focused on boosting crop productivity, farm technology, and national food sufficiency.\n• Sustansya para sa Masa: A multi-sectoral national movement launched to combat malnutrition through public food fortification strategies, such as adding Vitamin A to localized products.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Ginintuang masaganang ani, Sustansya para sa masa, Tindahan natin"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:which is a livelihood assistance program?:::', 'which is a livelihood assistance program?', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Lingap sa Mahirap: A historical, comprehensive poverty alleviation fund introduced during the Estrada administration targeting the 100 poorest families in every province and city to deliver integrated social welfare packages.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Lingap sa mahirap\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Lingap sa Mahirap: A historical, comprehensive poverty alleviation fund introduced during the Estrada administration targeting the 100 poorest families in every province and city to deliver integrated social welfare packages.\n\n• Tindahan Natin Program (TNP): This is a national government initiative implemented by the Department of Social Welfare and Development (DSWD). It serves as a livelihood assistance and job generation project alongside working as a targeted food price subsidy. It provides micro-financing and starter capital for low-income individuals, barangay councils, or community groups to set up small grocery stores (tindahan) that sell low-priced, quality food items like NFA rice and noodles.\n• Ginintuang Masaganang Ani: An overarching agricultural modernization program run by the Department of Agriculture (DA) focused on boosting crop productivity, farm technology, and national food sufficiency.\n• Sustansya para sa Masa: A multi-sectoral national movement launched to combat malnutrition through public food fortification strategies, such as adding Vitamin A to localized products.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Ginintuang masaganang ani, Sustansya para sa masa, Tindahan natin"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:what is/are the priority foods source/s during the early emergency period?:::water and calories', 'what is/are the priority foods source/s during the early emergency period?', 'Water and Calories', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Water and calories are the two most immediately life-sustaining priorities in the very early phase of an emergency response. ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Water and Calories\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Water and calories are the two most immediately life-sustaining priorities in the very early phase of an emergency response. \n\n• Water alone is insufficient because caloric/energy needs are also urgently critical for survival. \n• Adding protein and further adding fat reflect priorities that become important slightly later, as the emergency response matures beyond the immediate survival phase into more complete dietary support.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Water, Water, Calories, and Protein, Water, Calores, Protein, and Fat"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:what is/are the priority foods source/s during the early emergency period?:::', 'what is/are the priority foods source/s during the early emergency period?', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Water and calories are the two most immediately life-sustaining priorities in the very early phase of an emergency response. ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Water and Calories\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Water and calories are the two most immediately life-sustaining priorities in the very early phase of an emergency response. \n\n• Water alone is insufficient because caloric/energy needs are also urgently critical for survival. \n• Adding protein and further adding fat reflect priorities that become important slightly later, as the emergency response matures beyond the immediate survival phase into more complete dietary support.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Water, Water, Calories, and Protein, Water, Calores, Protein, and Fat"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:which cmam component treats children with sam with poor appetite or medical complications?:::inpatient care', 'which cmam component treats children with sam with poor appetite or medical complications?', 'Inpatient care', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Inpatient care, which is specifically designated within the Community-based Management of Acute Malnutrition (CMAM) framework for children with severe acute malnutrition (SAM) who present with poor appetite (failed appetite test) or medical complications requiring more intensive, facility-based treatment. ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Inpatient care\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Inpatient care, which is specifically designated within the Community-based Management of Acute Malnutrition (CMAM) framework for children with severe acute malnutrition (SAM) who present with poor appetite (failed appetite test) or medical complications requiring more intensive, facility-based treatment. \n\n• Outpatient care is instead used for SAM children who pass the appetite test and have no medical complications, allowing home-based management with ready-to-use therapeutic food.\n• Home care and community care are not standard, formally defined CMAM components matching this specific clinical criterion.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Outpatient care, Home care, Community care"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:which cmam component treats children with sam with poor appetite or medical complications?:::', 'which cmam component treats children with sam with poor appetite or medical complications?', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Inpatient care, which is specifically designated within the Community-based Management of Acute Malnutrition (CMAM) framework for children with severe acute malnutrition (SAM) who present with poor appetite (failed appetite test) or medical complications requiring more intensive, facility-based treatment. ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Inpatient care\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Inpatient care, which is specifically designated within the Community-based Management of Acute Malnutrition (CMAM) framework for children with severe acute malnutrition (SAM) who present with poor appetite (failed appetite test) or medical complications requiring more intensive, facility-based treatment. \n\n• Outpatient care is instead used for SAM children who pass the appetite test and have no medical complications, allowing home-based management with ready-to-use therapeutic food.\n• Home care and community care are not standard, formally defined CMAM components matching this specific clinical criterion.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Outpatient care, Home care, Community care"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:characterized mainly by a program already prepared by a group external to a community or environment. it may also mean top-down approach which is characterized mainly by the formulation of a plan at a higher level (e.g. national level), for implementation at a lower level (e.g. municipality or barangay).:::pre-determined planning', 'characterized mainly by a program already prepared by a group external to a community or environment. it may also mean top-down approach which is characterized mainly by the formulation of a plan at a higher level (e.g. national level), for implementation at a lower level (e.g. municipality or barangay).', 'Pre-Determined planning', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Pre-determined planning is defined as a top-down approach where plans are formulated at a higher level (e.g., national) for implementation at a lower level (e.g., barangay), without the community''s initial input into design. ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Pre-Determined planning\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Pre-determined planning is defined as a top-down approach where plans are formulated at a higher level (e.g., national) for implementation at a lower level (e.g., barangay), without the community''s initial input into design. \n\n• Self-determined planning instead involves the community itself formulating its own plan. \n• Joint planning involves collaboration between external and community stakeholders together. \n• Strategic planning refers to a broader planning methodology focused on long-term goal-setting.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Self-Determined planning, Joint planning, Strategic planning"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:characterized mainly by a program already prepared by a group external to a community or environment. it may also mean top-down approach which is characterized mainly by the formulation of a plan at a higher level (e.g. national level), for implementation at a lower level (e.g. municipality or barangay).:::', 'characterized mainly by a program already prepared by a group external to a community or environment. it may also mean top-down approach which is characterized mainly by the formulation of a plan at a higher level (e.g. national level), for implementation at a lower level (e.g. municipality or barangay).', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Pre-determined planning is defined as a top-down approach where plans are formulated at a higher level (e.g., national) for implementation at a lower level (e.g., barangay), without the community''s initial input into design. ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Pre-Determined planning\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Pre-determined planning is defined as a top-down approach where plans are formulated at a higher level (e.g., national) for implementation at a lower level (e.g., barangay), without the community''s initial input into design. \n\n• Self-determined planning instead involves the community itself formulating its own plan. \n• Joint planning involves collaboration between external and community stakeholders together. \n• Strategic planning refers to a broader planning methodology focused on long-term goal-setting.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Self-Determined planning, Joint planning, Strategic planning"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:the following are characteristics of nutrition-oriented development planning except::::malnutrition is merely a problem of food consumption and availability', 'the following are characteristics of nutrition-oriented development planning except:', 'Malnutrition is merely a problem of food consumption and availability', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Nutrition-oriented development planning explicitly recognizes malnutrition as a complex, multi-causal problem, not one reducible to just food consumption/availability alone. ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Malnutrition is merely a problem of food consumption and availability\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Nutrition-oriented development planning explicitly recognizes malnutrition as a complex, multi-causal problem, not one reducible to just food consumption/availability alone. \n\nNutrition being included as an objective integrated into development planning, diagnostic analysis used to identify causes, and nutrition actions applied across local/national and sectoral plans are all genuine, defining characteristics of this planning approach.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Nutrition is included as an objective and integrated into development planning, Diagnostic analysis is used in identifying cause of malnutrition, Nutrition actions are applied in local and national levels; and in sectoral development plans"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:the aim of work design is to::::', 'the aim of work design is to:', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Work design aims to develop jobs and methods that improve productivity and employee satisfaction while supporting efficient, safe work.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"increase productivity and employee satisfaction\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Work design aims to develop jobs and methods that improve productivity and employee satisfaction while supporting efficient, safe work.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: provide efficient and effective work methods, provide safe and healthy work environment, design a staff of fit people"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:the following are characteristics of nutrition-oriented development planning except::::', 'the following are characteristics of nutrition-oriented development planning except:', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Nutrition-oriented development planning explicitly recognizes malnutrition as a complex, multi-causal problem, not one reducible to just food consumption/availability alone. ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Malnutrition is merely a problem of food consumption and availability\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Nutrition-oriented development planning explicitly recognizes malnutrition as a complex, multi-causal problem, not one reducible to just food consumption/availability alone. \n\nNutrition being included as an objective integrated into development planning, diagnostic analysis used to identify causes, and nutrition actions applied across local/national and sectoral plans are all genuine, defining characteristics of this planning approach.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Nutrition is included as an objective and integrated into development planning, Diagnostic analysis is used in identifying cause of malnutrition, Nutrition actions are applied in local and national levels; and in sectoral development plans"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:mechanism for planning, implementing, monitoring, evaluating, and coordinating the local plans of action for nutrition at the province, city/municipality, and barangay levels.:::local nutrition committees', 'mechanism for planning, implementing, monitoring, evaluating, and coordinating the local plans of action for nutrition at the province, city/municipality, and barangay levels.', 'Local Nutrition Committees', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Local Nutrition Committees (LNCs) serve as multi-function coordinating role across all local government levels in the Philippines, chaired by the respective local chief executive, and the basic functional unit of the nutrition program implementation and management.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Local Nutrition Committees\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Local Nutrition Committees (LNCs) serve as multi-function coordinating role across all local government levels in the Philippines, chaired by the respective local chief executive, and the basic functional unit of the nutrition program implementation and management.\n\nSee more here: https://nnc.gov.ph/mindanao-region/lnc-the-basic-functional-unit-of-the-nutrition-program/","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Local Nutrition Action Officers, Local Development Coordinators, Local Development Planning Team"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:mechanism for planning, implementing, monitoring, evaluating, and coordinating the local plans of action for nutrition at the province, city/municipality, and barangay levels.:::', 'mechanism for planning, implementing, monitoring, evaluating, and coordinating the local plans of action for nutrition at the province, city/municipality, and barangay levels.', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Local Nutrition Committees (LNCs) serve as multi-function coordinating role across all local government levels in the Philippines, chaired by the respective local chief executive, and the basic functional unit of the nutrition program implementation and management.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Local Nutrition Committees\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Local Nutrition Committees (LNCs) serve as multi-function coordinating role across all local government levels in the Philippines, chaired by the respective local chief executive, and the basic functional unit of the nutrition program implementation and management.\n\nSee more here: https://nnc.gov.ph/mindanao-region/lnc-the-basic-functional-unit-of-the-nutrition-program/","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Local Nutrition Action Officers, Local Development Coordinators, Local Development Planning Team"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:local nutrition committees are chaired by the following local chief executives, except::::congressmen', 'local nutrition committees are chaired by the following local chief executives, except:', 'Congressmen', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Congressmen are national legislative officials, not local chief executives, and therefore do not chair Local Nutrition Committees. ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Congressmen\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Congressmen are national legislative officials, not local chief executives, and therefore do not chair Local Nutrition Committees. \n\nBarangay Captains, Mayors, and Governors are all local chief executives who chair LNCs at their respective barangay, city/municipal, and provincial levels.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Barangay Captains, Mayors, Governors"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:local nutrition committees are chaired by the following local chief executives, except::::', 'local nutrition committees are chaired by the following local chief executives, except:', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Congressmen are national legislative officials, not local chief executives, and therefore do not chair Local Nutrition Committees. ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Congressmen\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Congressmen are national legislative officials, not local chief executives, and therefore do not chair Local Nutrition Committees. \n\nBarangay Captains, Mayors, and Governors are all local chief executives who chair LNCs at their respective barangay, city/municipal, and provincial levels.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Barangay Captains, Mayors, Governors"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:local nutrition action plans (lnap) serves as the mechanism to achieve nutrition goals at the city/municipal/provincial level. it should be harmonized in the local development system and plans, except::::environmental impact assessment', 'local nutrition action plans (lnap) serves as the mechanism to achieve nutrition goals at the city/municipal/provincial level. it should be harmonized in the local development system and plans, except:', 'Environmental Impact Assessment', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Environmental Impact Assessment is a project-specific environmental review process, not one of the standard local development planning documents that the Local Nutrition Action Plan (LNAP) is meant to be harmonized with. ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Environmental Impact Assessment\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Environmental Impact Assessment is a project-specific environmental review process, not one of the standard local development planning documents that the Local Nutrition Action Plan (LNAP) is meant to be harmonized with. \n\nThe Comprehensive Land Use Plan, Executive Legislative Agenda, and Comprehensive Development Plan are all standard local government planning documents that the LNAP should align with to ensure nutrition is mainstreamed into broader development planning and budgeting processes.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Comprehensive Land Use Plan, Executive Legislative Agenda, Comprehensive Development Plan"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:local nutrition action plans (lnap) serves as the mechanism to achieve nutrition goals at the city/municipal/provincial level. it should be harmonized in the local development system and plans, except::::', 'local nutrition action plans (lnap) serves as the mechanism to achieve nutrition goals at the city/municipal/provincial level. it should be harmonized in the local development system and plans, except:', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Environmental Impact Assessment is a project-specific environmental review process, not one of the standard local development planning documents that the Local Nutrition Action Plan (LNAP) is meant to be harmonized with. ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Environmental Impact Assessment\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Environmental Impact Assessment is a project-specific environmental review process, not one of the standard local development planning documents that the Local Nutrition Action Plan (LNAP) is meant to be harmonized with. \n\nThe Comprehensive Land Use Plan, Executive Legislative Agenda, and Comprehensive Development Plan are all standard local government planning documents that the LNAP should align with to ensure nutrition is mainstreamed into broader development planning and budgeting processes.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Comprehensive Land Use Plan, Executive Legislative Agenda, Comprehensive Development Plan"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:focal persons for nutrition at the local levels are::::bns, cnao, mnao, pnao', 'focal persons for nutrition at the local levels are:', 'BNS, CNAO, MNAO, PNAO', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Regional nutrition focal points/officers serve national/sub-national levels.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"BNS, CNAO, MNAO, PNAO\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Regional nutrition focal points/officers serve national/sub-national levels.\n\n• BNS, CNAO, MNAO, PNAO, RNAO - national level\n• BNS, CNAO, MNAO, PNAO, RNPC - national level\n• BNS, CNPC, MNPC, PNPC, RNPC - national level","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: BNS, CNAO, MNAO, PNAO, RNAO, BNS, CNAO, MNAO, PNAO, RNPC, BNS, CPNC, MNPC, PNPC, RNPC"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:focal persons for nutrition at the local levels are::::', 'focal persons for nutrition at the local levels are:', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Regional nutrition focal points/officers serve national/sub-national levels.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"BNS, CNAO, MNAO, PNAO\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Regional nutrition focal points/officers serve national/sub-national levels.\n\n• BNS, CNAO, MNAO, PNAO, RNAO - national level\n• BNS, CNAO, MNAO, PNAO, RNPC - national level\n• BNS, CNPC, MNPC, PNPC, RNPC - national level","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: BNS, CNAO, MNAO, PNAO, RNAO, BNS, CNAO, MNAO, PNAO, RNPC, BNS, CPNC, MNPC, PNPC, RNPC"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:a method of delivering goods and/or services to a selected group of individuals or households rather than to every individual or household in the population.:::targeting', 'a method of delivering goods and/or services to a selected group of individuals or households rather than to every individual or household in the population.', 'Targeting', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Targeting is defined as directing program benefits to a specifically selected subgroup rather than universally to the entire population. ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Targeting\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Targeting is defined as directing program benefits to a specifically selected subgroup rather than universally to the entire population. \n\n• Prioritizing of beneficiaries is a related but broader concept describing the ranking of need, not the delivery mechanism. \n• Sampling refers to a research/survey selection method, not a program service delivery approach. \n• Identification and selection of clients is part of the targeting process but does not capture the full definition of the delivery method as precisely as \"targeting\" does.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Prioritizing of beneficiaries, Sampling, Identification and selection of clients"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:a method of delivering goods and/or services to a selected group of individuals or households rather than to every individual or household in the population.:::', 'a method of delivering goods and/or services to a selected group of individuals or households rather than to every individual or household in the population.', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Targeting is defined as directing program benefits to a specifically selected subgroup rather than universally to the entire population. ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Targeting\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Targeting is defined as directing program benefits to a specifically selected subgroup rather than universally to the entire population. \n\n• Prioritizing of beneficiaries is a related but broader concept describing the ranking of need, not the delivery mechanism. \n• Sampling refers to a research/survey selection method, not a program service delivery approach. \n• Identification and selection of clients is part of the targeting process but does not capture the full definition of the delivery method as precisely as \"targeting\" does.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Prioritizing of beneficiaries, Sampling, Identification and selection of clients"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:depends on decision-making structures at the community level to allocate program goods or services effectively according to the criteria as defined in the program objectives.:::community-based', 'depends on decision-making structures at the community level to allocate program goods or services effectively according to the criteria as defined in the program objectives.', 'Community-based', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Community-based uses local knowledge and consensus (e.g., councils) to select beneficiaries.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Community-based\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Community-based uses local knowledge and consensus (e.g., councils) to select beneficiaries.\n\n• Administrative - uses official records and pre-determined criteria (e.g., income data, public registries).\n• Self-targeting - uses program design (e.g., low-quality food, hard labor requirement) to make the benefit unattractive","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Administrative, Self-targeting, Market-based"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:depends on decision-making structures at the community level to allocate program goods or services effectively according to the criteria as defined in the program objectives.:::', 'depends on decision-making structures at the community level to allocate program goods or services effectively according to the criteria as defined in the program objectives.', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Community-based uses local knowledge and consensus (e.g., councils) to select beneficiaries.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Community-based\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Community-based uses local knowledge and consensus (e.g., councils) to select beneficiaries.\n\n• Administrative - uses official records and pre-determined criteria (e.g., income data, public registries).\n• Self-targeting - uses program design (e.g., low-quality food, hard labor requirement) to make the benefit unattractive","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Administrative, Self-targeting, Market-based"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb)
