('mc:the lnap is best prepared on the first semester of an election year to ensure that the nutrition agenda is integrated in the executive legislative agenda which becomes the bases for local development plan and in-turn the annual investment plan. this is essential for::::', 'the lnap is best prepared on the first semester of an election year to ensure that the nutrition agenda is integrated in the executive legislative agenda which becomes the bases for local development plan and in-turn the annual investment plan. this is essential for:', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Local budgeting because timely integration of the nutrition agenda into the Executive Legislative Agenda ensures that nutrition programs are properly reflected and funded in the subsequent Annual Investment Plan and local budget allocations. ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Local Budgeting\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Local budgeting because timely integration of the nutrition agenda into the Executive Legislative Agenda ensures that nutrition programs are properly reflected and funded in the subsequent Annual Investment Plan and local budget allocations. \n\nWhile local planning, implementation, and monitoring/evaluation are all eventually affected by this timing, the question mentioning ELA and AIP points most directly to securing adequate budgeting for nutrition programs.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Local Planning, Local Implementation, Local Monitoring and evaluation"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
