('mc:a decision-making process of identifying potential nutrition problems and needs of a specific population group, analyzing possible ways of preventing and controlling malnutrition, allocating resources based on needs and expectations, and taking deliberate action to address nutritional problems, including those related to monitoring and evaluation.:::nutrition program management', 'a decision-making process of identifying potential nutrition problems and needs of a specific population group, analyzing possible ways of preventing and controlling malnutrition, allocating resources based on needs and expectations, and taking deliberate action to address nutritional problems, including those related to monitoring and evaluation.', 'Nutrition Program Management', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Nutrition Program Management is executing, supervising, and coordinating all activities to achieve program goals.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Nutrition Program Management\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Nutrition Program Management is executing, supervising, and coordinating all activities to achieve program goals.\n\n• Nutrition Program Planning - designing the specific program: defining objectives, strategies, resources, and implementation steps.\n• Nutrition Intervention - specific action designed to directly improve nutritional status (e.g., supplementation, education).\n• Food and Nutrition Planning - macro-level process to set national/regional policies and strategies for food supply and consumption.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Nutrition Program Planning, Nutrition Intervention, Food and Nutrition Planning"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:a decision-making process of identifying potential nutrition problems and needs of a specific population group, analyzing possible ways of preventing and controlling malnutrition, allocating resources based on needs and expectations, and taking deliberate action to address nutritional problems, including those related to monitoring and evaluation.:::', 'a decision-making process of identifying potential nutrition problems and needs of a specific population group, analyzing possible ways of preventing and controlling malnutrition, allocating resources based on needs and expectations, and taking deliberate action to address nutritional problems, including those related to monitoring and evaluation.', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Nutrition Program Management is executing, supervising, and coordinating all activities to achieve program goals.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Nutrition Program Management\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Nutrition Program Management is executing, supervising, and coordinating all activities to achieve program goals.\n\n• Nutrition Program Planning - designing the specific program: defining objectives, strategies, resources, and implementation steps.\n• Nutrition Intervention - specific action designed to directly improve nutritional status (e.g., supplementation, education).\n• Food and Nutrition Planning - macro-level process to set national/regional policies and strategies for food supply and consumption.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Nutrition Program Planning, Nutrition Intervention, Food and Nutrition Planning"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:a researcher wants to conduct a study wherein men with coronary artery disease and a comparable group of men without coronary artery disease were asked about their prior use of aspirin. this is an example of which type of study?:::case control', 'a researcher wants to conduct a study wherein men with coronary artery disease and a comparable group of men without coronary artery disease were asked about their prior use of aspirin. this is an example of which type of study?', 'Case control', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"This scenario perfectly illustrates the design of a case-control study based on two defining factors:","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Case control\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"This scenario perfectly illustrates the design of a case-control study based on two defining factors:\n\n• Selection by Outcome (Disease Status): The researcher selects participants based on whether they already have the condition of interest. The \"cases\" are the men with coronary artery disease, and the \"controls\" are the comparable group of men without the disease.\n• Retrospective Assessment: The researcher then looks backward in time (\"asked about their prior use of aspirin\") to compare how frequently each group was exposed to the factor being studied.\n\n• Ecological study - Comparing the average per capita salt intake across ten different countries to the average national hypertension rate in those same countries.\n• Randomized clinical trial - Dividing 500 patients with a specific disease into two groups: one receiving a new drug and one receiving a placebo (or standard treatment), and then following both groups for a year to see which group has a better outcome.\n• Case series - A doctor publishing a report detailing the clinical presentation, diagnosis, treatment, and outcomes for three unusual patients presenting with the same rare cluster of symptoms at their clinic over a six-month period.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Ecological study, Randomized clinial trial, Case series"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:a researcher wants to conduct a study wherein men with coronary artery disease and a comparable group of men without coronary artery disease were asked about their prior use of aspirin. this is an example of which type of study?:::', 'a researcher wants to conduct a study wherein men with coronary artery disease and a comparable group of men without coronary artery disease were asked about their prior use of aspirin. this is an example of which type of study?', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"This scenario perfectly illustrates the design of a case-control study based on two defining factors:","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Case control\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"This scenario perfectly illustrates the design of a case-control study based on two defining factors:\n\n• Selection by Outcome (Disease Status): The researcher selects participants based on whether they already have the condition of interest. The \"cases\" are the men with coronary artery disease, and the \"controls\" are the comparable group of men without the disease.\n• Retrospective Assessment: The researcher then looks backward in time (\"asked about their prior use of aspirin\") to compare how frequently each group was exposed to the factor being studied.\n\n• Ecological study - Comparing the average per capita salt intake across ten different countries to the average national hypertension rate in those same countries.\n• Randomized clinical trial - Dividing 500 patients with a specific disease into two groups: one receiving a new drug and one receiving a placebo (or standard treatment), and then following both groups for a year to see which group has a better outcome.\n• Case series - A doctor publishing a report detailing the clinical presentation, diagnosis, treatment, and outcomes for three unusual patients presenting with the same rare cluster of symptoms at their clinic over a six-month period.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Ecological study, Randomized clinial trial, Case series"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:it refers to the epidemiological approach which explains the occurence, nature, and extent of a disease::::man-agent-environment triad', 'it refers to the epidemiological approach which explains the occurence, nature, and extent of a disease:', 'Man-Agent-Environment Triad', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Man-Agent-Environment triad - epidemiological model; analyzing disease causation via host, pathogen, and surroundings.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Man-Agent-Environment Triad\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Man-Agent-Environment triad - epidemiological model; analyzing disease causation via host, pathogen, and surroundings.\n\n• Triple A approach - cycle for planning: assessment, analysis, action\n• UNICEF framework - three-level causes of malnutrition: basic, underlying, and immediate (food/health).\n• Undernutrition infection cycle - vicious spiral where poor nutrition weakens immunity, increasing infection risk, which worsens nutrition.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Triple A approach, UNICEF framework, Undernutrition infection cycle"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
