('mc:risk factors for malnutrition in older adults include all of the following except;:::all of the above', 'risk factors for malnutrition in older adults include all of the following except;', 'all of the above', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Malnutrition in geriatrics is driven by an interplay of systemic pathways. Tooth loss or oral pain compromises the mechanical phase of digestion, limiting the intake of fiber- and protein-dense whole foods due to masticatory dysfunction and painful mucosal lesions. Polypharmacy (multiple medications) induces anorexia via xerostomia (drug-induced salivary gland hypofunction reducing taste acuity through zinc binding or neural inhibition), alters GI motility, causes nausea, and induces direct nutrient malabsorption or micronutrient depletion via competitive enzymatic antagonism (e.g., proton pump inhibitors blocking gastric acid-dependent protein-bound Vitamin B12 cleavage and iron/calcium ionization). Conversely, economic insecurity restricts purchasing power for nutrient-dense whole foods, forcing reliance on energy-dense, micronutrient-deficient processed alternatives.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"all of the above\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Malnutrition in geriatrics is driven by an interplay of systemic pathways. Tooth loss or oral pain compromises the mechanical phase of digestion, limiting the intake of fiber- and protein-dense whole foods due to masticatory dysfunction and painful mucosal lesions. Polypharmacy (multiple medications) induces anorexia via xerostomia (drug-induced salivary gland hypofunction reducing taste acuity through zinc binding or neural inhibition), alters GI motility, causes nausea, and induces direct nutrient malabsorption or micronutrient depletion via competitive enzymatic antagonism (e.g., proton pump inhibitors blocking gastric acid-dependent protein-bound Vitamin B12 cleavage and iron/calcium ionization). Conversely, economic insecurity restricts purchasing power for nutrient-dense whole foods, forcing reliance on energy-dense, micronutrient-deficient processed alternatives.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: multiple medications, tooth loss or oral pain, economic security"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
