('mc:let us trace the digestion of a peanut butter and banana sandwich on whole-wheat sesame bread through the gastrointestinal (gi) tract. in the mouth, there is chewing and swallowing, but little digestion takes place. which nutrients are involved in this process?:::carbohydrates and fiber', 'let us trace the digestion of a peanut butter and banana sandwich on whole-wheat sesame bread through the gastrointestinal (gi) tract. in the mouth, there is chewing and swallowing, but little digestion takes place. which nutrients are involved in this process?', 'Carbohydrates and fiber', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Salivary alpha-amylase is secreted by the parotid and submandibular glands, targeting internal alpha-1,4-glycosidic bonds of starches (found in the whole-wheat bread and banana) to produce dextrins and maltose. Dietary fiber (complex plant polysaccharides such as cellulose, hemicellulose, and pectin found in whole grains, sesame seeds, and banana) is resistant to human endogenous hydrolytic enzymes; thus, fiber undergoes mechanical size reduction via chewing but experiences zero enzymatic degradation in the mouth or stomach.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Carbohydrates and fiber\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Salivary alpha-amylase is secreted by the parotid and submandibular glands, targeting internal alpha-1,4-glycosidic bonds of starches (found in the whole-wheat bread and banana) to produce dextrins and maltose. Dietary fiber (complex plant polysaccharides such as cellulose, hemicellulose, and pectin found in whole grains, sesame seeds, and banana) is resistant to human endogenous hydrolytic enzymes; thus, fiber undergoes mechanical size reduction via chewing but experiences zero enzymatic degradation in the mouth or stomach.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Carbohydrates and protein, Carbohydrates and fats, Carbohydrates and vitamins"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
