ative options: I, II, III, IV, I, III, IV, II, IV, I, II, III"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:based on the latest national nutrition survey, which regions in the philippines have the highest prevalence of overweight and obesity among adults?:::ncr, car, central luzon', 'based on the latest national nutrition survey, which regions in the philippines have the highest prevalence of overweight and obesity among adults?', 'NCR, CAR, Central Luzon', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Compared with the national estimate, the National Capital Region has the highest obesity prevalence with 52.7%, followed by the Cordillera Administrative Region (50.6%) and Central Luzon (49.6%).","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"NCR, CAR, Central Luzon\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Compared with the national estimate, the National Capital Region has the highest obesity prevalence with 52.7%, followed by the Cordillera Administrative Region (50.6%) and Central Luzon (49.6%).","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: NCR, BARMM, MIMAROPA, NCR, BARMM, SOCCSKSARGEN, NCR, CALABARZON, MIMAROPA"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
