('mc:all are types of nonprobability sampling except::::cluster sampling', 'all are types of nonprobability sampling except:', 'cluster sampling', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Convenience, purposive, and quota sampling are nonprobability methods, meaning population units do not have a known or equal chance of selection, and selection is instead guided by accessibility, judgment, or predetermined quotas. ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"cluster sampling\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Convenience, purposive, and quota sampling are nonprobability methods, meaning population units do not have a known or equal chance of selection, and selection is instead guided by accessibility, judgment, or predetermined quotas. \n\nCluster sampling, in contrast, is a probability sampling technique in which naturally occurring groups (clusters) are randomly selected, giving every unit in the population a calculable chance of inclusion.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: convenience sampling, purposive sampling, quota sampling"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:sa palabas ng abs-cbn foundation na dok ricky, pedia ng barangay, sino ang gumanap na dok riki bautista na katambal ni dominic ochoa?:::', 'sa palabas ng abs-cbn foundation na dok ricky, pedia ng barangay, sino ang gumanap na dok riki bautista na katambal ni dominic ochoa?', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Ang tamang sagot ay Alessandra de Rossi, na gumanap bilang si Dra. Marikina \"Dok Riki\" Bautista sa \"sitcom-mentary\" na palabas na Dok Ricky, Pedia ng Barangay.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Alessandra de Rossi\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Ang tamang sagot ay Alessandra de Rossi, na gumanap bilang si Dra. Marikina \"Dok Riki\" Bautista sa \"sitcom-mentary\" na palabas na Dok Ricky, Pedia ng Barangay.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Yen Santos, Arci Muñoz, Bella Padilla"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:all are types of nonprobability sampling except::::', 'all are types of nonprobability sampling except:', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Convenience, purposive, and quota sampling are nonprobability methods, meaning population units do not have a known or equal chance of selection, and selection is instead guided by accessibility, judgment, or predetermined quotas. ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"cluster sampling\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Convenience, purposive, and quota sampling are nonprobability methods, meaning population units do not have a known or equal chance of selection, and selection is instead guided by accessibility, judgment, or predetermined quotas. \n\nCluster sampling, in contrast, is a probability sampling technique in which naturally occurring groups (clusters) are randomly selected, giving every unit in the population a calculable chance of inclusion.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: convenience sampling, purposive sampling, quota sampling"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:the recommended amount of fish and alternatives based on the pinggang pinoy is .:::', 'the recommended amount of fish and alternatives based on the pinggang pinoy is .', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Under the Pinggang Pinoy food exchange guide developed by the DOST Food and Nutrition Research Institute, one serving from the fish and alternatives (\"Grow\") food group, such as a small piece of fish, a matchbox-sized portion of meat, or an equivalent like shrimp or legumes, corresponds to approximately half a cup, consistent with the food guide''s exchange list of household measures (DOST-FNRI, n.d.).","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"½ cup\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Under the Pinggang Pinoy food exchange guide developed by the DOST Food and Nutrition Research Institute, one serving from the fish and alternatives (\"Grow\") food group, such as a small piece of fish, a matchbox-sized portion of meat, or an equivalent like shrimp or legumes, corresponds to approximately half a cup, consistent with the food guide''s exchange list of household measures (DOST-FNRI, n.d.).","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: ¼ cup, ⅓ cup, ¾ cup"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:which of the following dishes is not included in the three sets of vegetables provided by the may gulay project at affordable prices?:::dinengdeng', 'which of the following dishes is not included in the three sets of vegetables provided by the may gulay project at affordable prices?', 'Dinengdeng', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"The Department of Agriculture''s \"May Gulay Project\" was launched to ensure a continuous and stable supply of vegetables at affordable prices (traditionally packed and retailed as pre-cut, hygienic half-kilo sets).","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Dinengdeng\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"The Department of Agriculture''s \"May Gulay Project\" was launched to ensure a continuous and stable supply of vegetables at affordable prices (traditionally packed and retailed as pre-cut, hygienic half-kilo sets).\n\nThe program officially provides three specific sets of pre-packaged vegetable combinations tailored for classic Filipino dishes:\n1. Pinakbet\n2. Sinigang\n3. Chopsuey","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Pinakbet, Sinigang, Chopsuey"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:which of the following dishes is not included in the three sets of vegetables provided by the may gulay project at affordable prices?:::', 'which of the following dishes is not included in the three sets of vegetables provided by the may gulay project at affordable prices?', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"The Department of Agriculture''s \"May Gulay Project\" was launched to ensure a continuous and stable supply of vegetables at affordable prices (traditionally packed and retailed as pre-cut, hygienic half-kilo sets).","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Dinengdeng\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"The Department of Agriculture''s \"May Gulay Project\" was launched to ensure a continuous and stable supply of vegetables at affordable prices (traditionally packed and retailed as pre-cut, hygienic half-kilo sets).\n\nThe program officially provides three specific sets of pre-packaged vegetable combinations tailored for classic Filipino dishes:\n1. Pinakbet\n2. Sinigang\n3. Chopsuey","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Pinakbet, Sinigang, Chopsuey"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:in this type of planning approach, the programs are dictated by the mandate, thrusts, and concerns of the sector where the program is lodged.:::sectoral planning', 'in this type of planning approach, the programs are dictated by the mandate, thrusts, and concerns of the sector where the program is lodged.', 'Sectoral planning', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Sectoral planning is an approach in which programs and priorities are determined primarily by the specific mandate and thrust of the government sector or agency implementing them (e.g., health, agriculture, or education) rather than by a shared, cross-sectoral nutrition goal.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Sectoral planning\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Sectoral planning is an approach in which programs and priorities are determined primarily by the specific mandate and thrust of the government sector or agency implementing them (e.g., health, agriculture, or education) rather than by a shared, cross-sectoral nutrition goal.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Nutrition-based development planning, Option C, Community nutrition planning"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:in this type of planning approach, the programs are dictated by the mandate, thrusts, and concerns of the sector where the program is lodged.:::', 'in this type of planning approach, the programs are dictated by the mandate, thrusts, and concerns of the sector where the program is lodged.', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Sectoral planning is an approach in which programs and priorities are determined primarily by the specific mandate and thrust of the government sector or agency implementing them (e.g., health, agriculture, or education) rather than by a shared, cross-sectoral nutrition goal.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Sectoral planning\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Sectoral planning is an approach in which programs and priorities are determined primarily by the specific mandate and thrust of the government sector or agency implementing them (e.g., health, agriculture, or education) rather than by a shared, cross-sectoral nutrition goal.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Nutrition-based development planning, Option C, Community nutrition planning"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:this is the human resource strategy of the philippine plan of action for nutrition.:::barangay nutrition scholar program', 'this is the human resource strategy of the philippine plan of action for nutrition.', 'Barangay Nutrition Scholar Program', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"The Barangay Nutrition Scholar (BNS) Program is the human resource development strategy of the PPAN, involving the recruitment, training, deployment, and supervision of volunteer community nutrition workers in every barangay, originally mandated under Presidential Decree No. 1569.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Barangay Nutrition Scholar Program\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"The Barangay Nutrition Scholar (BNS) Program is the human resource development strategy of the PPAN, involving the recruitment, training, deployment, and supervision of volunteer community nutrition workers in every barangay, originally mandated under Presidential Decree No. 1569.\n\nOperation Timbang Plus, Nutriskwela, and the Promote Good Nutrition Program are service-delivery or advocacy programs.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Nutriskwela Community Radio Network Program, Promote Good Nutrition Program, Operation Timbang Plus Program"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:this is the human resource strategy of the philippine plan of action for nutrition.:::', 'this is the human resource strategy of the philippine plan of action for nutrition.', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"The Barangay Nutrition Scholar (BNS) Program is the human resource development strategy of the PPAN, involving the recruitment, training, deployment, and supervision of volunteer community nutrition workers in every barangay, originally mandated under Presidential Decree No. 1569.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Barangay Nutrition Scholar Program\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"The Barangay Nutrition Scholar (BNS) Program is the human resource development strategy of the PPAN, involving the recruitment, training, deployment, and supervision of volunteer community nutrition workers in every barangay, originally mandated under Presidential Decree No. 1569.\n\nOperation Timbang Plus, Nutriskwela, and the Promote Good Nutrition Program are service-delivery or advocacy programs.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Nutriskwela Community Radio Network Program, Promote Good Nutrition Program, Operation Timbang Plus Program"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:which agency is not a member of the nnc governing board?:::dar', 'which agency is not a member of the nnc governing board?', 'DAR', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"According to the official National Nutrition Council (NNC) Guidelines, the Governing Board is the highest policy-making body on nutrition in the Philippines. It is composed of 10 national government agencies and three representatives from the private sector:","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"DAR\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"According to the official National Nutrition Council (NNC) Guidelines, the Governing Board is the highest policy-making body on nutrition in the Philippines. It is composed of 10 national government agencies and three representatives from the private sector:\n\n1. Department of Health (DOH) – Chairperson\n2. Department of Agriculture (DA) – Vice-Chairperson\n3. Department of the Interior and Local Government (DILG) – Vice-Chairperson\n4. Department of Budget and Management (DBM)\n5. Department of Education (DepEd)\n6. Department of Labor and Employment (DOLE)\n7. Department of Science and Technology (DOST)\n8. Department of Social Welfare and Development (DSWD)\n9. Department of Trade and Industry (DTI)\n10. National Economic and Development Authority (NEDA)","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: DOST, DOLE, DBM"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:which agency is not a member of the nnc governing board?:::', 'which agency is not a member of the nnc governing board?', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"According to the official National Nutrition Council (NNC) Guidelines, the Governing Board is the highest policy-making body on nutrition in the Philippines. It is composed of 10 national government agencies and three representatives from the private sector:","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"DAR\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"According to the official National Nutrition Council (NNC) Guidelines, the Governing Board is the highest policy-making body on nutrition in the Philippines. It is composed of 10 national government agencies and three representatives from the private sector:\n\n1. Department of Health (DOH) – Chairperson\n2. Department of Agriculture (DA) – Vice-Chairperson\n3. Department of the Interior and Local Government (DILG) – Vice-Chairperson\n4. Department of Budget and Management (DBM)\n5. Department of Education (DepEd)\n6. Department of Labor and Employment (DOLE)\n7. Department of Science and Technology (DOST)\n8. Department of Social Welfare and Development (DSWD)\n9. Department of Trade and Industry (DTI)\n10. National Economic and Development Authority (NEDA)","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: DOST, DOLE, DBM"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:who is the first director of the national nutrition council?:::dr. florentino solon', 'who is the first director of the national nutrition council?', 'Dr. Florentino Solon', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Dr. Florentino S. Solon, widely regarded as the \"Father of Nutrition\" in the Philippines, served as the first Executive Director of the National Nutrition Council beginning in 1974, and concurrently founded the Nutrition Center of the Philippines the same year (NNC, 2025).","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Dr. Florentino Solon\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Dr. Florentino S. Solon, widely regarded as the \"Father of Nutrition\" in the Philippines, served as the first Executive Director of the National Nutrition Council beginning in 1974, and concurrently founded the Nutrition Center of the Philippines the same year (NNC, 2025).","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Dr. Juan Salcedo, Jr., Dr. Coronado Pascual, Dr. Francisco Santos"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:who is the first director of the national nutrition council?:::', 'who is the first director of the national nutrition council?', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Dr. Florentino S. Solon, widely regarded as the \"Father of Nutrition\" in the Philippines, served as the first Executive Director of the National Nutrition Council beginning in 1974, and concurrently founded the Nutrition Center of the Philippines the same year (NNC, 2025).","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Dr. Florentino Solon\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Dr. Florentino S. Solon, widely regarded as the \"Father of Nutrition\" in the Philippines, served as the first Executive Director of the National Nutrition Council beginning in 1974, and concurrently founded the Nutrition Center of the Philippines the same year (NNC, 2025).","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Dr. Juan Salcedo, Jr., Dr. Coronado Pascual, Dr. Francisco Santos"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:the nutrient that is considered most difficult to meet during pregnancy::::iron', 'the nutrient that is considered most difficult to meet during pregnancy:', 'iron', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Iron requirements roughly double during pregnancy to support the expansion of maternal blood volume, fetal and placental growth, and stores for the newborn, and this increased demand is very difficult to meet through diet alone, which is why iron-folic acid supplementation is routinely recommended for pregnant women (WHO, 2001). ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"iron\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Iron requirements roughly double during pregnancy to support the expansion of maternal blood volume, fetal and placental growth, and stores for the newborn, and this increased demand is very difficult to meet through diet alone, which is why iron-folic acid supplementation is routinely recommended for pregnant women (WHO, 2001). \n\nAmong the macro- and micronutrients needed in pregnancy, iron is consistently identified as the nutrient hardest to obtain in adequate amounts from food sources alone.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: calcium, protein, vitamin D"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb)
