('mc:it is a statement of general thrust of the organization.:::mission', 'it is a statement of general thrust of the organization.', 'Mission', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"A mission statement articulates an organization''s general thrust or overarching purpose, why it exists and what it broadly seeks to accomplish, distinct from a vision (the aspirational future state it seeks to achieve), a goal (a broad long-term aim derived from the mission), and an objective (a specific, measurable, time-bound target that operationalizes a goal).","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Mission\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"A mission statement articulates an organization''s general thrust or overarching purpose, why it exists and what it broadly seeks to accomplish, distinct from a vision (the aspirational future state it seeks to achieve), a goal (a broad long-term aim derived from the mission), and an objective (a specific, measurable, time-bound target that operationalizes a goal).","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Vision, Objective, Goal"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:it is a statement of general thrust of the organization.:::', 'it is a statement of general thrust of the organization.', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"A mission statement articulates an organization''s general thrust or overarching purpose, why it exists and what it broadly seeks to accomplish, distinct from a vision (the aspirational future state it seeks to achieve), a goal (a broad long-term aim derived from the mission), and an objective (a specific, measurable, time-bound target that operationalizes a goal).","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Mission\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"A mission statement articulates an organization''s general thrust or overarching purpose, why it exists and what it broadly seeks to accomplish, distinct from a vision (the aspirational future state it seeks to achieve), a goal (a broad long-term aim derived from the mission), and an objective (a specific, measurable, time-bound target that operationalizes a goal).","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Vision, Objective, Goal"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:the national government agency that makes sure that nutrition concerns are integrated in both national and sub-national development plans.:::depdev', 'the national government agency that makes sure that nutrition concerns are integrated in both national and sub-national development plans.', 'DEPDev', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"The Department of Economy, Planning, and Development (DEPDev) created under Republic Act No. 12145 through the reorganization of the former National Economic and Development Authority (NEDA) serves as the primary planning agency responsible for issuing and integrating nutrition and other socioeconomic concerns into the Philippine Development Plan, Regional Development Plans, and related national and sub-national planning instruments (DEPDev, 2025).","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"DEPDev\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"The Department of Economy, Planning, and Development (DEPDev) created under Republic Act No. 12145 through the reorganization of the former National Economic and Development Authority (NEDA) serves as the primary planning agency responsible for issuing and integrating nutrition and other socioeconomic concerns into the Philippine Development Plan, Regional Development Plans, and related national and sub-national planning instruments (DEPDev, 2025).","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: DBM, DSWD, DILG"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:the national government agency that makes sure that nutrition concerns are integrated in both national and sub-national development plans.:::', 'the national government agency that makes sure that nutrition concerns are integrated in both national and sub-national development plans.', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"The Department of Economy, Planning, and Development (DEPDev) created under Republic Act No. 12145 through the reorganization of the former National Economic and Development Authority (NEDA) serves as the primary planning agency responsible for issuing and integrating nutrition and other socioeconomic concerns into the Philippine Development Plan, Regional Development Plans, and related national and sub-national planning instruments (DEPDev, 2025).","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"DEPDev\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"The Department of Economy, Planning, and Development (DEPDev) created under Republic Act No. 12145 through the reorganization of the former National Economic and Development Authority (NEDA) serves as the primary planning agency responsible for issuing and integrating nutrition and other socioeconomic concerns into the Philippine Development Plan, Regional Development Plans, and related national and sub-national planning instruments (DEPDev, 2025).","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: DBM, DSWD, DILG"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:a level of health care facilities which includes rural health units, chest clinics, and malaria eradication units.:::primary level', 'a level of health care facilities which includes rural health units, chest clinics, and malaria eradication units.', 'primary level', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Primary level health care facilities serve as the first point of contact between community members and the formal healthcare system. According to the Department of Health (DOH) structural framework, this level manages simple, routine, and specialized community-wide preventive and promotive health programs.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"primary level\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Primary level health care facilities serve as the first point of contact between community members and the formal healthcare system. According to the Department of Health (DOH) structural framework, this level manages simple, routine, and specialized community-wide preventive and promotive health programs.\n\nIt encompasses:\n• Rural Health Units (RHUs) and Barangay Health Stations (BHS)\n• Chest clinics (for tuberculosis management and screening)\n• Malaria eradication units and other specialized disease surveillance outposts\n• Private medical clinics and community health centers\n\n• Tertiary level: Consists of highly specialized national or regional medical centers and teaching hospitals equipped with advanced diagnostic and treatment facilities (e.g., specialized surgeries, intensive care units).\n• Secondary level: Consists of smaller, departmentalized hospitals (such as district, provincial, or municipal hospitals) capable of providing basic surgical, pediatric, obstetric, and medical treatments that require hospitalization but not highly specialized equipment.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: secondary level, tertiary level, none of the above"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:a level of health care facilities which includes rural health units, chest clinics, and malaria eradication units.:::', 'a level of health care facilities which includes rural health units, chest clinics, and malaria eradication units.', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Primary level health care facilities serve as the first point of contact between community members and the formal healthcare system. According to the Department of Health (DOH) structural framework, this level manages simple, routine, and specialized community-wide preventive and promotive health programs.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"primary level\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Primary level health care facilities serve as the first point of contact between community members and the formal healthcare system. According to the Department of Health (DOH) structural framework, this level manages simple, routine, and specialized community-wide preventive and promotive health programs.\n\nIt encompasses:\n• Rural Health Units (RHUs) and Barangay Health Stations (BHS)\n• Chest clinics (for tuberculosis management and screening)\n• Malaria eradication units and other specialized disease surveillance outposts\n• Private medical clinics and community health centers\n\n• Tertiary level: Consists of highly specialized national or regional medical centers and teaching hospitals equipped with advanced diagnostic and treatment facilities (e.g., specialized surgeries, intensive care units).\n• Secondary level: Consists of smaller, departmentalized hospitals (such as district, provincial, or municipal hospitals) capable of providing basic surgical, pediatric, obstetric, and medical treatments that require hospitalization but not highly specialized equipment.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: secondary level, tertiary level, none of the above"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:which agency leads the implementation of hapag (halina''t magtanim ng prutas at gulay)?:::', 'which agency leads the implementation of hapag (halina''t magtanim ng prutas at gulay)?', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"The HAPAG (Halina''t Magtanim ng Prutas at Gulay) sa Barangay Project is a community-based agriculture initiative spearheaded and implemented by the DILG pursuant to DILG Memorandum Circular No. 2023-001.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"DILG\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"The HAPAG (Halina''t Magtanim ng Prutas at Gulay) sa Barangay Project is a community-based agriculture initiative spearheaded and implemented by the DILG pursuant to DILG Memorandum Circular No. 2023-001.\n\nWhile it is heavily supported by the Department of Agriculture (DA) as a key technical partner supplying seeds, tools, and agricultural training, the DILG serves as the primary leading agency tasked with mandating and overseeing barangays nationwide in establishing their communal food gardens.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: DA, DAR, NNC"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:this measures how fast people are added to the population through births.:::crude birth rate', 'this measures how fast people are added to the population through births.', 'crude birth rate', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"The crude birth rate, computed as the number of live births per 1,000 population in a given year, measures the overall rate at which a population is being added to through births, without adjusting for age or sex structure. Fertility rate measures births relative to women of reproductive age, and crude birth rate the broader population-growth-through-births indicator being described.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"crude birth rate\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"The crude birth rate, computed as the number of live births per 1,000 population in a given year, measures the overall rate at which a population is being added to through births, without adjusting for age or sex structure. Fertility rate measures births relative to women of reproductive age, and crude birth rate the broader population-growth-through-births indicator being described.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: fertility rate, Option C, crude fertility rate"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:this measures how fast people are added to the population through births.:::', 'this measures how fast people are added to the population through births.', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"The crude birth rate, computed as the number of live births per 1,000 population in a given year, measures the overall rate at which a population is being added to through births, without adjusting for age or sex structure. Fertility rate measures births relative to women of reproductive age, and crude birth rate the broader population-growth-through-births indicator being described.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"crude birth rate\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"The crude birth rate, computed as the number of live births per 1,000 population in a given year, measures the overall rate at which a population is being added to through births, without adjusting for age or sex structure. Fertility rate measures births relative to women of reproductive age, and crude birth rate the broader population-growth-through-births indicator being described.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: fertility rate, Option C, crude fertility rate"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:what is the acceptable minimum diet diversity?:::5 out of 8 food groups', 'what is the acceptable minimum diet diversity?', '5 out of 8 food groups', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"According to the updated World Health Organization (WHO) and UNICEF guidelines (which are officially utilized by the Philippine Statistics Authority (PSA) and the Department of Science and Technology - Food and Nutrition Research Institute (DOST-FNRI) for reporting), Minimum Dietary Diversity (MDD) for infants and young children aged 6–23 months is defined as consuming items from at least 5 out of 8 defined food groups.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"5 out of 8 food groups\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"According to the updated World Health Organization (WHO) and UNICEF guidelines (which are officially utilized by the Philippine Statistics Authority (PSA) and the Department of Science and Technology - Food and Nutrition Research Institute (DOST-FNRI) for reporting), Minimum Dietary Diversity (MDD) for infants and young children aged 6–23 months is defined as consuming items from at least 5 out of 8 defined food groups.\n\nThe indicator was updated globally to include breast milk as its own distinct eighth group to eliminate measurement disparities between breastfed and non-breastfed children.\n\nThe 8 defined food groups are:\n1. Breast milk\n2. Grains, white/pale starchy roots, tubers, and plantains\n3. Legumes (pulses) and nuts\n4. Dairy products (milk, infant formula, yogurt, cheese)\n5. Flesh foods (meat, fish, poultry, and organ meats)\n6. Eggs\n7. Vitamin A-rich fruits and vegetables\n8. Other fruits and vegetables","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: 4 out of 8 food groups, 4 out of 7 food groups, 5 out of 7 food groups"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:what is the acceptable minimum diet diversity?:::', 'what is the acceptable minimum diet diversity?', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"According to the updated World Health Organization (WHO) and UNICEF guidelines (which are officially utilized by the Philippine Statistics Authority (PSA) and the Department of Science and Technology - Food and Nutrition Research Institute (DOST-FNRI) for reporting), Minimum Dietary Diversity (MDD) for infants and young children aged 6–23 months is defined as consuming items from at least 5 out of 8 defined food groups.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"5 out of 8 food groups\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"According to the updated World Health Organization (WHO) and UNICEF guidelines (which are officially utilized by the Philippine Statistics Authority (PSA) and the Department of Science and Technology - Food and Nutrition Research Institute (DOST-FNRI) for reporting), Minimum Dietary Diversity (MDD) for infants and young children aged 6–23 months is defined as consuming items from at least 5 out of 8 defined food groups.\n\nThe indicator was updated globally to include breast milk as its own distinct eighth group to eliminate measurement disparities between breastfed and non-breastfed children.\n\nThe 8 defined food groups are:\n1. Breast milk\n2. Grains, white/pale starchy roots, tubers, and plantains\n3. Legumes (pulses) and nuts\n4. Dairy products (milk, infant formula, yogurt, cheese)\n5. Flesh foods (meat, fish, poultry, and organ meats)\n6. Eggs\n7. Vitamin A-rich fruits and vegetables\n8. Other fruits and vegetables","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: 4 out of 8 food groups, 4 out of 7 food groups, 5 out of 7 food groups"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:which agency leads the implementation of hapag (halina''t magtanim ng prutas at gulay)?:::dilg', 'which agency leads the implementation of hapag (halina''t magtanim ng prutas at gulay)?', 'DILG', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"The HAPAG (Halina''t Magtanim ng Prutas at Gulay) sa Barangay Project is a community-based agriculture initiative spearheaded and implemented by the DILG pursuant to DILG Memorandum Circular No. 2023-001.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"DILG\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"The HAPAG (Halina''t Magtanim ng Prutas at Gulay) sa Barangay Project is a community-based agriculture initiative spearheaded and implemented by the DILG pursuant to DILG Memorandum Circular No. 2023-001.\n\nWhile it is heavily supported by the Department of Agriculture (DA) as a key technical partner supplying seeds, tools, and agricultural training, the DILG serves as the primary leading agency tasked with mandating and overseeing barangays nationwide in establishing their communal food gardens.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: DA, DAR, NNC"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:which of the following questions are not answered by monitoring?:::were the intervention strategies appropriate to the target population?', 'which of the following questions are not answered by monitoring?', 'Were the intervention strategies appropriate to the target population?', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Monitoring tracks what is happening (activities, inputs, participation numbers). It cannot tell you if the fundamental design or strategy of the intervention was inherently appropriate for that specific cultural or demographic group in the first place. Assessing whether a strategy is \"appropriate\" is a qualitative judgment that belongs strictly to formative evaluation or process evaluation.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Were the intervention strategies appropriate to the target population?\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Monitoring tracks what is happening (activities, inputs, participation numbers). It cannot tell you if the fundamental design or strategy of the intervention was inherently appropriate for that specific cultural or demographic group in the first place. Assessing whether a strategy is \"appropriate\" is a qualitative judgment that belongs strictly to formative evaluation or process evaluation.\n\n\t• Needs met: In basic operational monitoring (like supply-chain or emergency relief monitoring), managers constantly track target outputs to see if immediate operational needs (e.g., \"Did everyone get their ration?\") are being met.\n\t• Appropriate for the problem: Operational monitoring can flag immediate mismatches between a program''s activities and the problem on the ground (e.g., if a program provides food but the actual problem is a water shortage, monitoring will immediately show zero uptake).\n\t• Stakeholder participation: This is a textbook monitoring metric (tracking attendance and engagement levels).","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Were the needs met?, What is the level of participation of various stakeholders?, Was the program appropriate for the problem identified?"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:which of the following questions are not answered by monitoring?:::', 'which of the following questions are not answered by monitoring?', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Monitoring tracks what is happening (activities, inputs, participation numbers). It cannot tell you if the fundamental design or strategy of the intervention was inherently appropriate for that specific cultural or demographic group in the first place. Assessing whether a strategy is \"appropriate\" is a qualitative judgment that belongs strictly to formative evaluation or process evaluation.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Were the intervention strategies appropriate to the target population?\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Monitoring tracks what is happening (activities, inputs, participation numbers). It cannot tell you if the fundamental design or strategy of the intervention was inherently appropriate for that specific cultural or demographic group in the first place. Assessing whether a strategy is \"appropriate\" is a qualitative judgment that belongs strictly to formative evaluation or process evaluation.\n\n\t• Needs met: In basic operational monitoring (like supply-chain or emergency relief monitoring), managers constantly track target outputs to see if immediate operational needs (e.g., \"Did everyone get their ration?\") are being met.\n\t• Appropriate for the problem: Operational monitoring can flag immediate mismatches between a program''s activities and the problem on the ground (e.g., if a program provides food but the actual problem is a water shortage, monitoring will immediately show zero uptake).\n\t• Stakeholder participation: This is a textbook monitoring metric (tracking attendance and engagement levels).","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Were the needs met?, What is the level of participation of various stakeholders?, Was the program appropriate for the problem identified?"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:how many micronutrients are included in the micronutrient powder?:::15', 'how many micronutrients are included in the micronutrient powder?', '15', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"The multiple micronutrient powder (MNP) formulation used in the Philippines and recommended for home fortification of complementary foods for children 6–23 months contains 15 essential vitamins and minerals, including iron, zinc, vitamin A, and iodine, in a single daily sachet (Department of Health, n.d.).","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"15\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"The multiple micronutrient powder (MNP) formulation used in the Philippines and recommended for home fortification of complementary foods for children 6–23 months contains 15 essential vitamins and minerals, including iron, zinc, vitamin A, and iodine, in a single daily sachet (Department of Health, n.d.).","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: 8, 10, 12"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:how many micronutrients are included in the micronutrient powder?:::', 'how many micronutrients are included in the micronutrient powder?', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"The multiple micronutrient powder (MNP) formulation used in the Philippines and recommended for home fortification of complementary foods for children 6–23 months contains 15 essential vitamins and minerals, including iron, zinc, vitamin A, and iodine, in a single daily sachet (Department of Health, n.d.).","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"15\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"The multiple micronutrient powder (MNP) formulation used in the Philippines and recommended for home fortification of complementary foods for children 6–23 months contains 15 essential vitamins and minerals, including iron, zinc, vitamin A, and iodine, in a single daily sachet (Department of Health, n.d.).","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: 8, 10, 12"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:a study will be conducted to test the effects on the fat content of fried chicken using two different frying techniques. what is the appropriate research design to use?:::experimental research', 'a study will be conducted to test the effects on the fat content of fried chicken using two different frying techniques. what is the appropriate research design to use?', 'experimental research', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Because the researcher actively manipulates an independent variable (the frying technique) under controlled conditions to measure its effect on a dependent variable (fat content), this is a true experimental design. ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"experimental research\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Because the researcher actively manipulates an independent variable (the frying technique) under controlled conditions to measure its effect on a dependent variable (fat content), this is a true experimental design. \n\nCorrelational and observational designs, by contrast, examine naturally occurring relationships or exposures without researcher-controlled manipulation, and a descriptive survey merely characterizes existing conditions without testing a causal intervention.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: descriptive survey, correlational research, observational study"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:a study will be conducted to test the effects on the fat content of fried chicken using two different frying techniques. what is the appropriate research design to use?:::', 'a study will be conducted to test the effects on the fat content of fried chicken using two different frying techniques. what is the appropriate research design to use?', NULL, true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Because the researcher actively manipulates an independent variable (the frying technique) under controlled conditions to measure its effect on a dependent variable (fat content), this is a true experimental design. ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"experimental research\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Because the researcher actively manipulates an independent variable (the frying technique) under controlled conditions to measure its effect on a dependent variable (fat content), this is a true experimental design. \n\nCorrelational and observational designs, by contrast, examine naturally occurring relationships or exposures without researcher-controlled manipulation, and a descriptive survey merely characterizes existing conditions without testing a causal intervention.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: descriptive survey, correlational research, observational study"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
('mc:based on the latest nns results, what is the trend of wasting in adolescents?:::decreasing', 'based on the latest nns results, what is the trend of wasting in adolescents?', 'decreasing', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Decreasing trend for wasting: 2025: 9.6% 2023: 11.5% 2021: 10.9% 2018-2019: 11.5%","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"decreasing\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Decreasing trend for wasting: 2025: 9.6% 2023: 11.5% 2021: 10.9% 2018-2019: 11.5%","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: increasing, minimal change, no change"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
