('mc:sentence a. ice cream is agitated to form tiny crystals. sentence b. large crystals may be formed with slow freezing.:::both sentences are correct', 'sentence a. ice cream is agitated to form tiny crystals. sentence b. large crystals may be formed with slow freezing.', 'Both sentences are correct', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Agitation during ice-cream freezing helps distribute air and prevents the formation of excessively large crystals. ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Both sentences are correct\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Agitation during ice-cream freezing helps distribute air and prevents the formation of excessively large crystals. \n\nSlow freezing favors the growth of larger ice crystals and produces a coarser texture.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Sentence A is correct, Sentence B is correct, Both sentences are incorrect"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
