('mc:sentence a. fish contains trimethylamine oxide. sentence b. fish easily spoils more than red meat.:::both sentences are correct', 'sentence a. fish contains trimethylamine oxide. sentence b. fish easily spoils more than red meat.', 'Both sentences are correct', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Marine fish contain trimethylamine oxide (TMAO), which can be converted to trimethylamine during spoilage. ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Both sentences are correct\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Marine fish contain trimethylamine oxide (TMAO), which can be converted to trimethylamine during spoilage. \n\nFish generally spoils faster than red meat because of its high water activity, relatively mild postmortem acidity, and highly active spoilage enzymes and microorganisms.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Sentence A is correct, Sentence B is correct, Both sentences are incorrect"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
