('mc:sentence a. oven spring is the rapid rise of breads during baking. sentence b. oven spring is due to the action of gluten.:::sentence a is correct', 'sentence a. oven spring is the rapid rise of breads during baking. sentence b. oven spring is due to the action of gluten.', 'Sentence A is correct', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Sentence A is correct because oven spring is the rapid increase in bread volume during the early stage of baking. ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Sentence A is correct\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Sentence A is correct because oven spring is the rapid increase in bread volume during the early stage of baking. \n\nSentence B is incorrect because oven spring results mainly from expansion of gases and continued yeast activity before yeast is inactivated, while gluten provides structure that helps retain the expanding gases.\n\nOven Spring happens during baking, while gluten formation happens during kneading.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Sentence B is correct, Both sentences are correct, Both sentences are incorrect"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
