('mc:sentence a. margarine is a mixture of skim milk and vegetable fat. sentence b. margarine contains hydrogenated fat.:::both sentences are correct', 'sentence a. margarine is a mixture of skim milk and vegetable fat. sentence b. margarine contains hydrogenated fat.', 'Both sentences are correct', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Margarine – a butter substitute made from vegetable oils and may contain butter, salt, artificial coloring, emulsifiers, and preservatives; made by emulsifying fat other than milk fat with cultured milk; contains eighty percent (80%) fat and sixteen percent (16%) water; usually fortified","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Both sentences are correct\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Margarine – a butter substitute made from vegetable oils and may contain butter, salt, artificial coloring, emulsifiers, and preservatives; made by emulsifying fat other than milk fat with cultured milk; contains eighty percent (80%) fat and sixteen percent (16%) water; usually fortified\n\nMargarine is roughly 80% fat (from vegetable oils or animal fats) and about 17% to 18.5% liquid. Pasteurized skimmed milk, water, or soybean protein fluid makes up this liquid portion.\n\nTraditional margarines also commonly contain hydrogenated or otherwise modified vegetable fats to obtain suitable texture and plasticity.\n\n[Note: \"made by emulsifying fat other than milk fat with cultured milk\"  is a specific traditional or legal standard (resembling statutory definitions found in some food codes like the FDA/Codex Alimentarius for standard margarine blends), though today''s products can use various water-in-oil formulations without strictly requiring cultured milk.]","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Sentence A is correct, Sentence B is correct, Both sentences are incorrect"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
