('mc:sentence a. spices and herbs keep longer if stored whole. sentence b. herbs are crushed before measuring to bring out the full flavor:::sentence a is correct', 'sentence a. spices and herbs keep longer if stored whole. sentence b. herbs are crushed before measuring to bring out the full flavor', 'Sentence A is correct', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Whole spices retain volatile flavor compounds longer than ground spices. ","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Sentence A is correct\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Whole spices retain volatile flavor compounds longer than ground spices. \n\nCrushing or grinding herbs or spices releases aromatic compounds, so they are often crushed right before adding them to a hot dish to activate the flavors or release trapped essential oils.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Sentence B is correct, Both sentences are correct, Both sentences are incorrect"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
