('mc:apan-apan is traditionally prepared using::::kangkong', 'apan-apan is traditionally prepared using:', 'Kangkong', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Apan-apan is a popular Ilonggo vegetable dish from Western Visayas, Philippines. It is a flavorful, savory, and tangy variation of adobong kangkong made with water spinach (kangkong), sautéed garlic, onions, vinegar, soy sauce, and fermented shrimp paste (guinamos or bagoong alamang), often topped with crispy fried pork (tulapho).<img alt=\"Apan-Apan Recipe\" src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" width=\"289\">","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Kangkong\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Apan-apan is a popular Ilonggo vegetable dish from Western Visayas, Philippines. It is a flavorful, savory, and tangy variation of adobong kangkong made with water spinach (kangkong), sautéed garlic, onions, vinegar, soy sauce, and fermented shrimp paste (guinamos or bagoong alamang), often topped with crispy fried pork (tulapho).<img alt=\"Apan-Apan Recipe\" src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" width=\"289\">","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Eggplant, Fish, Malunggay"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
