ur local laing variant. It is made from fresh young gabi leaves,  coconut cream, grated salted fish meat, lemon grass and chilies. 📸 Ana  Katherine Reyes\" src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" width=\"200\">c. Tinuto: coconut-based dish from Quezon province and Marinduque, similar to Bicolano laing<img alt=\"Nilaneg - Ang Sarap\" src=\"data:image/jpeg;base64,\" width=\"202\">d. Nilanega: Filipino soup dish from Batanes and the Cagayan Valley region, made with broiled fresh fish and pork liver simmered in a savory bagoong broth along with local vegetables","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Pipian, Tinuto, Nilaneg"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
