('mc:the shortage of potatoes due to the war between russia and ukraine has an impact on the production of this known alcoholic beverage.:::vodka', 'the shortage of potatoes due to the war between russia and ukraine has an impact on the production of this known alcoholic beverage.', 'Vodka', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"Vodka –  While vodka can be distilled from various grains (like wheat or rye), potatoes are historically and traditionally one of its primary, iconic raw base ingredients.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Vodka\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"Vodka –  While vodka can be distilled from various grains (like wheat or rye), potatoes are historically and traditionally one of its primary, iconic raw base ingredients.\n\n• Gin: Typically distilled from a grain mash (like wheat or barley) and flavored heavily with juniper berries.\n• Rum: Distilled exclusively from sugarcane byproducts, such as molasses or sugarcane juice.\n• Brandy: Produced by distilling wine or fermented fruit mashes (most commonly grapes).\n\n• Beer – Made from barley and hops.\n• Wine – Made from grapes.\n• Sake – Made from rice.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Brandy, Gin, Rum"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
