('mc:a picture shows four pieces of institutional kitchen equipment. which equipment would be most appropriate for large-volume soup production?:::steam-jacketed kettle', 'a picture shows four pieces of institutional kitchen equipment. which equipment would be most appropriate for large-volume soup production?', 'Steam-jacketed kettle', true, '{"sources":[{"url":"","title":"Krause and Mahan''s Food & the Nutrition Care Process"},{"url":"","title":"NDLE Board Licensure Reference Manual"}],"whyRight":"• Salamander: primarily used for broiling or finishing foods.","modelUsed":"Gemini 2.5 Flash","isAiPowered":true,"keyDifference":"Key differentiator: \"Steam-jacketed kettle\" aligns strictly with standard dietetics criteria.","searchOverview":"Official NDLE Board Licensure Reference & Evidence Breakdown","authorRationale":"• Salamander: primarily used for broiling or finishing foods.\n• Bain-marie: suited to gentle heating or holding rather than primary large-volume soup production.\n• Griddle: designed for direct cooking on a heated flat surface.","whyWrongChoices":"Alternative options: Bain-marie, Griddle, Salamander"}'::jsonb, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, '"2026-11-04T11:21:38.282Z"'::jsonb),
